window.EXAMS = [{"id": "exam_practice_exam_practice_exams_aws_certifi", "name": "Đề 1", "source": "Practice Exam _ Practice Exams _ AWS Certified Generative AI Developer Professional - AIP-C01 _ Cloud Exam Pro.html", "questions": [{"number": 1, "status": "Incorrect", "question": "A healthcare company is developing an application to process medical queries. The application must answer complex queries with high accuracy by reducing semantic dilution. The application must refer to domain-specific terminology in medical documents to reduce ambiguity in medical terminology. The application must be able to respond to 1,000 queries each minute with response times less than 2 seconds.\nWhich solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Create an Amazon Bedrock agent to orchestrate multiple AWS Lambda functions to decompose queries. Create an Amazon Bedrock knowledge base to store the reference medical documents. Use the agent's built-in knowledge base capabilities. Add deep research and reasoning capabilities to the agent to reduce ambiguity in the medical terminology.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Use Amazon SageMaker Al to host custom ML models for both query decomposition and query expansion. Configure Amazon Bedrock knowledge bases to store the reference medical documents. Encrypt the documents in the knowledge base.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Configure an Amazon Bedrock knowledge base to store the reference medical documents. Enable query decomposition in the knowledge base. Configure an Amazon Bedrock flow that uses a foundation model (FM) and the knowledge base to support the application.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Use Amazon API Gateway to route incoming queries to an Amazon Bedrock agent. Configure the agent to use an Anthropic Claude model to decompose queries and an Amazon Titan model to expand queries. Create an Amazon Bedrock knowledge base to store the reference medical documents.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["C"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nTruy vấn\nphức tạp, độ chính xác cao (complex queries, high accuracy)\nGiảm pha loãng ngữ nghĩa (reduce semantic dilution)\n+ thuật ngữ chuyên ngành y tế\n1000 queries/phút, <2s,\nít vận hành nhất (LEAST operational overhead)\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nConfigure an Amazon Bedrock knowledge base to store the reference medical documents. Enable query decomposition in the knowledge base. Configure an Amazon Bedrock flow that uses a foundation model (FM) and the knowledge base to support the application.\nQuery decomposition là tính năng built-in\ncủa Bedrock Knowledge Bases, chuyên giải quyết \"complex queries\" và \"semantic dilution\" bằng cách tách câu hỏi phức tạp thành sub-queries.\nBedrock Flows\nđiều phối low-code → ít vận hành nhất.\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Use Amazon API Gateway to route incoming queries to an Amazon Bedrock agent. Configure the agent to use an Anthropic Claude model to decompose queries and an Amazon Titan model to expand queries. Create an Amazon Bedrock knowledge base to store the reference medical documents.\n→ Sai. Tự dựng agent + 2 model riêng để decompose/expand → nhiều vận hành hơn hẳn so với dùng tính năng có sẵn.\n❌ Use Amazon SageMaker Al to host custom ML models for both query decomposition and query expansion. Configure Amazon Bedrock knowledge bases to store the reference medical documents. Encrypt the documents in the knowledge base.\n→ Sai. Self-host custom ML model = vận hành cực cao, loại ngay khi gặp \"LEAST overhead\".\n❌ Create an Amazon Bedrock agent to orchestrate multiple AWS Lambda functions to decompose queries. Create an Amazon Bedrock knowledge base to store the reference medical documents. Use the agent's built-in knowledge base capabilities. Add deep research and reasoning capabilities to the agent to reduce ambiguity in the medical terminology.\n→ Sai. Agent + nhiều Lambda để decompose = thừa, \"deep research\" mơ hồ, overhead cao.\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\ncomplex queries + semantic dilution → Query Decomposition (built-in KB feature)\nLEAST overhead + orchestration → Bedrock Flows\n(không tự code agent/Lambda)"}, {"number": 2, "status": "Incorrect", "question": "A GenAI developer is evaluating Amazon Bedrock foundation models (FMs) to enhance a Europe-based company's internal business application. The company has a multi-account landing zone in AWS Control Tower. The company uses SCPs to allow its accounts to use only the eu-north-1 Region and the eu-west-1 Region. All customer data must remain in private networks within the approved AWS Regions.\nThe GenAI developer selects an FM based on analysis and testing and hosts the model in the eu-central-1 Region and the eu-west-3 Region. The GenAI developer must enable access to the FM for the company’s employees. The GenAI developer must ensure that requests to the FM are private and remain with the same Regions as the FM.\nWhich solution will meet these requirements?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Deploy the FM on Amazon EC2 instances in eu-north-1. Deploy a private Amazon API Gateway REST API in front of the EC2 instances. Configure an Amazon Bedrock VPC endpoint. Integrate the REST API with the business application.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Deploy the FM in Amazon SageMaker AI in eu-north-1. Configure a SageMaker AI VPC endpoint. Extend existing SCPs to allow employees to use the SageMaker AI endpoint. Integrate the FM in SageMaker AI with the business application.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Deploy an AWS Lambda function that is exposed by a private Amazon API Gateway REST API to a VPC in eu-north-1. Create a VPC endpoint for the selected FM in eu-central-1 and eu-west-3. Extend existing SCPs to allow employees to use the FM. Integrate the REST API with the business application.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Configure the FM to use cross-Region inference through an eu.amazon.* endpoint to ensure that all calls remain within Europe. Configure an Amazon Bedrock VPC endpoint. Extend existing SCPs to allow employees to use the FM through inference profiles in Europe-based Regions where the FM is available. Use an inference profile to integrate Amazon Bedrock with the business application.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["C"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nCông ty ở châu Âu đang đánh giá các Foundation Model (FM) trên Amazon Bedrock cho ứng dụng nội bộ.\nCông ty sử dụng môi trường multi-account với AWS Control Tower.\nSCP chỉ cho phép sử dụng 2 Region:\neu-north-1\neu-west-1\nToàn bộ dữ liệu khách hàng phải:\nKhông đi qua Internet công cộng.\nLuôn nằm trong các AWS Region đã được phê duyệt.\nGenAI Developer chọn một FM trên Bedrock.\nModel này được host tại:\neu-central-1\neu-west-3\nYêu cầu:\nCho phép nhân viên truy cập Foundation Model.\nRequest tới FM phải đi qua mạng riêng (private network).\nDữ liệu không được ra Internet.\nDữ liệu phải ở cùng Region với nơi model được host (eu-central-1 hoặc eu-west-3).\nVẫn phải tuân thủ các giới hạn Region của tổ chức.\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nDeploy an AWS Lambda function that is exposed by a private Amazon API Gateway REST API to a VPC in eu-north-1. Create a VPC endpoint for the selected FM in eu-central-1 and eu-west-3. Extend existing SCPs to allow employees to use the FM. Integrate the REST API with the business application.\nPrivate API Gateway + VPC endpoint\nđảm bảo traffic\nprivate\n(PrivateLink).\nVPC endpoint đặt\nđúng tại eu-central-1/eu-west-3\n= request ở lại đúng Region của FM.\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Deploy the FM on Amazon EC2 instances in eu-north-1. Deploy a private Amazon API Gateway REST API in front of the EC2 instances. Configure an Amazon Bedrock VPC endpoint. Integrate the REST API with the business application.\n→ Sai. Bedrock FM\nkhông deploy lên EC2\n→ sai bản chất.\n❌ Configure the FM to use cross-Region inference through an eu.amazon.* endpoint to ensure that all calls remain within Europe. Configure an Amazon Bedrock VPC endpoint. Extend existing SCPs to allow employees to use the FM through inference profiles in Europe-based Regions where the FM is available. Use an inference profile to integrate Amazon Bedrock with the business application.\n→ Sai.\nCross-Region inference\nsẽ route sang Region khác → vi phạm \"remain with the SAME Regions as the FM\" (chỉ \"within Europe\" là chưa đủ chặt).\n❌ Deploy the FM in Amazon SageMaker AI in eu-north-1. Configure a SageMaker AI VPC endpoint. Extend existing SCPs to allow employees to use the SageMaker AI endpoint. Integrate the FM in SageMaker AI with the business application.\n→ Sai. Đây là Bedrock FM, không phải SageMaker model → sai dịch vụ.\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nprivate access tới Bedrock → VPC endpoint (PrivateLink)\n\"remain within SAME Region as FM\" → KHÔNG dùng cross-Region inference"}, {"number": 3, "status": "Correct", "question": "A large ecommerce company has deployed a foundation model (FM) to generate product descriptions. The company's engineering team monitors technical metrics such as token usage, latency, and error rates by using Amazon CloudWatch. The company's marketing team tracks business metrics such as conversion rates and revenue impact in its own systems.\nThe company needs a unified observability solution that correlates technical performance with business outcomes. The solution must provide automatic alerts to stakeholders when operational metrics indicate degradation. The solution must provide comprehensive visibility across both technical and business metrics.\nWhich solution will meet these requirements?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Create CloudWatch dashboards that include technical metrics and imported business metrics. Configure CloudWatch composite alarms that combine technical data and business data. Use Amazon SNS to set up notifications to stakeholders.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Use Amazon Managed Grafana to visualize technical metrics from CloudWatch with business metrics from external sources. Configure Amazon Managed Grafana alerts to invoke AWS Lambda functions. Configure the Lambda functions to remediate issues automatically when metrics exceed predefined thresholds.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Stream CloudWatch metrics to Amazon S3 by using CloudWatch metric streams. Create Amazon QuickSight dashboards to visualize the combined technical metrics and business metrics. Set up Amazon EventBridge rules to send notifications to stakeholders when metrics exceed predefined thresholds.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Configure CloudWatch custom dashboards that integrate operational metrics with imported business metrics. Set up CloudWatch composite alarms with anomaly detection. Use Amazon SNS to create alarm actions to notify stakeholders when correlated metrics indicate performance issues.", "is_correct": true}], "correct_answers": ["D"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nGiải pháp quan sát thống nhất (unified observability solution)\ncho ecommerce dùng FM\nChỉ số kỹ thuật (technical metrics)\n: token usage, latency, error rates → đang trên\nCloudWatch\nChỉ số kinh doanh (business metrics)\n: conversion rates, revenue → trên\nhệ thống riêng\nYêu cầu:\ntự động cảnh báo (automatic alerts)\n,\ntương quan (correlate)\ncả 2 loại metrics\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nConfigure CloudWatch custom dashboards that integrate operational metrics with imported business metrics. Set up CloudWatch composite alarms with anomaly detection. Use Amazon SNS to create alarm actions to notify stakeholders when correlated metrics indicate performance issues.\nComposite alarms\ncho phép kết hợp nhiều alarm (cả technical lẫn business metrics) thành 1 alarm duy nhất → đáp ứng yêu cầu \"correlate\"\nAnomaly detection\ntự động phát hiện degradation mà không cần đặt ngưỡng thủ công\nSNS\nxử lý notification đến stakeholders đúng yêu cầu\nToàn bộ nằm trong CloudWatch ecosystem → ít operational overhead nhất\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Create CloudWatch dashboards that include technical metrics and imported business metrics. Configure CloudWatch composite alarms that combine technical data and business data. Use Amazon SNS to set up notifications to stakeholders.\n→ Sai. Gần đúng nhưng\nthiếu anomaly detection\n→ phải set threshold thủ công, kém linh hoạt\n❌ Use Amazon Managed Grafana to visualize technical metrics from CloudWatch with business metrics from external sources. Configure Amazon Managed Grafana alerts to invoke AWS Lambda functions. Configure the Lambda functions to remediate issues automatically when metrics exceed predefined thresholds.\n→ Sai.\nAuto-remediate\nkhông được yêu cầu, chỉ cần alert. Grafana phức tạp hơn cần thiết, operational overhead cao hơn\n❌ Stream CloudWatch metrics to Amazon S3 by using CloudWatch metric streams. Create Amazon QuickSight dashboards to visualize the combined technical metrics and business metrics. Set up Amazon EventBridge rules to send notifications to stakeholders when metrics exceed predefined thresholds.\n→ Sai. Pipeline quá phức tạp (CloudWatch → S3 → QuickSight). EventBridge không phải công cụ tối ưu cho alarm notifications so với SNS\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nCorrelate technical + business metrics\n→ CloudWatch\nComposite Alarms\nAutomatic alerts on degradation\n→ CloudWatch\nAnomaly Detection\nNotify stakeholders\n→\nAmazon SNS\n(không phải EventBridge)\nUnified observability\n→ ưu tiên giải pháp\nall-in-CloudWatch\nthay vì multi-service pipeline"}, {"number": 4, "status": "Correct", "question": "A medical device company wants to feed reports of medical procedures that used the company's devices into an AI assistant. To protect patient privacy, the AI assistant must expose patient personally identifiable information (PII) only to surgeons. The AI assistant must redact PII for engineers. The AI assistant must reference only medical reports that are less than 3 years old.\nThe company stores reports in an Amazon S3 bucket as soon as each report is published. The company has already set up an Amazon Bedrock knowledge base. The AI assistant uses Amazon Cognito to authenticate users.\nWhich solution will meet these requirements?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Set up an S3 Lifecycle configuration on the bucket to remove reports that are older than 3 years. Schedule an AWS Lambda function to run daily syncs between the bucket and the knowledge base. When users interact with the AI assistant, call the ApplyGuardrail configuration that matches the user's Cognito user group to redact PII from the agent’s responses if appropriate.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Enable Amazon Macie PII detection on the S3 bucket. Use an S3 trigger to invoke an AWS Lambda function that redacts PII from the reports. Configure the Lambda function to delete outdated documents from the bucket and to invoke knowledge base syncing.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Invoke an AWS Lambda function to sync the S3 bucket and the knowledge base when a new report is uploaded to the bucket. Use a second Lambda function to invoke Amazon Comprehend to detect and redact PII if a user is part of the engineer Cognito user group. Set up an S3 Lifecycle configuration to remove reports that are older than 3 years from the bucket.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Create a second knowledge base. Set up an S3 Lifecycle configuration on the bucket to remove reports that are older than 3 years. Invoke an AWS Lambda function that syncs the bucket with the original knowledge base when a new report is uploaded to the bucket. Use Amazon Comprehend to detect and redact PII before syncing the bucket with the second knowledge base. When a user interacts with the AI assistant, redirect the model to the appropriate knowledge base depending on the user’s Cognito user group.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["C"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nAI assistant cho\nthiết bị y tế (medical device)\n, dùng\nAmazon Bedrock Knowledge Base\n+\nAmazon Cognito\nPII\n: surgeons được xem, engineers phải\nbị redact\nChỉ dùng\nbáo cáo dưới 3 năm (reports less than 3 years old)\nReports lưu trong\nS3\n, upload liên tục khi publish\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nInvoke an AWS Lambda function to sync the S3 bucket and the knowledge base when a new report is uploaded to the bucket. Use a second Lambda function to invoke Amazon Comprehend to detect and redact PII if a user is part of the engineer Cognito user group. Set up an S3 Lifecycle configuration to remove reports that are older than 3 years from the bucket.\nLambda trigger on S3 upload\n→ sync knowledge base\nreal-time\nngay khi report mới được tạo\nAmazon Comprehend\ndetect & redact PII → phân biệt theo\nCognito user group\n(engineer vs surgeon)\nS3 Lifecycle\ntự động xóa reports > 3 năm → đảm bảo knowledge base chỉ chứa dữ liệu hợp lệ\nKiến trúc event-driven, đơn giản, đúng yêu cầu\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Enable Amazon Macie PII detection on the S3 bucket. Use an S3 trigger to invoke an AWS Lambda function that redacts PII from the reports. Configure the Lambda function to delete outdated documents from the bucket and to invoke knowledge base syncing.\nAmazon Macie\nthiên về\nphát hiện/báo cáo\nPII, không phải redact theo user role\nKhông có cơ chế phân biệt surgeon vs engineer khi serving\n❌ Set up an S3 Lifecycle configuration on the bucket to remove reports that are older than 3 years. Schedule an AWS Lambda function to run daily syncs between the bucket and the knowledge base. When users interact with the AI assistant, call the ApplyGuardrail configuration that matches the user's Cognito user group to redact PII from the agent’s responses if appropriate.\nDaily sync\n→ không real-time, có thể miss reports mới tạo\nApplyGuardrail dùng để filter output của FM, không phải redact PII theo user role đúng cách\n❌ Create a second knowledge base. Set up an S3 Lifecycle configuration on the bucket to remove reports that are older than 3 years. Invoke an AWS Lambda function that syncs the bucket with the original knowledge base when a new report is uploaded to the bucket. Use Amazon Comprehend to detect and redact PII before syncing the bucket with the second knowledge base. When a user interacts with the AI assistant, redirect the model to the appropriate knowledge base depending on the user’s Cognito user group.\n2 knowledge bases\n→ phức tạp, tốn kém, operational overhead cao\nKhông phân biệt được surgeon vs engineer một cách dynamic\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nRedact PII theo role (role-based PII redaction)\n→\nAmazon Comprehend\n+\nCognito user group\nXóa data cũ tự động (auto-expire old data)\n→\nS3 Lifecycle policy\nSync ngay khi upload (real-time sync)\n→\nS3 trigger → Lambda\n(không phải scheduled)\nMacie\n→ phát hiện/báo cáo PII, KHÔNG phải redact"}, {"number": 5, "status": "Correct", "question": "A financial services company wants to use Amazon Bedrock foundation models (FMs) to analyze call center recordings. When calls end, the call center stores recordings as MP3 files in an Amazon S3 bucket. The company needs to generate summaries and sentiment analysis for the recordings in a structured format as soon as new files are created. The recordings average 20 MB in size.\nWhich combination of solutions will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Use AWS Step Functions to orchestrate a workflow to process the recordings. Configure steps to invoke Amazon Transcribe to convert audio to text, validate job completion, and to invoke an AWS Lambda function to process the text by using Amazon Bedrock FMs to generate structured analysis output.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Use AWS Step Functions to orchestrate a workflow to process the recordings. Configure steps to invoke Amazon Transcribe to convert audio to text, validate job completion, and to directly invoke Amazon Bedrock FMs to generate summaries and sentiment analysis in JSON format.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Configure the source S3 bucket to send notifications to the Step Functions workflow when an object is created in the bucket.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Use AWS Step Functions to orchestrate a workflow to process the recordings. Configure steps to invoke Amazon Transcribe to convert audio to text, validate job completion, and to invoke an AWS Lambda function to create a prompt to invoke Amazon Bedrock FMs to generate structured analysis output.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "E", "text": "Configure the source S3 bucket to send events to Amazon EventBridge. Create an EventBridge rule to invoke the Step Functions workflow when an object is created in the bucket.", "is_correct": true}], "correct_answers": ["B", "E"], "explanation": "A.\nUse AWS Step Functions to orchestrate a workflow to process the recordings. Configure steps to invoke Amazon Transcribe to convert audio to text, validate job completion, and to invoke an AWS Lambda function to process the text by using Amazon Bedrock FMs to generate structured analysis output."}, {"number": 6, "status": "Correct", "question": "A university recently digitized a collection of archival documents, academic journals, and manuscripts. The university stores the digital files in an AWS Lake Formation data lake.\nThe university hires a GenAI developer to build a solution to allow users to search the digital files by using text queries. The solution must return journal abstracts that are semantically similar to a user's query. Users must be able to search the digitized collection based on text and metadata that is associated with the journal abstracts. The metadata of the digitized files does not contain keywords. The solution must match similar abstracts to one another based on the similarity of their text. The data lake contains fewer than 1 million files.\nWhich solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Use Amazon Titan Embeddings in Amazon Bedrock to create vector representations of the digitized files. Store embeddings in the OpenSearch Neural Plugin for Amazon OpenSearch Service.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Use Amazon Comprehend to extract topics from the digitized files. Store the topics and file metadata in an Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL database. Query the abstract metadata against the data in the Aurora database.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Use Amazon SageMaker AI to deploy a sentence-transformer model. Use the model to create vector representations of the digitized files. Store embeddings in an Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL database that has the pgvector extension.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Use Amazon Titan Embeddings in Amazon Bedrock to create vector representations of the digitized files. Store embeddings in an Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL Serverless database that has the pgvector extension.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["A"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nUniversity số hóa tài liệu, lưu trên\nAWS Lake Formation\nCần\nsemantic search\n(tìm kiếm theo nghĩa, không phải keyword)\nSearch dựa trên\ntext AND metadata\ncủa journal abstracts\nMetadata không chứa keywords\n; dữ liệu < 1 triệu files\nYêu cầu:\nLEAST operational overhead\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nUse Amazon Titan Embeddings in Amazon Bedrock to create vector representations of the digitized files. Store embeddings in the OpenSearch Neural Plugin for Amazon OpenSearch Service.\nAmazon Titan Embeddings\nlà managed embedding model → không cần deploy, maintain model\nOpenSearch Neural Plugin\nhỗ trợ\nk-NN vector search\nnative → semantic search out-of-the-box\nToàn bộ managed services →\nLEAST operational overhead\nHỗ trợ search cả text lẫn metadata embeddings\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Use Amazon Comprehend to extract topics from the digitized files. Store the topics and file metadata in an Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL database. Query the abstract metadata against the data in the Aurora database.\nComprehend topic extraction\n≠ semantic similarity search\nAurora PostgreSQL không có native vector search → không phù hợp cho semantic search\n❌ Use Amazon SageMaker AI to deploy a sentence-transformer model. Use the model to create vector representations of the digitized files. Store embeddings in an Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL database that has the pgvector extension.\nSageMaker deploy & maintain model →\nhigh operational overhead\nMặc dù pgvector hỗ trợ vector search, nhưng vẫn phức tạp hơn OpenSearch Neural Plugin\n❌ Use Amazon Titan Embeddings in Amazon Bedrock to create vector representations of the digitized files. Store embeddings in an Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL Serverless database that has the pgvector extension.\npgvector trên Aurora Serverless phức tạp hơn, và\nAurora Serverless\ncó cold start latency\nOpenSearch với Neural Plugin được thiết kế tối ưu hơn cho vector search ở scale < 1M files\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nSemantic search + LEAST overhead\n→\nAmazon Titan Embeddings + OpenSearch Neural Plugin\nMetadata không có keywords\n→ phải dùng\nvector/semantic search\n(không phải keyword search)\nSageMaker deploy model\n→ HIGH operational overhead\nOpenSearch Neural Plugin\n= giải pháp vector search managed, ít overhead nhất"}, {"number": 7, "status": "Correct", "question": "A company is using Amazon Bedrock to develop a customer support AI assistant. The AI assistant must respond to customer questions about their accounts. The AI assistant must not expose personal information in responses. The company must comply with data residency policies by ensuring that all processing occurs within the same AWS Region where each customer is located.\nThe company wants to evaluate how effective the AI assistant is at preventing the exposure of personal information before the company makes the AI assistant available to customers.\nWhich solution will meet these requirements?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Configure a cross-Region Amazon Bedrock guardrail to apply a set of content and word filters. Set the guardrail to detect mode during development and testing. Switch to mask mode for production deployment.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Configure an Amazon Bedrock guardrail to apply content and topic filters. Set the guardrail to detect mode during development, testing, and production. Disable invocation logging for the Amazon Bedrock model.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Configure an Amazon Bedrock guardrail to apply sensitive information filters. Set the guardrail to mask mode during development and testing. Switch to block mode for production deployment. Deploy a copy of the guardrail to each Region where the company operates.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Configure a cross-Region Amazon Bedrock guardrail to apply sensitive information filters. Set the guardrail to detect mode during development and testing. Switch to block mode for production deployment.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["C"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nAI assistant dùng\nAmazon Bedrock\n, không được expose\nthông tin cá nhân (personal information)\nPhải tuân thủ\ndata residency\n→ xử lý trong\ncùng AWS Region\nvới customer\nCần\nevaluate\n(đánh giá) trước khi deploy → tức đang trong giai đoạn\ntesting\nYêu cầu: ngăn personal information trong responses\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nConfigure an Amazon Bedrock guardrail to apply sensitive information filters. Set the guardrail to mask mode during development and testing. Switch to block mode for production deployment. Deploy a copy of the guardrail to each Region where the company operates.\nSensitive information filters\nđúng loại filter cần dùng (personal info = PII)\nMask mode\nkhi testing → cho phép evaluate hiệu quả của guardrail mà không block hoàn toàn\nBlock mode\nproduction → bảo vệ tối đa\nDeploy per Region\n→ đáp ứng\ndata residency\nrequirement (processing within same Region)\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Configure a cross-Region Amazon Bedrock guardrail to apply sensitive information filters. Set the guardrail to detect mode during development and testing. Switch to block mode for production deployment.\nCross-Region guardrail\nvi phạm\ndata residency\nrequirement (data phải xử lý trong cùng Region)\n❌ Configure an Amazon Bedrock guardrail to apply content and topic filters. Set the guardrail to detect mode during development, testing, and production. Disable invocation logging for the Amazon Bedrock model.\nContent/topic filters\n≠ sensitive information/PII filters\nDùng\ndetect mode\ntrong production → không block được personal information\n❌ Configure a cross-Region Amazon Bedrock guardrail to apply a set of content and word filters. Set the guardrail to detect mode during development and testing. Switch to mask mode for production deployment.\nCross-Region\nvi phạm data residency\nContent/word filters\nkhông phải loại phù hợp cho personal information\nMask\nthay vì\nblock\nở production → kém an toàn hơn\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nPersonal information / PII\n→ Bedrock Guardrails\nSensitive Information Filters\nEvaluate trước khi deploy\n→\nMask mode\n(detect & mask nhưng không block để test)\nData residency + same Region\n→\nKHÔNG dùng cross-Region guardrail\n; deploy\nper Region\nBlock mode\n= production |\nMask mode\n= testing |\nDetect mode\n= monitoring only"}, {"number": 8, "status": "Incorrect", "question": "A software as a service (SaaS) company is building a recommendation model that uses Amazon SageMaker AI to support an application that recommends airline cabin upgrades to customers. The company will host SageMaker AI models on Amazon Bedrock by using Amazon Bedrock Custom Model Import. Airline companies will use the application to send customized offers to customers.\nThe model must examine the travel history of customers to help make more relevant recommendations. The company stores customer travel history data in an Amazon RDS database. The company must ensure that the application delivers consistent, relevant, and accurate results across multiple airlines and customer populations.\nWhich solution will meet these requirements?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Implement text-to-SQL transformations with SQL validations to accurately retrieve relevant booking patterns, preferences, and loyalty information from the RDS database. Use the results to generate personalized cabin upgrade recommendations. Apply Amazon Bedrock guardrails to filter responses. Use confidence scoring and semantic similarity searches to reduce hallucinations.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Use Amazon OpenSearch Service to implement vector searches of customer travel history embeddings. Use the vector searches to give the application the ability to perform similarity-based retrieval of booking patterns, preferences, and loyalty information to generate personalized cabin upgrade recommendations. Apply Amazon Bedrock guardrails to filter responses. Use confidence scoring and semantic similarity searches to reduce hallucinations.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Implement text-to-SQL transformations with SQL validations to accurately retrieve relevant booking patterns, preferences, and loyalty information from the RDS database. Use the results to generate personalized cabin upgrade recommendations. Apply Amazon Bedrock guardrails to filter content. Use AWS Step Functions and AWS Lambda functions to orchestrate validation workflows to reduce hallucinations.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Use Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases to implement a RAG architecture to analyze customer travel history data to give the application semantic search capabilities. Use the semantic search capabilities to retrieve relevant booking patterns, preferences, and loyalty information to generate personalized cabin upgrade recommendations. Apply Amazon Bedrock guardrails to filter content. Use AWS Step Functions and AWS Lambda functions to orchestrate validation workflows to reduce hallucinations.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["C"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nModel được train bằng\nAmazon SageMaker AI\nDeploy trên\nAmazon Bedrock bằng Custom Model Import\nDữ liệu khách hàng nằm trong\nAmazon RDS\nMục tiêu:\nPhân tích lịch sử du lịch\nĐưa ra recommendation chính xác\nKết quả phải\nconsistent, relevant, accurate\nHoạt động trên nhiều airline\nĐiểm quan trọng nhất:\nNguồn dữ liệu là Amazon RDS (structured relational database).\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nImplement text-to-SQL transformations with SQL validations to accurately retrieve relevant booking patterns, preferences, and loyalty information from the RDS database. Use the results to generate personalized cabin upgrade recommendations. Apply Amazon Bedrock guardrails to filter content. Use AWS Step Functions and AWS Lambda functions to orchestrate validation workflows to reduce hallucinations.\nText-to-SQL\n→ truy vấn trực tiếp\nstructured data\ntừ RDS → chính xác và nhất quán\nSQL validation\ngiúp đảm bảo truy vấn chính xác trước khi thực thi.\nAWS Step Functions + Lambda\ntạo workflow kiểm tra, retry và xác thực, giúp giảm hallucination và tăng tính nhất quán.\nData trong RDS là\nstructured\n→ text-to-SQL phù hợp hơn RAG/vector search\nBedrock Guardrails\nlọc nội dung đầu ra.\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Use Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases to implement a RAG architecture to analyze customer travel history data to give the application semantic search capabilities. Use the semantic search capabilities to retrieve relevant booking patterns, preferences, and loyalty information to generate personalized cabin upgrade recommendations. Apply Amazon Bedrock guardrails to filter content. Use AWS Step Functions and AWS Lambda functions to orchestrate validation workflows to reduce hallucinations.\nRAG\nphù hợp cho\nunstructured data\n; data trong RDS là\nstructured\n→ text-to-SQL hiệu quả hơn\nKnowledge Base không kết nối trực tiếp RDS database\n❌ Use Amazon OpenSearch Service to implement vector searches of customer travel history embeddings. Use the vector searches to give the application the ability to perform similarity-based retrieval of booking patterns, preferences, and loyalty information to generate personalized cabin upgrade recommendations. Apply Amazon Bedrock guardrails to filter responses. Use confidence scoring and semantic similarity searches to reduce hallucinations.\nVector search phù hợp cho unstructured/semantic search\nTravel history data trong RDS là structured → không cần vector embedding\n❌ Implement text-to-SQL transformations with SQL validations to accurately retrieve relevant booking patterns, preferences, and loyalty information from the RDS database. Use the results to generate personalized cabin upgrade recommendations. Apply Amazon Bedrock guardrails to filter responses. Use confidence scoring and semantic similarity searches to reduce hallucinations.\nThiếu\nStep Functions/Lambda validation workflow\n\"Confidence scoring + semantic similarity\" không phù hợp cho SQL-based validation\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nStructured data trong RDS/SQL database\n→\nText-to-SQL\n(không phải RAG/vector search)\nReduce hallucination\ntừ SQL queries →\nSQL validation + Step Functions workflow\nRAG/Vector search\n→ dành cho\nunstructured data\n(documents, PDFs, text)\nConsistent & accurate results\ntừ structured DB → Text-to-SQL + validation"}, {"number": 9, "status": "Correct", "question": "A company is developing a customer communication platform that uses an AI assistant powered by an Amazon Bedrock foundation model (FM). The AI assistant summarizes customer messages and generates initial response drafts.\nThe company wants to use Amazon Comprehend to implement layered content filtering. The layered content filtering must prevent sharing of offensive content, protect customer privacy, and detect potential inappropriate advice solicitation. Inappropriate advice solicitation includes requests for unethical practices, harmful activities, or manipulative behaviors. The solution must maintain acceptable overall response times, so all pre-processing filters must finish before the content reaches the FM.\nWhich solution will meet these requirements?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Use custom classification to build an FM that detects offensive content and inappropriate advice solicitation. Apply personally identifiable information (PII) detection as a secondary filter only when messages pass the custom classifier.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Use toxicity detection with thresholds configured to 0.5 for all categories. Use parallel processing for both prompt safety classification and personally identifiable information (PII) detection with entity redaction. Apply Amazon CloudWatch alarms to filter metrics.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Use parallel processing with asynchronous API calls. Use toxicity detection for offensive content. Use prompt safety classification for inappropriate advice solicitation. Use personally identifiable information (PII) detection without redaction.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Deploy a multi-stage process. Configure the process to use prompt safety classification first, then toxicity detection on safe prompts only, and finally personally identifiable information (PII) detection in streaming mode. Route flagged messages through Amazon EventBridge for human review.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["B"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nCustomer communication platform\ndùng Amazon Bedrock FM\nCần\nlayered content filtering\nbằng\nAmazon Comprehend\n:\nNgăn\noffensive content\nBảo vệ\ncustomer privacy (PII)\nPhát hiện\ninappropriate advice solicitation\nTất cả pre-processing filters phải hoàn thành TRƯỚC khi đến FM\nYêu cầu: maintain\nacceptable response times\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nUse toxicity detection with thresholds configured to 0.5 for all categories. Use parallel processing for both prompt safety classification and personally identifiable information (PII) detection with entity redaction. Apply Amazon CloudWatch alarms to filter metrics.\nParallel processing\n→ tất cả filters chạy đồng thời →\ngiảm latency\n, maintain response times\nToxicity detection\n→ offensive content\nPII detection with entity redaction\n→ bảo vệ privacy\nPrompt safety classification\n→ inappropriate advice solicitation\nTất cả hoàn thành trước FM → đúng yêu cầu\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Use parallel processing with asynchronous API calls. Use toxicity detection for offensive content. Use prompt safety classification for inappropriate advice solicitation. Use personally identifiable information (PII) detection without redaction.\nAsynchronous\n= không đảm bảo hoàn thành trước FM\nPII detection WITHOUT redaction\n→ không bảo vệ privacy\n❌ Use custom classification to build an FM that detects offensive content and inappropriate advice solicitation. Apply personally identifiable information (PII) detection as a secondary filter only when messages pass the custom classifier.\nBuilding custom FM → high complexity\nPII detection chỉ khi pass classifier → có thể bỏ sót PII\n❌ Deploy a multi-stage process. Configure the process to use prompt safety classification first, then toxicity detection on safe prompts only, and finally personally identifiable information (PII) detection in streaming mode. Route flagged messages through Amazon EventBridge for human review.\nSequential (tuần tự)\n→ latency cao, vi phạm \"acceptable response times\"\nStreaming mode\ncho PII không phù hợp\nHuman review không được đề cập trong requirements\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nLayered filtering + acceptable response times\n→\nParallel processing\n(tất cả filters đồng thời)\nOffensive content\n→\nToxicity detection\nPrivacy / PII\n→\nPII detection with entity redaction\nInappropriate advice solicitation\n→\nPrompt safety classification\nAsynchronous\n→ KHÔNG đảm bảo hoàn thành trước FM → sai yêu cầu"}, {"number": 10, "status": "Incorrect", "question": "A company runs a Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) application that uses Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases to perform regulatory compliance queries. The application uses the RetrieveAndGenerateStream API. The application retrieves relevant documents from a knowledge base that contains more than 50,000 regulatory documents, legal precedents, and policy updates.\nThe RAG application is producing suboptimal responses because the initial retrieval often returns semantically similar but contextually irrelevant documents. The poor responses are causing model hallucinations and incorrect regulatory guidance. The company needs to improve the performance of the RAG application so it returns more relevant documents.\nWhich solution will meet this requirement with the LEAST operational overhead?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Deploy an Amazon SageMaker endpoint to run a fine-tuned ranking model. Use an Amazon API Gateway REST API to route requests. Configure the application to make requests through the REST API to rerank the results.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Use the latest Amazon reranker model through the reranking configuration within Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases. Use the model to improve document relevance scoring and to reorder results based on contextual assessments.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Implement a retrieval pipeline that uses the Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases Retrieve API to perform initial document retrieval. Call the Amazon Bedrock Rerank API to rerank the results. Invoke the InvokeModelWithResponseStream operation to generate responses.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Use Amazon Comprehend to classify documents and apply relevance scores. Integrate the RAG application’s reranking process with Amazon Textract to run document analysis. Use Amazon Neptune to perform graph-based relevance calculations.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["B"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nRAG application\ndùng\nAmazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases\n+\nRetrieveAndGenerateStream API\nKnowledge base:\n50,000+ regulatory documents\nVấn đề\n: retrieval trả về documents\nsemantically similar nhưng contextually irrelevant\n→ hallucination\nCần cải thiện\ndocument relevance\nvới\nLEAST operational overhead\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nUse the latest Amazon reranker model through the reranking configuration within Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases. Use the model to improve document relevance scoring and to reorder results based on contextual assessments.\nReranking trong Bedrock Knowledge Bases\nlà native feature →\nLEAST operational overhead\nReranker đánh giá lại documents dựa trên\ncontextual relevance\n(không chỉ semantic similarity)\nGiải quyết đúng vấn đề: \"semantically similar nhưng contextually irrelevant\"\nKhông cần infrastructure mới, không cần modify pipeline\nVí dụ về: Semantically similar but contextually irrelevant\n-> Hai câu\ncó ý nghĩa/từ ngữ khá giống nhau\n, nhưng\nkhông liên quan đến ngữ cảnh mà mình đang tìm\n,\nkhông giúp giải quyết vấn đề hiện tại.\nQuery\n ↓\n\"Reset Gmail password\"\n ↓\nSemantic similarity\n ↓\n\"Use a strong Gmail password\"\n ↓\nCó vẻ liên quan về mặt từ khóa/ý nghĩa\n ↓\nNhưng không trả lời câu hỏi \"reset password\"\n ↓\n❌ Contextually irrelevant\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Deploy an Amazon SageMaker endpoint to run a fine-tuned ranking model. Use an Amazon API Gateway REST API to route requests. Configure the application to make requests through the REST API to rerank the results.\nSageMaker endpoint + API Gateway →\nHIGH operational overhead\nInfrastructure phức tạp không cần thiết\n❌ Use Amazon Comprehend to classify documents and apply relevance scores. Integrate the RAG application’s reranking process with Amazon Textract to run document analysis. Use Amazon Neptune to perform graph-based relevance calculations.\nComprehend/Textract/Neptune = overkill, không phải giải pháp reranking chuẩn\nVery high operational overhead\n❌ Implement a retrieval pipeline that uses the Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases Retrieve API to perform initial document retrieval. Call the Amazon Bedrock Rerank API to rerank the results. Invoke the InvokeModelWithResponseStream operation to generate responses.\nGần đúng nhưng approach\nmanual/custom pipeline\nphức tạp\nThay đổi từ\nRetrieveAndGenerateStream\nsang Retrieve API riêng → thêm complexity\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nSemantically similar nhưng contextually irrelevant\n→ cần\nReranking\n(không phải thay embedding model)\nLEAST operational overhead + Bedrock KB\n→\nNative reranking configuration\ntrong Bedrock KB\nReranker\n= second-pass model đánh giá lại top-k results theo context thực sự\nSageMaker endpoint → HIGH overhead | Bedrock native feature → LOW overhead"}, {"number": 11, "status": "Correct", "question": "A company uses AWS Lake Formation to set up a data lake that contains databases and tables for multiple business units across multiple AWS Regions. The company wants to use a foundation model (FM) through Amazon Bedrock to perform fraud detection. The FM must ingest sensitive financial data from the data lake. The data includes some customer personally identifiable information (PM).\nThe company must design an access control solution that prevents PII from appearing in a production environment. The FM must access only authorized data subsets that have PHI redacted from specific data columns. The company must capture audit trails for all data access.\nWhich solution will meet these requirements?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Configure the FM to authenticate by using IAM roles and Lake Formation permissions based on LF-Tag expressions. Define business units and Regions as LF-Tags that are assigned to databases and tables. Use AWS CloudTrail to collect comprehensive audit trails of data access.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Configure the FM to request temporary credentials from AWS STS. Access the data by using presigned S3 URLs that are generated by an API that applies business unit and Regional filters. Use AWS CloudTrail to collect comprehensive audit trails of data access.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Create a separate dataset in a separate Amazon S3 bucket for each business unit and Region combination. Configure S3 bucket policies to control access based on IAM roles that are assigned to FM training instances. Use S3 access logs to track data access.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Use direct IAM principal grants on specific databases and tables in Lake Formation. Create a custom application layer that logs access requests and further filters sensitive columns before sending data to the FM.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["A"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nAWS Lake Formation\ndata lake, multiple business units, multiple Regions\nFM dùng để\nfraud detection\n, cần ingest\nsensitive financial data\ncó\nPII\nYêu cầu:\nngăn PII xuất hiện\ntrong production,\nredact PII từ specific columns\nFM chỉ access\nauthorized data subsets\nAudit trails\ncho tất cả data access\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nConfigure the FM to authenticate by using IAM roles and Lake Formation permissions based on LF-Tag expressions. Define business units and Regions as LF-Tags that are assigned to databases and tables. Use AWS CloudTrail to collect comprehensive audit trails of data access.\nLF-Tags (Lake Formation Tags)\ncho phép access control granular theo business unit và Region\nIAM roles + Lake Formation permissions\n= cơ chế native để control access trong data lake\nLake Formation có\ncolumn-level security\n→ redact PII từ specific columns\nCloudTrail\n= standard solution cho audit trails\nToàn bộ native Lake Formation features → đúng context của đề bài\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Create a separate dataset in a separate Amazon S3 bucket for each business unit and Region combination. Configure S3 bucket policies to control access based on IAM roles that are assigned to FM training instances. Use S3 access logs to track data access.\nKhông tận dụng Lake Formation (đề bài đã dùng Lake Formation)\nS3 access logs\nkém comprehensive hơn CloudTrail cho audit\nKhông có column-level PII redaction\n❌ Use direct IAM principal grants on specific databases and tables in Lake Formation. Create a custom application layer that logs access requests and further filters sensitive columns before sending data to the FM.\nCustom application layer\n→ high operational overhead\nDirect IAM grants không linh hoạt bằng LF-Tags cho multi-business-unit setup\n❌ Configure the FM to request temporary credentials from AWS STS. Access the data by using presigned S3 URLs that are generated by an API that applies business unit and Regional filters. Use AWS CloudTrail to collect comprehensive audit trails of data access.\nPresigned S3 URLs\nkhông phù hợp cho Lake Formation data lake access control\nKhông có column-level PII redaction\nSTS temporary credentials không cung cấp Lake Formation row/column level security\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nLake Formation + column-level PII redaction\n→\nLF-Tags + Lake Formation permissions\nMultiple business units + Regions access control\n→\nLF-Tag expressions\nAudit trails trong AWS\n→\nAWS CloudTrail\n(không phải S3 access logs)\nRedact specific columns\n→ Lake Formation\ncolumn-level security\n(không phải custom app layer)"}, {"number": 12, "status": "Correct", "question": "A financial services company is deploying a generative AI (GenAI) application that uses Amazon Bedrock to assist customer service representatives to provide personalized investment advice to customers. The company must implement a comprehensive governance solution that follows responsible AI practices and meets regulatory requirements.\nThe solution must detect and prevent hallucinations in recommendations. The solution must have safety controls for customer interactions. The solution must also monitor model behavior drift in real time and maintain audit trails of all prompt-response pairs for regulatory review.\nThe company must deploy the solution within 60 days. The solution must integrate with the company's existing compliance dashboard and respond to customers within 200 ms.\nWhich solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Configure Amazon Bedrock guardrails to apply custom content filters and toxicity detection. Use Amazon Bedrock Model Evaluation to detect hallucinations. Store prompt-response pairs in Amazon DynamoDB to capture audit trails and set a TTL. Integrate Amazon CloudWatch custom metrics with the existing compliance dashboard.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Use Amazon SageMaker Model Monitor to detect model behavior drift. Use AWS WAF to filter content. Store customer interactions in an encrypted Amazon RDS database. Use Amazon API Gateway to create custom HTTP APIs to integrate with the compliance dashboard.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Deploy Amazon Bedrock and use AWS PrivateLink to access the application securely. Use AWS Lambda functions to implement custom prompt validation. Store prompt-response pairs in an Amazon S3 bucket and configure S3 Lifecycle policies. Create custom Amazon CloudWatch dashboards to monitor model performance metrics.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Use Amazon Bedrock Agents and Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases to ground responses. Use Amazon Bedrock Guardrails to enforce content safety. Use Amazon OpenSearch Service to store and index prompt-responses pairs. Integrate OpenSearch Service with Amazon QuickSight to create compliance reports and to detect model behavior drift.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["A"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nGenAI app\ndùng Amazon Bedrock,\nfinancial services\n,\npersonalized investment advice\nYêu cầu comprehensive governance:\nDetect & prevent\nhallucinations\nSafety controls\ncho customer interactions\nMonitor\nmodel behavior drift\nreal-time\nAudit trails\ncủa prompt-response pairs\nDeploy trong\n60 days\n, tích hợp\ncompliance dashboard\n, latency\n< 200ms\nLEAST operational overhead\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nConfigure Amazon Bedrock guardrails to apply custom content filters and toxicity detection. Use Amazon Bedrock Model Evaluation to detect hallucinations. Store prompt-response pairs in Amazon DynamoDB to capture audit trails and set a TTL. Integrate Amazon CloudWatch custom metrics with the existing compliance dashboard.\nBedrock Guardrails\n→ safety controls, content filtering (native feature, low overhead)\nBedrock Model Evaluation\n→ detect hallucinations (native Bedrock feature)\nDynamoDB\n→ fast write, TTL tự động expire data, low latency < 200ms\nCloudWatch custom metrics\n→ tích hợp với compliance dashboard, monitor drift real-time\nTất cả native Bedrock/AWS services →\nLEAST operational overhead\n, deploy nhanh trong 60 days\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Deploy Amazon Bedrock and use AWS PrivateLink to access the application securely. Use AWS Lambda functions to implement custom prompt validation. Store prompt-response pairs in an Amazon S3 bucket and configure S3 Lifecycle policies. Create custom Amazon CloudWatch dashboards to monitor model performance metrics.\nPrivateLink không liên quan đến hallucination detection hay drift monitoring\nCustom Lambda validation → high operational overhead\nS3 không tối ưu cho audit trail queries (latency cao hơn DynamoDB)\n❌ Use Amazon Bedrock Agents and Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases to ground responses. Use Amazon Bedrock Guardrails to enforce content safety. Use Amazon OpenSearch Service to store and index prompt-responses pairs. Integrate OpenSearch Service with Amazon QuickSight to create compliance reports and to detect model behavior drift.\nOpenSearch để store audit trail = overkill\nQuickSight không phải tool cho real-time drift detection\nKhông có explicit hallucination detection mechanism\n❌ Use Amazon SageMaker Model Monitor to detect model behavior drift. Use AWS WAF to filter content. Store customer interactions in an encrypted Amazon RDS database. Use Amazon API Gateway to create custom HTTP APIs to integrate with the compliance dashboard.\nSageMaker Model Monitor\n→ cho SageMaker models, không phải Bedrock FM → không phù hợp\nWAF không phải tool cho AI content safety\nRDS + API Gateway → phức tạp, latency cao hơn DynamoDB\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nHallucination detection trong Bedrock\n→\nAmazon Bedrock Model Evaluation\nSafety controls + content filtering\n→\nAmazon Bedrock Guardrails\nAudit trails với low latency\n→\nDynamoDB + TTL\n(không phải S3 hay RDS)\nModel behavior drift monitoring\n→\nCloudWatch custom metrics\n(cho Bedrock; SageMaker Model Monitor dành cho SageMaker)\nLEAST overhead + 60 days\n→ ưu tiên\nnative Bedrock features"}, {"number": 13, "status": "Correct", "question": "A company is developing a generative AI (GenAI) application by using Amazon Bedrock. The application will analyze patterns and relationships in the company's data. The application will process millions of new data points daily across AWS Regions in Europe, North America, and Asia before storing the data in Amazon S3.\nThe application must comply with local data protection and storage regulations. Data residency and processing must occur within the same continent. The application must also maintain audit trails of the application's decision-making processes and provide data classification capabilities.\nWhich solution will meet these requirements?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Create separate AWS accounts for each Region with individual compliance frameworks. Use Amazon SageMaker AI with custom monitoring to track model performance and compliance with data residency requirements. Create manual reports for each regulatory jurisdiction.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Use Amazon S3 Object Lock with Region-specific S3 bucket policies. Pre-process the data points within the Region based on geographic origin before sending the data points to Amazon Bedrock. Use Amazon Macie to classify the data. Use AWS CloudTrail immutable logs to audit the decision-making processes.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Use SCPs with AWS Organizations to manage location-specific permissions. Use AWS CloudTrail immutable logs to audit the decision-making processes. Import a custom model into Amazon Bedrock and deploy the model to each Region.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Deploy the application in each Region with local IAM policies. Use Amazon Bedrock cross-Region inference to distribute the workload. Use Amazon CloudWatch to log AI decision-making processes and data processing activities. Manually track compliance certifications across Regions.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["B"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nGenAI app\ndùng Amazon Bedrock, process\nmillions of data points daily\nacross\nEurope, North America, Asia\nData stored in\nAmazon S3\nYêu cầu:\nData residency\n: processing trong\ncùng continent\nAudit trails\ncủa decision-making processes\nData classification\ncapabilities\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nUse Amazon S3 Object Lock with Region-specific S3 bucket policies. Pre-process the data points within the Region based on geographic origin before sending to Amazon Bedrock. Use Amazon Macie to classify the data. Use AWS CloudTrail immutable logs to audit the decision-making processes.\nS3 Object Lock\n+\nRegion-specific bucket policies\n→ enforce data stays trong Region/continent\nPre-process within Region\ntrước khi gửi Bedrock → đảm bảo\ndata residency\ncompliance\nAmazon Macie\n= AWS native service cho\ndata classification\n(đặc biệt sensitive data)\nCloudTrail immutable logs\n→ audit trail không thể bị tamper, phù hợp regulatory compliance\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Deploy the application in each Region with local IAM policies. Use Amazon Bedrock cross-Region inference to distribute the workload. Use Amazon CloudWatch to log AI decision-making processes and data processing activities. Manually track compliance certifications across Regions.\nCross-Region inference\ncó thể vi phạm data residency (data có thể chuyển sang Region khác)\nManual tracking\n→ không scalable, không phải automated solution\n❌ Use SCPs with AWS Organizations to manage location-specific permissions. Use AWS CloudTrail immutable logs to audit the decision-making processes. Import a custom model into Amazon Bedrock and deploy the model to each Region.\nSCPs tốt cho permission control nhưng\nkhông enforce data residency ở continent level\n\"Import custom model\" không liên quan đến yêu cầu\nKhông có data classification mechanism\n❌ Create separate AWS accounts for each Region with individual compliance frameworks. Use Amazon SageMaker AI with custom monitoring to track model performance and compliance with data residency requirements. Create manual reports for each regulatory jurisdiction.\nSeparate accounts = overkill và phức tạp\nSageMaker\nkhông phải Bedrock (đề bài yêu cầu Bedrock)\nManual reports\nkhông scalable\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nData residency + continent-level\n→\nRegion-specific S3 bucket policies + pre-process within Region\nData classification\n→\nAmazon Macie\n(đặc biệt cho sensitive/PII data)\nImmutable audit trails\n→\nCloudTrail immutable logs\nCross-Region inference\n→ CÓ THỂ vi phạm data residency → cẩn thận!\nS3 Object Lock\n→ WORM storage, phù hợp compliance/regulatory requirements"}, {"number": 14, "status": "Correct", "question": "A specialty coffee company has a mobile app that generates personalized coffee roast profiles by using Amazon Bedrock with a three-stage prompt chain. The prompt chain converts user inputs into structured metadata, retrieves relevant logs for coffee roasts, and generates a personalized roast recommendation for each customer.\nUsers in multiple AWS Regions report inconsistent roast recommendations for identical inputs, slow inference during the retrieval step, and unsafe recommendations such as brewing at excessively high temperatures. The company must improve the stability of outputs for repeated inputs. The company must also improve app performance and the safety of the app's outputs. The updated solution must ensure 99.5% output consistency for identical inputs and achieve inference latency of less than 1 second. The solution must also block unsafe or hallucinated recommendations by using validated safety controls.\nWhich solution will meet these requirements?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Deploy Amazon Bedrock with provisioned throughput to stabilize inference latency. Apply Amazon Bedrock guardrails that have semantic denial rules to block unsafe outputs. Use Amazon Bedrock Prompt Management to manage prompts by using approval workflows.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Use Amazon Kendra to improve roast log retrieval accuracy. Store normalized prompt metadata within Amazon DynamoDB. Use AWS Step Functions to orchestrate multistep prompts.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Use Amazon Bedrock Agents to manage chaining. Log model inputs and outputs to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Use logs from Amazon CloudWatch to perform A/B testing for prompt versions.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Cache prompt results in Amazon ElastiCache. Use AWS Lambda functions to pre-process metadata and to trace end-to-end latency. Use AWS X-Ray to identify and remediate performance bottlenecks.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["A"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nCoffee app\ndùng\n3-stage prompt chain\ntrên Amazon Bedrock\nVấn đề:\ninconsistent outputs\ncho identical inputs,\nslow inference\nở retrieval step,\nunsafe recommendations\nYêu cầu:\n99.5% output consistency\ncho identical inputs\nInference latency < 1 second\nBlock unsafe/hallucinated recommendations\nbằng safety controls\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nDeploy Amazon Bedrock with provisioned throughput to stabilize inference latency. Apply Amazon Bedrock guardrails that have semantic denial rules to block unsafe outputs. Use Amazon Bedrock Prompt Management to manage prompts by using approval workflows.\nProvisioned throughput\n→ đảm bảo consistent performance, giảm latency < 1 second\nSemantic denial rules\ntrong Bedrock Guardrails → block unsafe/hallucinated recommendations theo nghĩa (không chỉ keyword)\nPrompt Management + approval workflows\n→ quản lý prompt versions, đảm bảo\n99.5% consistency\ncho identical inputs (approved prompts → same output)\nToàn bộ native Bedrock features\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Use Amazon Bedrock Agents to manage chaining. Log model inputs and outputs to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Use logs from Amazon CloudWatch to perform A/B testing for prompt versions.\nA/B testing\n→ inconsistency (mục tiêu là TĂNG consistency)\nKhông giải quyết latency và safety requirements\n❌ Cache prompt results in Amazon ElastiCache. Use AWS Lambda functions to pre-process metadata and to trace end-to-end latency. Use AWS X-Ray to identify and remediate performance bottlenecks.\nElastiCache caching không giải quyết được\nconsistency\ncủa new/unique inputs\nX-Ray chỉ để trace, không fix latency\nKhông có safety controls\n❌ Use Amazon Kendra to improve roast log retrieval accuracy. Store normalized prompt metadata within Amazon DynamoDB. Use AWS Step Functions to orchestrate multistep prompts.\nKendra = enterprise search, không phải solution cho prompt consistency\nStep Functions không giải quyết safety/latency requirements\nKhông có safety controls\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nConsistent output + stable latency\n→\nProvisioned Throughput\n(không phải on-demand)\nBlock unsafe/hallucinated outputs\n→\nBedrock Guardrails\nvới\nsemantic denial rules\nPrompt consistency + version control\n→\nAmazon Bedrock Prompt Management\n+ approval workflows\nA/B testing prompts\n→ TẠO RA inconsistency → sai mục tiêu\nProvisioned Throughput\nvs\nOn-demand\n: Provisioned = guaranteed capacity, consistent performance"}, {"number": 15, "status": "Correct", "question": "A retail company is using Amazon Bedrock to develop a customer service AI assistant. Analysis shows that 70% of customer inquiries are simple product questions that a smaller model can effectively handle. However, 30% of inquiries are complex return policy questions that require advanced reasoning. The company wants to implement a cost-effective model selection framework to automatically route customer inquiries to appropriate models based on inquiry complexity. The framework must maintain high customer satisfaction and minimize response latency.\nWhich solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST implementation effort?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Create a multi-stage architecture that uses a small foundation model (FM) to classify the complexity of each inquiry. Route simple inquiries to a smaller, more cost-effective model. Route complex inquiries to a larger, more capable model. Use AWS Lambda functions to handle the routing logic.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Use Amazon Bedrock intelligent prompt routing to automatically analyze inquiries. Route simple product inquiries to smaller models, and route complex return policy inquiries to more capable larger models.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Implement a single-model solution that uses an Amazon Bedrock mid-sized foundation model (FM) with on-demand pricing. Include special instructions in model prompts to handle both simple and complex inquiries by using the same model.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Create separate Amazon Bedrock endpoints for simple and complex inquiries. Implement a rule-based routing system based on keyword detection. Use on-demand pricing for the smaller model and provisioned throughput for the larger model.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["B"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nCustomer service AI assistant\ndùng Amazon Bedrock\n70% simple questions\n→ smaller model đủ dùng\n30% complex questions\n(return policy) → cần advanced reasoning model\nCần\nauto-route\ninquiries đến model phù hợp\nYêu cầu:\nhigh satisfaction\n,\nminimize latency\n,\nLEAST implementation effort\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nUse Amazon Bedrock intelligent prompt routing to automatically analyze inquiries. Route simple product inquiries to smaller models, and route complex return policy inquiries to more capable larger models.\nIntelligent prompt routing\nlà native Bedrock feature →\nLEAST implementation effort\nTự động phân tích độ phức tạp và route đến model phù hợp\nKhông cần code custom routing logic, không cần maintain multiple endpoints\nTối ưu cost (small model cho simple queries) và latency\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Create a multi-stage architecture that uses a small foundation model (FM) to classify the complexity of each inquiry. Route simple inquiries to a smaller, more cost-effective model. Route complex inquiries to a larger, more capable model. Use AWS Lambda functions to handle the routing logic.\nPhải build thêm classification stage + Lambda routing logic →\nMORE implementation effort\nThêm latency từ classification step\n❌ Implement a single-model solution that uses an Amazon Bedrock mid-sized foundation model (FM) with on-demand pricing. Include special instructions in model prompts to handle both simple and complex inquiries by using the same model.\nKhông phải cost-effective (không route đến smaller model cho simple queries)\nKhông \"automatically route\" theo yêu cầu\nPrompt instructions không đảm bảo routing consistency\n❌ Create separate Amazon Bedrock endpoints for simple and complex inquiries. Implement a rule-based routing system based on keyword detection. Use on-demand pricing for the smaller model and provisioned throughput for the larger model.\nRule-based keyword detection\n→ brittle, không handle edge cases tốt\nMaintain 2 endpoints riêng biệt → more operational overhead\nKeyword matching kém thông minh hơn intelligent routing\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nAuto-route queries đến different models + LEAST effort\n→\nAmazon Bedrock Intelligent Prompt Routing\n70/30 simple/complex routing\n→ Bedrock Intelligent Prompt Routing (built-in, không cần code)\nKeyword-based routing\n→ fragile, NOT recommended cho complex NLP tasks\nMulti-stage classification\n→ EXTRA latency + effort → không phải LEAST effort\nKhi thấy \"LEAST implementation effort\" + Bedrock + routing → nghĩ ngay đến\nnative Bedrock features"}, {"number": 16, "status": "Correct", "question": "A company is designing an API for a generative AI (GenAI) application that uses a foundation model (FM) that is hosted on a managed model service. The API must stream responses to reduce latency, enforce token limits to manage compute resource usage, and implement retry logic to handle model timeouts and partial responses.\nWhich solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Integrate an Amazon API Gateway REST API with an AWS Lambda function that invokes Amazon Bedrock. Use Lambda response streaming to stream responses. Enforce token limits within the Lambda function. Implement retry logic by using Lambda and API Gateway timeout configurations.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Connect an Amazon API Gateway HTTP API directly to Amazon Bedrock. Simulate streaming by using client-side polling. Enforce token limits on the frontend. Configure retry behavior by using API Gateway integration settings.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Connect an Amazon API Gateway WebSocket API to an Amazon ECS service that hosts a containerized inference server. Stream responses by using the WebSocket protocol. Enforce token limits within Amazon ECS. Handle model timeouts by using ECS task lifecycle hooks and restart policies.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Integrate an Amazon API Gateway HTTP API with an AWS Lambda function to invoke Amazon Bedrock. Use Lambda response streaming to stream responses. Enforce token limits within the Lambda function. Implement retry logic for model timeouts by using Lambda and API Gateway timeout configurations.", "is_correct": true}], "correct_answers": ["D"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nGenAI API\ndùng\nfoundation model (FM)\ntrên managed model service\nYêu cầu:\nStream responses\nđể giảm latency\nEnforce token limits\nđể quản lý compute\nRetry logic\ncho model timeouts và partial responses\nLEAST operational overhead\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nIntegrate an Amazon API Gateway HTTP API with an AWS Lambda function to invoke Amazon Bedrock. Use Lambda response streaming to stream responses. Enforce token limits within the Lambda function. Implement retry logic for model timeouts by using Lambda and API Gateway timeout configurations.\nHTTP API\n(không phải REST API) = lighter weight, lower latency, lower cost → LEAST overhead\nLambda response streaming\n= native feature cho real-time streaming responses\nToken limits enforce trong Lambda = đơn giản, không cần infrastructure thêm\nLambda + API Gateway timeout configurations = retry logic built-in\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Connect an Amazon API Gateway HTTP API directly to Amazon Bedrock. Simulate streaming by using client-side polling. Enforce token limits on the frontend. Configure retry behavior by using API Gateway integration settings.\nClient-side polling ≠ true streaming\n→ không đáp ứng yêu cầu stream responses\nEnforce token limits \"on the frontend\" → không reliable\nKhông có proper retry logic\n❌ Connect an Amazon API Gateway WebSocket API to an Amazon ECS service that hosts a containerized inference server. Stream responses by using the WebSocket protocol. Enforce token limits within Amazon ECS. Handle model timeouts by using ECS task lifecycle hooks and restart policies.\nECS container =\nHIGH operational overhead\n(manage containers, scaling, etc.)\nWebSocket phức tạp hơn cần thiết\nECS lifecycle hooks cho retry = phức tạp\n❌ Integrate an Amazon API Gateway REST API with an AWS Lambda function that invokes Amazon Bedrock. Use Lambda response streaming to stream responses. Enforce token limits within the Lambda function. Implement retry logic by using Lambda and API Gateway timeout configurations.\nREST API\ntốn kém hơn và có nhiều overhead hơn\nHTTP API\nVề mặt kỹ thuật gần giống A nhưng HTTP API (A) là lựa chọn tối ưu hơn cho LEAST overhead\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nStreaming responses + LEAST overhead\n→\nLambda response streaming\n+\nHTTP API\n(không phải REST API)\nHTTP API vs REST API\n: HTTP API = cheaper, faster, less features | REST API = more features, more expensive\nClient-side polling\n≠\ntrue streaming\n→ KHÔNG đáp ứng yêu cầu streaming\nECS\n→ HIGH operational overhead → loại ngay khi thấy \"LEAST overhead\""}, {"number": 17, "status": "Correct", "question": "A company uses an organization in AWS Organizations with all features enabled to manage multiple AWS accounts. Employees use Amazon Bedrock across multiple accounts. The company must prevent specific topics and proprietary information from being included in prompts to Amazon Bedrock models. The company must ensure that employees can use only approved Amazon Bedrock models. The company centrally manages IAM roles for employees.\nWhich combination of solutions will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Use AWS CloudFormation to create a custom Amazon Bedrock guardrail that has a block filtering policy. Use stack sets to deploy the guardrail to each account in the organization.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Create an SCP that allows employees to use only approved models. Configure the SCP to require employees to specify a guardrail identifier in calls to invoke an approved model.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Use AWS CloudFormation to create a custom Amazon Bedrock guardrail that has a mask filtering policy. Use stack sets to deploy the guardrail to each account in the organization.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Create an IAM permissions boundary for each employee's IAM role. Configure the permissions boundary to require an approved Amazon Bedrock guardrail identifier to invoke Amazon Bedrock models. Create an SCP that allows employees to use only approved models.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "E", "text": "Create an SCP that prevents an employee from invoking a model if a centrally deployed guardrail identifier is not specified in a call to the model. Create a permissions boundary on each employee's IAM role that allows each employee to invoke only approved models.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["A", "B"], "explanation": "A.\nUse AWS CloudFormation to create a custom Amazon Bedrock guardrail that has a block filtering policy. Use stack sets to deploy the guardrail to each account in the organization."}, {"number": 18, "status": "Incorrect", "question": "A wildlife conservation agency operates zoos globally. The agency uses various sensors, trackers, and audiovisual recorders to monitor animal behavior. The agency wants to launch a generative AI (GenAI) assistant that can ingest multimodal data to study animal behavior.\nThe GenAI assistant must support natural language queries, avoid speculative behavioral interpretations, and maintain audit logs for ethical research audits.\nWhich solution will meet these requirements?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Configure Amazon Q Business to federate data across Amazon S3, Amazon Kinesis, and Amazon SageMaker Feature Store. Configure Amazon EventBridge to invoke data ingestion jobs. Use custom AWS Lambda functions to filter large language model (LLM) outputs for ethical compliance before returning results to users.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Use Amazon OpenSearch Serverless to index behavioral logs and telemetry events. Use Amazon Comprehend to extract entities. Use Amazon Bedrock to build a layer to answer questions. Embed study summaries into OpenSearch Serverless documents. Use IAM to control access. Use AWS CloudTrail to log user interactions with the AI assistant.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Ingest raw videos into Amazon Rekognition to detect animal postures and expressions. Use Amazon Data Firehose to stream sensor and GPS data into an Amazon S3 data lake. Prompt an Amazon Bedrock foundation model (FM) by using basic templates that are stored in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store. Use IAM policies to control access. Use AWS CloudTrail for audit logging.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Use Amazon SageMaker Processing and Amazon Transcribe to pre-process multimodal data. Ingest summaries into an Amazon Bedrock Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) knowledge base. Apply Amazon Bedrock guardrails to restrict speculative outputs. Use AWS AppConfig to manage prompt templates. Use AWS CloudTrail to log research activity for audits.", "is_correct": true}], "correct_answers": ["D"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nWildlife conservation agency\n, sensors/trackers/audiovisual recorders →\nmultimodal data\nGenAI assistant cần:\nIngest\nmultimodal data\n(video, sensor, GPS, audio)\nSupport\nnatural language queries\nTránh speculative behavioral interpretations (avoid speculation)\nMaintain\naudit logs\ncho ethical research\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nUse Amazon SageMaker Processing and Amazon Transcribe to pre-process multimodal data. Ingest summaries into an Amazon Bedrock RAG knowledge base. Apply Amazon Bedrock guardrails to restrict speculative outputs. Use AWS AppConfig to manage prompt templates. Use AWS CloudTrail to log research activity for audits.\nSageMaker Processing + Transcribe\n→ xử lý multimodal data (video, audio, sensor)\nBedrock RAG KB\n→ ground responses in actual data → tránh speculation\nBedrock Guardrails\n→ explicitly restrict speculative behavioral interpretations\nCloudTrail\n→ audit logs cho ethical research\nAppConfig\n→ quản lý prompt templates tập trung\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Ingest raw videos into Amazon Rekognition to detect animal postures and expressions. Use Amazon Data Firehose to stream sensor and GPS data into an Amazon S3 data lake. Prompt an Amazon Bedrock foundation model (FM) by using basic templates that are stored in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store. Use IAM policies to control access. Use AWS CloudTrail for audit logging.\nRekognition detect postures/expressions nhưng không xử lý sensor/GPS data\nParameter Store cho prompt templates = không phù hợp bằng AppConfig (thiếu version control, rollback)\nKhông có guardrails để ngăn speculation\n❌ Use Amazon OpenSearch Serverless to index behavioral logs and telemetry events. Use Amazon Comprehend to extract entities. Use Amazon Bedrock to build a layer to answer questions. Embed study summaries into OpenSearch Serverless documents. Use IAM to control access. Use AWS CloudTrail to log user interactions with the AI assistant.\nKhông handle multimodal data (video, audio)\nKhông có explicit mechanism để ngăn speculative outputs\nComprehend không phải tool cho multimodal processing\n❌ Configure Amazon Q Business to federate data across Amazon S3, Amazon Kinesis, and Amazon SageMaker Feature Store. Configure Amazon EventBridge to invoke data ingestion jobs. Use custom AWS Lambda functions to filter large language model (LLM) outputs for ethical compliance before returning results to users.\nAmazon Q Business không designed cho scientific/research multimodal data\nCustom Lambda để filter = high operational overhead\nKhông có proper audit mechanism\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nMultimodal data (video + audio + sensor)\n→\nSageMaker Processing + Transcribe\n(pre-process trước)\nAvoid speculative outputs\n→\nBedrock Guardrails\n(restrict speculative interpretations)\nAudit logs cho research\n→\nAWS CloudTrail\nPrompt template management\n→\nAWS AppConfig\n(version control, rollback) > Parameter Store"}, {"number": 19, "status": "Correct", "question": "A company uses Amazon Bedrock to implement a Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG)-based system to serve medical information to users. The company needs to compare multiple chunking strategies, evaluate the generation quality of two foundation models (FMs), and enforce quality thresholds for deployment.\nWhich Amazon Bedrock evaluation configuration will meet these requirements?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Create a retrieve-only evaluation job that uses a supported version of Anthropic Claude Sonnet as the evaluator model. Configure metrics for context relevance and context coverage. Define deployment thresholds in a separate CI/CD pipeline.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Create a separate evaluation job for each chunking strategy and FM combination. Use Amazon Bedrock built-in metrics for correctness and completeness. Manually review scores before deployment approval.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Set up a pipeline that uses multiple retrieve-only evaluation jobs to assess retrieval quality. Create separate evaluation jobs for both FMs that use Amazon Nova Pro as the LLM-as-a-judge model. Evaluate based on faithfulness and citation precision metrics.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Create a retrieve-and-generate evaluation job that uses custom precision at k metrics and an LLM-as-a-judge metric that uses a scale of 1-5. Include each chunking strategy in the evaluation dataset. Use a supported version of Anthropic Claude Sonnet to evaluate responses from both FMs.", "is_correct": true}], "correct_answers": ["D"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nRAG system\ncho\nmedical information\n, dùng Amazon Bedrock\nCần:\nSo sánh\nmultiple chunking strategies\nEvaluate\ngeneration quality của 2 FMs\nEnforce quality thresholds\ncho deployment\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nCreate a retrieve-and-generate evaluation job that uses custom precision at k metrics and an LLM-as-a-judge metric that uses a scale of 1-5. Include each chunking strategy in the evaluation dataset. Use a supported version of Anthropic Claude Sonnet to evaluate responses from both FMs.\nRetrieve-and-generate\njob = evaluate cả retrieval lẫn generation quality (đúng yêu cầu)\nCustom precision at k\n= đánh giá retrieval quality với chunking strategies\nLLM-as-a-judge\n= evaluate generation quality của 2 FMs\nInclude\neach chunking strategy\ntrong dataset → so sánh trực tiếp\nClaude Sonnet\n= supported evaluator model trong Bedrock Model Evaluation\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Create a retrieve-only evaluation job that uses a supported version of Anthropic Claude Sonnet as the evaluator model. Configure metrics for context relevance and context coverage. Define deployment thresholds in a separate CI/CD pipeline.\nRetrieve-only\nchỉ đánh giá retrieval, KHÔNG đánh giá generation quality của FMs\nKhông compare 2 FMs\nDeployment threshold trong CI/CD riêng = không integrated\n❌ Create a separate evaluation job for each chunking strategy and FM combination. Use Amazon Bedrock built-in metrics for correctness and completeness. Manually review scores before deployment approval.\nMultiple separate jobs = không efficient\nManual review\n= không phải enforce quality thresholds tự động\nBuilt-in metrics kém flexible hơn LLM-as-a-judge\n❌ Set up a pipeline that uses multiple retrieve-only evaluation jobs to assess retrieval quality. Create separate evaluation jobs for both FMs that use Amazon Nova Pro as the LLM-as-a-judge model. Evaluate based on faithfulness and citation precision metrics.\nRetrieve-only\n= không evaluate generation\nAmazon Nova Pro\n= không phải supported evaluator trong Bedrock Model Evaluation (Claude Sonnet là supported)\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nEvaluate cả retrieval lẫn generation\n→\nRetrieve-and-generate evaluation job\n(không phải retrieve-only)\nCompare chunking strategies\n→ include\neach chunking strategy\ntrong evaluation dataset\nLLM-as-a-judge\ntrong Bedrock → dùng\nAnthropic Claude Sonnet\n(supported evaluator)\nRetrieve-only\n→ chỉ test retrieval quality, KHÔNG test generation"}, {"number": 20, "status": "Correct", "question": "An insurance company uses existing Amazon SageMaker AI infrastructure to support a web-based application that allows customers to predict what their insurance premiums will be. The company stores customer data that is used to train the SageMaker AI model in an Amazon S3 bucket. The dataset is growing rapidly. The company wants a solution to continuously re-train the model. The solution must automatically re-train and re-deploy the model to the application when an employee uploads a new customer data file to the S3 bucket.\nWhich solution will meet these requirements?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Create an AWS Step Functions Express workflow with AWS SDK integrations to retrieve the customer data from the S3 bucket when an employee uploads a new file to the S3 bucket. Use a SageMaker Data Wrangler flow to export the data from the S3 bucket to SageMaker Autopilot. Use SageMaker Autopilot to re-deploy the model after it has been re-trained on the updated customer dataset.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Create an AWS Lambda function and webhook handlers to generate an event when an employee uploads a new file. Configure SageMaker Pipelines to re-deploy the model after it is re-trained on the updated customer dataset. Use Amazon EventBridge to create an event bus. Set the Lambda function event as the source and SageMaker Pipelines as the target.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Use AWS Glue to run an ETL job on each uploaded file. Configure the ETL job to use the AWS SDK to invoke the Sage Maker AI model endpoint. Use real-time inference with the endpoint to re-deploy the model after it is re-trained on the updated customer dataset.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Create an AWS Step Functions Standard workflow. Configure the first state to call an AWS Lambda function to respond when an employee uploads a new file to the S3 bucket. Use a pipeline in SageMaker Pipelines to re-deploy the model after it has been re-trained on the updated customer dataset. Use the next state in the workflow to run the pipeline when the first state receives a response.", "is_correct": true}], "correct_answers": ["D"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nInsurance company\n, SageMaker AI infrastructure\nCustomer data trong\nS3 bucket\n, dataset growing rapidly\nCần\nautomatically re-train và re-deploy\nmodel khi\nemployee uploads new data file to S3\nEvent-driven, continuous operation\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nCreate an AWS Step Functions Standard workflow. Configure the first state to call an AWS Lambda function to respond when an employee uploads a new file to the S3 bucket. Use a pipeline in SageMaker Pipelines to re-deploy the model after it has been re-trained. Use the next state in the workflow to run the pipeline when the first state receives a response.\nStep Functions Standard\norchestrate multi-step workflow (trigger → train → deploy)\nLambda\nresponds to S3 upload event → kicks off workflow\nSageMaker Pipelines\nhandles re-training và re-deployment\nMulti-state workflow đảm bảo sequential execution (train trước, deploy sau)\nStandard workflow = long-running, durable (phù hợp training job có thể mất nhiều giờ)\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Use AWS Glue to run an ETL job on each uploaded file. Configure the ETL job to use the AWS SDK to invoke the Sage Maker AI model endpoint. Use real-time inference with the endpoint to re-deploy the model after it is re-trained on the updated customer dataset.\nAWS Glue = ETL tool, không phải ML training orchestration\n\"Real-time inference to re-deploy\" = không có nghĩa trong context này\n❌ Create an AWS Lambda function and webhook handlers to generate an event when an employee uploads a new file. Configure SageMaker Pipelines to re-deploy the model after it is re-trained on the updated customer dataset. Use Amazon EventBridge to create an event bus. Set the Lambda function event as the source and SageMaker Pipelines as the target.\nEventBridge không thể invoke SageMaker Pipelines trực tiếp như target\nWebhook handlers = unnecessary complexity\n❌ Create an AWS Step Functions Express workflow with AWS SDK integrations to retrieve the customer data from the S3 bucket when an employee uploads a new file to the S3 bucket. Use a SageMaker Data Wrangler flow to export the data from the S3 bucket to SageMaker Autopilot. Use SageMaker Autopilot to re-deploy the model after it has been re-trained on the updated customer dataset.\nExpress workflow\n= short-lived (max 5 min) → không phù hợp cho training jobs (hours)\nAutopilot\n= AutoML, không phải re-training existing model\nData Wrangler không phù hợp cho automated retraining pipeline\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nLong-running ML workflow (train + deploy)\n→\nStep Functions Standard\n(không phải Express)\nStep Functions Express\n→ max 5 phút → KHÔNG phù hợp cho training jobs\nSageMaker Pipelines\n→ orchestrate ML workflows (training, evaluation, deployment)\nTrigger on S3 upload\n→ Lambda (không phải Glue, không phải trực tiếp EventBridge → SageMaker)"}, {"number": 21, "status": "Correct", "question": "A company is building a video analysis platform on AWS. The platform will analyze a large video archive by using Amazon Rekognition and Amazon Bedrock. The platform must comply with predefined privacy standards. The platform must also use secure model I/O, control foundation model (FM) access patterns, and provide an audit of who accessed what and when.\nWhich solution will meet these requirements?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Configure VPC endpoints for Amazon Bedrock model API calls. Implement Amazon Bedrock Guardrails to filter harmful or unauthorized content in prompts and responses. Use Amazon Bedrock trace events to track all agent and model invocations for auditing purposes. Export the traces to Amazon CloudWatch Logs as an audit record of model usage. Store all prompts and outputs in Amazon S3 with server-side encryption with AWS KMS keys (SSE-KMS).", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Define access control by using IAM with attribute-based controls to map departments to specific permissions. Configure VPC endpoints for Amazon Bedrock model API calls. Use IAM condition keys to enforce specific GuardrailIdentifier and ModelId values. Configure AWS CloudTrail to capture management and data events for S3 objects and KMS key usage activities. Enable S3 server access logging to record detailed file-level interactions with the video archives. Send all CloudTrail logs to AWS CloudTrail Lake. Set up Amazon CloudWatch alarms to detect and alert on unexpected activity from Amazon Bedrock, Amazon Rekognition, and AWS KMS.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Configure AWS CloudTrail Insights to analyze API call patterns across accounts and detect anomalous activity in Amazon Bedrock, Amazon Rekognition, Amazon S3, and AWS KMS. Deploy Amazon Macie to scan and classify the video archive. Use server-side encryption with AWS KMS keys (SSE-KMS) to encrypt all stored data. Configure CloudTrail to capture KMS API usage events for audit purposes. Configure Amazon EventBridge rules to process CloudTrail Insights anomalies and Macie findings. Use CloudWatch alarms to trigger automated notifications and security responses when potential security issues are detected.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Restrict access to services by using VPC endpoint policies. Use AWS Config to track resource changes and compliance with security rules. Use server-side encryption with AWS KMS keys (SSE-KMS) to encrypt data at rest. Store the model's I/O in separate Amazon S3 buckets. Enable S3 server access logging to track file-level interactions.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["B"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nVideo analysis platform\ndùng\nAmazon Rekognition + Amazon Bedrock\nYêu cầu:\nPrivacy standards\ncompliance\nSecure model I/O\nControl FM access patterns\nAudit trail\n: who accessed what and when\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nDefine access control by using IAM with attribute-based controls to map departments to specific permissions. Configure VPC endpoints for Amazon Bedrock model API calls. Use IAM condition keys to enforce specific GuardrailIdentifier and ModelId values. Configure AWS CloudTrail to capture management and data events for S3 objects and KMS key usage. Enable S3 server access logging to record detailed file-level interactions. Set up Amazon CloudWatch alarms to detect and alert on unexpected activity.\nAttribute-based IAM\n→ fine-grained access control per department\nVPC endpoints\n→ secure model I/O (không qua internet)\nIAM condition keys với GuardrailIdentifier + ModelId\n→ control FM access patterns cụ thể\nCloudTrail data events + S3 access logging\n→ comprehensive audit trail (who, what, when)\nCloudWatch alarms\n→ detect unexpected activity\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Configure VPC endpoints for Amazon Bedrock model API calls. Implement Amazon Bedrock Guardrails to filter harmful or unauthorized content in prompts and responses. Use Amazon Bedrock trace events to track all agent and model invocations for auditing purposes. Export the traces to Amazon CloudWatch Logs as an audit record of model usage. Store all prompts and outputs in Amazon S3 with server-side encryption with AWS KMS keys (SSE-KMS).\nThiếu\nIAM condition keys\nđể control FM access patterns\nCloudWatch Logs trace ≠ comprehensive audit trail\nKhông có attribute-based access control\n❌ Restrict access to services by using VPC endpoint policies. Use AWS Config to track resource changes and compliance with security rules. Use server-side encryption with AWS KMS keys (SSE-KMS) to encrypt data at rest. Store the model's I/O in separate Amazon S3 buckets. Enable S3 server access logging to track file-level interactions.\nAWS Config = track configuration changes, KHÔNG phải access audit trail\nKhông có IAM condition keys để control FM access patterns\nKhông comprehensive audit trail\n❌ Configure AWS CloudTrail Insights to analyze API call patterns across accounts and detect anomalous activity in Amazon Bedrock, Amazon Rekognition, Amazon S3, and AWS KMS. Deploy Amazon Macie to scan and classify the video archive. Use server-side encryption with AWS KMS keys (SSE-KMS) to encrypt all stored data. Configure CloudTrail to capture KMS API usage events for audit purposes. Configure Amazon EventBridge rules to process CloudTrail Insights anomalies and Macie findings. Use CloudWatch alarms to trigger automated notifications and security responses when potential security issues are detected.\nCloudTrail Insights = anomaly detection, không phải primary audit mechanism\nMacie = data classification, không phải FM access control\nPhức tạp, không address secure model I/O và FM access patterns\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nControl FM access patterns\n→\nIAM condition keys\nvới\nGuardrailIdentifier + ModelId\nSecure model I/O\n→\nVPC endpoints\ncho Bedrock\nAudit: who accessed what, when\n→\nCloudTrail data events + S3 server access logging\nAttribute-based access control\n→ IAM ABAC (map departments → permissions)\nAWS Config\n→ resource configuration compliance, KHÔNG phải access audit"}, {"number": 22, "status": "Correct", "question": "A company has a generative AI (GenAI) application that uses Amazon Bedrock to provide real-time responses to customer queries. The company has noticed intermittent failures with API calls to foundation models (FMs) during peak traffic periods.\nThe company needs a solution to handle transient errors and provide detailed observability into FM performance. The solution must prevent cascading failures during throttling events and provide distributed tracing across service boundaries to identify latency contributors. The solution must also enable correlation of performance issues with specific FM characteristics.\nWhich solution will meet these requirements?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Implement a custom retry mechanism with a fixed delay of 1 second between retries. Configure Amazon CloudWatch alarms to monitor the application's error rates and latency metrics.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Implement client-side caching of all FM responses. Add custom logging statements in the application code to record API call durations.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Configure the AWS SDK with standard retry mode and exponential backoff with jitter. Use AWS X-Ray tracing with annotations to identify and filter service components.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Configure the AWS SDK with adaptive retry mode. Use AWS CloudTrail distributed tracing to monitor throttling events.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["C"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nGenAI app\ndùng Bedrock,\nreal-time responses\n,\npeak traffic\ngây intermittent failures\nCần:\nHandle\ntransient errors\n(throttling)\nPrevent cascading failures\nDistributed tracing\nacross service boundaries\nCorrelate performance với\nFM characteristics\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nConfigure the AWS SDK with standard retry mode and exponential backoff with jitter. Use AWS X-Ray tracing with annotations to identify and filter service components.\nExponential backoff with jitter\n→ handle throttling, prevent cascading failures (không retry đồng thời)\nStandard retry mode\ntrong AWS SDK → built-in retry với proper backoff\nAWS X-Ray\n→ distributed tracing across service boundaries\nX-Ray annotations\n→ correlate traces với specific FM characteristics\nToàn bộ là SDK-level configuration → LEAST overhead\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Implement a custom retry mechanism with a fixed delay of 1 second between retries. Configure Amazon CloudWatch alarms to monitor the application's error rates and latency metrics.\nFixed delay\n= không phù hợp, có thể gây thundering herd problem\nCustom retry = more overhead vs SDK built-in\nCloudWatch alarms ≠ distributed tracing\n❌ Implement client-side caching of all FM responses. Add custom logging statements in the application code to record API call durations.\nCaching tất cả FM responses không phù hợp cho real-time responses\nCustom logging ≠ distributed tracing\nKhông address retry/cascading failure\n❌ Configure the AWS SDK with adaptive retry mode. Use AWS CloudTrail distributed tracing to monitor throttling events.\nCloudTrail\n= API audit logging, KHÔNG phải distributed tracing tool\nAdaptive retry mode\n= điều chỉnh retry rate nhưng không có jitter → vẫn có risk cascading\nX-Ray (B) tốt hơn CloudTrail cho distributed tracing\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nPrevent cascading failures + handle throttling\n→\nExponential backoff with jitter\nDistributed tracing across services\n→\nAWS X-Ray\n(không phải CloudTrail)\nCorrelate performance với FM\n→\nX-Ray annotations\nCloudTrail\n= API audit |\nX-Ray\n= distributed tracing → KHÔNG nhầm lẫn!\nFixed delay retry\n→ thundering herd problem → SAI"}, {"number": 23, "status": "Correct", "question": "A company is building a serverless application that uses AWS Lambda functions to help students around the world summarize notes. The application uses Anthropic Claude through Amazon Bedrock. The company observed that most of the traffic occurs during evenings in each time zone. Users report experiencing throttling errors during peak usage times in their times zones.\nThe company needs to resolve the throttling issues by ensuring continuous operation of the application. The solution must maintain application performance quality. The company needs a solution that does not require a fixed hourly cost during low traffic periods.\nWhich solution will meet these requirements?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Create custom Amazon CloudWatch metrics to monitor model errors. Set provisioned throughput to a value that is safely higher than the peak traffic observed.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Enable invocation logging in Amazon Bedrock. Monitor key metrics such as Invocations, InputTokenCount, OutputTokenCount, and Invocation Throttles. Distribute traffic across cross-Region inference endpoints.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Create custom Amazon CloudWatch metrics to monitor model errors. Set up a failover mechanism to redirect invocations to a backup AWS Region when the errors exceed a specified threshold.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Enable invocation logging in Amazon Bedrock. Monitor InvocationLatency, InvocationClientErrors, and InvocationServerErrors metrics. Distribute traffic across multiple versions of the same model.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["B"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nServerless app (Lambda)\ndùng\nAnthropic Claude trên Bedrock\n, students globally\nTraffic peaks\ntheo múi giờ (time zone)\n, gây\nthrottling errors\nYêu cầu:\nResolve throttling\nMaintain performance quality\nKhông có fixed hourly cost\nkhi low traffic\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nEnable invocation logging in Amazon Bedrock. Monitor key metrics such as Invocations, InputTokenCount, OutputTokenCount, and Invocation Throttles. Distribute traffic across cross-Region inference endpoints.\nInvocation logging\n→ monitor throttle metrics cụ thể của Bedrock\nInvocation Throttles metric\n→ identify khi nào throttling xảy ra\nCross-Region inference endpoints\n→ phân tán traffic theo multiple regions → giảm throttling\nKhông có fixed cost (cross-region inference = on-demand)\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Create custom Amazon CloudWatch metrics to monitor model errors. Set provisioned throughput to a value that is safely higher than the peak traffic observed.\nProvisioned throughput\n=\nFIXED HOURLY COST\n→ vi phạm yêu cầu \"no fixed hourly cost\"\n❌ Create custom Amazon CloudWatch metrics to monitor model errors. Set up a failover mechanism to redirect invocations to a backup AWS Region when the errors exceed a specified threshold.\nFailover là reactive (sau khi error xảy ra), không phải proactive load distribution\nKhông address throttling prevention\n❌ Enable invocation logging in Amazon Bedrock. Monitor InvocationLatency, InvocationClientErrors, and InvocationServerErrors metrics. Distribute traffic across multiple versions of the same model.\nMetrics sai: không có\nInvocationThrottles\n→ không detect throttling\nMultiple versions of same model\n≠\ncross-Region endpoints\n→ không giảm throttling\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nThrottling errors + no fixed cost\n→\nCross-Region inference endpoints\n(on-demand, không phải provisioned throughput)\nProvisioned throughput\n= FIXED HOURLY COST → loại ngay khi đề nói \"no fixed cost\"\nBedrock throttling metrics\n→\nInvocationThrottles\n(không phải ClientErrors/ServerErrors)\nCross-Region inference\n→ giảm throttling bằng cách phân tán load sang nhiều regions"}, {"number": 24, "status": "Correct", "question": "A company is building a generative AI (GenAI) application that processes financial reports and provides summaries for analysts. The application must run two compute environments. In one environment, AWS Lambda function must use the Python SDK to analyze reports on demand. In the second environment, Amazon EKS containers must use the JavaScript SDK to batch process multiple reports on a schedule. The application must maintain conversational context throughout multi-tum interactions, use the same foundation model (FM) across environments, and ensure consistent authentication.\nWhich solution will meet these requirements?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Use the Amazon Bedrock InvokeModel API with a separate authentication method for each environment. Store conversation states in Amazon DynamoDB. Use custom I/O formatting logic for each programming language.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Use the Amazon Bedrock Converse API directly in both environments with a common authentication mechanism that uses IAM roles. Store conversation states in Amazon ElastiCache. Creating programming language-specific wrappers for model parameters.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Create a centralized Amazon API Gateway REST API endpoint that handles all model interactions by using the InvokeModel API. Store interaction history in application process memory in each Lambda function or EKS container. Use environment variables to configure model parameters.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Use the Amazon Bedrock Converse API and IAM roles for authentication. Pass previous messages in the request messages array to maintain conversational context. Use programming language-specific SDKs to establish consistent API interfaces.", "is_correct": true}], "correct_answers": ["D"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nFinancial reports processing\n, 2 environments:\nLambda\n(Python SDK) → on-demand analysis\nAmazon EKS\n(JavaScript SDK) → batch processing theo schedule\nYêu cầu:\nConversational context\nthroughout multi-turn interactions\nSame FM\nacross both environments\nConsistent authentication\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nUse the Amazon Bedrock Converse API and IAM roles for authentication. Pass previous messages in the request messages array to maintain conversational context. Use programming language-specific SDKs to establish consistent API interfaces.\nConverse API\n= unified API cho multi-turn conversations, hỗ trợ cả Python và JavaScript SDK\nIAM roles\n= consistent authentication mechanism across Lambda và EKS\nPass previous messages in messages array\n= cách chuẩn để maintain conversational context\nLanguage-specific SDKs\n= Python (Lambda) + JavaScript (EKS) đều call cùng Converse API\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Use the Amazon Bedrock InvokeModel API with a separate authentication method for each environment. Store conversation states in Amazon DynamoDB. Use custom I/O formatting logic for each programming language.\nInvokeModel\nkhông có native multi-turn support\nSeparate auth\ncho mỗi environment → không consistent\nDynamoDB để store conversation = thêm dependency không cần thiết\n❌ Use the Amazon Bedrock Converse API directly in both environments with a common authentication mechanism that uses IAM roles. Store conversation states in Amazon ElastiCache. Creating programming language-specific wrappers for model parameters.\nElastiCache để store conversation state = unnecessary (Converse API handles via messages array)\nLanguage-specific wrappers = thêm complexity\n❌ Create a centralized Amazon API Gateway REST API endpoint that handles all model interactions by using the InvokeModel API. Store interaction history in application process memory in each Lambda function or EKS container. Use environment variables to configure model parameters.\nIn-memory storage = không persistent, mất context khi Lambda cold start\nAPI Gateway layer = unnecessary overhead\nInvokeModel không có multi-turn support\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nMulti-turn conversations + maintain context\n→\nBedrock Converse API\n+\nmessages array\nConsistent auth across Lambda + EKS\n→\nIAM roles\n(không phải separate auth methods)\nConverse API\nvs\nInvokeModel API\n: Converse = multi-turn support | InvokeModel = single turn\nElastiCache/DynamoDB cho conversation state\n→ KHÔNG cần nếu dùng Converse API messages array"}, {"number": 25, "status": "Correct", "question": "An international company is building an AI assistant that uses RAG. The company wants the AI assistant to have near real-time, low-latency performance. The AI assistant must provide service to several geographic areas. The company's customers will use proprietary data with the AI assistant. The proprietary data must not leave the company's immediate geographic area.\nWhich solution will meet these requirements?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Configure a knowledge base stored in the Amazon S3 Express One Zone storage class in each AWS Local Zone the company operates in. Use Amazon RDS to deploy a vector database in each Local Zone the company operates in. Deploy a large language model (LLM) to Amazon EC2 instances in each Local Zone. Configure the AI assistant to route prompts to the model in the respective Local Zone.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Deploy an Amazon Bedrock model with a cross-Region model inference profile. Create Amazon S3 buckets in each AWS Region the company operates in. Store a knowledge base in each respective S3 bucket. In each Region, configure Amazon Kendra to interact with the respective knowledge base. In each Region, configure an AWS Lambda function that uses Kendra and Amazon Bedrock to process AI assistant prompts.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Deploy an Amazon Bedrock model in each AWS Region the company operates in. Configure an Amazon Bedrock cross-Region model inference profile. Configure a vector database that uses Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases. Store the knowledge bases in Amazon S3 in each Region the company operates in.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Use AWS Outposts to deploy an outpost in each AWS Region the company operates in. Create Amazon S3 buckets to store knowledge bases in each corresponding Region. Deploy Amazon RDS configured as a vector database to each outpost. Deploy an Amazon Bedrock model with a cross-Region inference profile in a central Region.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["C"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nInternational company\n, RAG assistant,\nnear real-time, low-latency\nServe\nseveral geographic areas\nProprietary data\nkhông được\nrời khỏi geographic area\ncủa công ty\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nDeploy an Amazon Bedrock model in each AWS Region the company operates in. Configure an Amazon Bedrock cross-Region model inference profile. Configure a vector database that uses Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases. Store the knowledge bases in Amazon S3 in each Region the company operates in.\nDeploy per Region\n→ data stays trong geographic area → đáp ứng data residency\nCross-Region inference profile\n→ low-latency bằng cách route đến region gần nhất\nBedrock Knowledge Bases\n→ managed vector database, native Bedrock feature\nS3 per Region\n→ proprietary data không rời khỏi region\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Deploy an Amazon Bedrock model with a cross-Region model inference profile. Create Amazon S3 buckets in each AWS Region the company operates in. Store a knowledge base in each respective S3 bucket. In each Region, configure Amazon Kendra to interact with the respective knowledge base. In each Region, configure an AWS Lambda function that uses Kendra and Amazon Bedrock to process AI assistant prompts.\nAmazon Kendra\n= enterprise search, không phải vector database cho RAG\nThêm Kendra layer = unnecessary complexity và cost\nKendra không hỗ trợ semantic/vector search tốt bằng Bedrock KB\n❌ Use AWS Outposts to deploy an outpost in each AWS Region the company operates in. Create Amazon S3 buckets to store knowledge bases in each corresponding Region. Deploy Amazon RDS configured as a vector database to each outpost. Deploy an Amazon Bedrock model with a cross-Region inference profile in a central Region.\nAWS Outposts\n= on-premises hardware, overkill cho geographic regions\nRDS as vector database\n= phải tự manage pgvector\nCentral Region\ninference vi phạm data residency (data có thể route sang Region khác)\n❌ Configure a knowledge base stored in the Amazon S3 Express One Zone storage class in each AWS Local Zone the company operates in. Use Amazon RDS to deploy a vector database in each Local Zone the company operates in. Deploy a large language model (LLM) to Amazon EC2 instances in each Local Zone. Configure the AI assistant to route prompts to the model in the respective Local Zone.\nLocal Zones\nkhông phải equivalent với AWS Regions cho geographic distribution\nDeploy LLM lên EC2 = HIGH operational overhead\nRDS + EC2 = manage everything manually\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nData không rời geographic area + low-latency\n→\nDeploy per Region + S3 per Region\nCross-Region inference profile\n→ route đến region gần nhất, tăng resilience\nAmazon Kendra\n→ enterprise keyword search, KHÔNG phải vector/semantic search\nAWS Outposts\n→ on-premises extension của AWS, KHÔNG phải geographic distribution solution\nLocal Zones\n≠ Regions → không phải solution cho data residency requirements"}, {"number": 26, "status": "Correct", "question": "A company is using Amazon Bedrock to develop an AI-powered application that uses a foundation model (FM) that supports cross-Region inference and provisioned throughput. The application must serve users in Europe and North America with consistently low latency. The application must comply with data residency regulations that require European user data to remain within Europe-based AWS Regions.\nDuring testing, the application experiences service degradation when Regional traffic spikes reach service quotas. The company needs a solution that maintains application resilience and minimizes operational complexity.\nWhich solution will meet these requirements?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Deploy separate Amazon Bedrock instances in North American and European Regions. Use a custom routing layer that directs traffic based on user location. Configure Amazon CloudWatch alarms to monitor Regional service usage. Use Amazon SNS to send email alerts to the company when usage approaches specified thresholds.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Use Amazon Bedrock cross-Region inference profiles by specifying geographical codes in profile IDs when the application calls the InvokeModel API. Configure separate Amazon API Gateway HTTP APIs to direct European and North American users to the appropriate Regional endpoints.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Deploy a multi-Region Amazon API Gateway HTTP API and AWS Lambda functions that implement retry logic to handle throttling. Configure the Lambda functions to call the FM in the nearest secondary Region when the application reaches service quotas in the primary Region. Use intelligent routing to ensure compliance with data residency requirements.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Configure provisioned throughput for Amazon Bedrock in multiple Regions. Implement failover logic in the application code to switch between Regions when throttling occurs. Use AWS Global Accelerator to route traffic to the appropriate endpoints based on user location.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["B"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nAmazon Bedrock FM hỗ trợ\ncross-Region inference + provisioned throughput\nServe users ở\nEurope và North America\n,\nlow latency\nData residency\n: European user data phải ở trong\nEurope-based AWS Regions\nService quotas\nbị reach khi Regional traffic spikes\nCần:\napplication resilience\n,\nminimize operational complexity\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nUse Amazon Bedrock cross-Region inference profiles by specifying geographical codes in profile IDs when the application calls the InvokeModel API. Configure separate Amazon API Gateway HTTP APIs to direct European and North American users to the appropriate Regional endpoints.\nCross-Region inference profiles với geographical codes\n→ tự động route trong geographic boundary (EU data stays in EU)\nSeparate API Gateway HTTP APIs\n→ route users đến đúng region (EU → EU endpoints, NA → NA endpoints)\nInvokeModel API với profile IDs\n→ use Bedrock provisioned throughput + cross-region capability\nMinimize operational complexity (managed service, không cần custom routing logic)\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Deploy separate Amazon Bedrock instances in North American and European Regions. Use a custom routing layer that directs traffic based on user location. Configure Amazon CloudWatch alarms to monitor Regional service usage. Use Amazon SNS to send email alerts to the company when usage approaches specified thresholds.\nCustom routing layer\n= HIGH operational complexity\nCustom routing không phải native Bedrock feature\nSNS alerts không address resilience\n❌ Deploy a multi-Region Amazon API Gateway HTTP API and AWS Lambda functions that implement retry logic to handle throttling. Configure the Lambda functions to call the FM in the nearest secondary Region when the application reaches service quotas in the primary Region. Use intelligent routing to ensure compliance with data residency requirements.\nCustom Lambda routing = HIGH operational complexity\n\"Intelligent routing\" tự implement = complex\nCó thể vi phạm data residency nếu \"nearest secondary Region\" cross geographic boundary\n❌ Configure provisioned throughput for Amazon Bedrock in multiple Regions. Implement failover logic in the application code to switch between Regions when throttling occurs. Use AWS Global Accelerator to route traffic to the appropriate endpoints based on user location.\nCustom failover logic trong application code = HIGH operational complexity\nGlobal Accelerator không specifically designed cho Bedrock data residency routing\nFailover logic = reactive, không phải proactive\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nCross-Region + data residency + low latency\n→\nBedrock cross-Region inference profiles với geographical codes\nGeographical codes trong profile ID\n→ tự động giới hạn inference trong geographic area (EU codes = EU regions only)\nSeparate API Gateway per geography\n→ route users đến đúng regional endpoint\nCustom routing/failover logic\n→ HIGH operational complexity → loại khi đề nói \"minimize complexity\"\nGlobal Accelerator\n→ network routing, KHÔNG phải Bedrock-specific data residency solution"}, {"number": 27, "status": "Correct", "question": "A company is developing a generative AI (GenAI) application that uses Amazon Bedrock foundation models (FMs). The application has several custom tool integrations. The application has experienced unexpected token consumption surges despite consistent user traffic.\nThe company needs a solution that uses Amazon Bedrock model invocation logging to monitor InputTokenCount metrics and OutputTokenCount metrics. The solution must detect unusual patterns in tool usage and identify which specific tool integrations cause abnormal token consumption. The solution must also automatically adjust thresholds as traffic patterns change.\nWhich solution will meet these requirements?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Use Amazon CloudWatch Logs to capture model invocation logs. Create CloudWatch metric filters to extract tool-specific invocation patterns. Apply CloudWatch anomaly detection alarms that adjust baselines for each tool's metrics.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Store model invocation logs in an Amazon S3 bucket. Use AWS Glue to catalog the logs. Analyze token consumption patterns by using scheduled Amazon Athena queries that generate reports on tool usage trends.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Store model invocation logs in an Amazon S3 bucket. Create an AWS Lambda function to process logs in real time. Manually update Amazon CloudWatch alarm thresholds based on token consumption trends that the Lambda function identifies.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Use Amazon CloudWatch Logs to capture model invocation logs. Create CloudWatch dashboards based on InputTokenCount metrics and OutputTokenCount metrics. Configure static CloudWatch alarms with fixed thresholds for each tool integration.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["A"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nGenAI app\ndùng Bedrock với\ncustom tool integrations\nToken consumption surges\nbất thường dù traffic ổn định\nCần:\nMonitor\nInputTokenCount + OutputTokenCount\n(yêu cầu cụ thể trong đề)\nDetect\nunusual patterns trong tool usage\nIdentify\nspecific tool integrations\ngây abnormal consumption\nAutomatically adjust thresholds\nkhi traffic patterns thay đổi\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nUse Amazon CloudWatch Logs to capture model invocation logs. Create CloudWatch metric filters to extract tool-specific invocation patterns. Apply CloudWatch anomaly detection alarms that adjust baselines for each tool's metrics.\nCloudWatch Logs\ncapture Bedrock invocation logs (bao gồm InputTokenCount, OutputTokenCount)\nMetric filters\n→ extract patterns theo\ntừng tool integration cụ thể\nAnomaly detection alarms\n→ tự động adjust thresholds khi traffic pattern thay đổi\nĐáp ứng tất cả 3 yêu cầu: detect unusual patterns + identify specific tools + auto-adjust thresholds\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Use Amazon CloudWatch Logs to capture model invocation logs. Create CloudWatch dashboards based on InputTokenCount metrics and OutputTokenCount metrics. Configure static CloudWatch alarms with fixed thresholds for each tool integration.\nStatic/fixed thresholds\n→ KHÔNG tự động adjust khi traffic patterns thay đổi\nVi phạm yêu cầu \"automatically adjust thresholds\"\n❌ Store model invocation logs in an Amazon S3 bucket. Use AWS Glue to catalog the logs. Analyze token consumption patterns by using scheduled Amazon Athena queries that generate reports on tool usage trends.\nScheduled Athena queries\n= không real-time, không auto-adjust thresholds\nGlue + Athena = batch analysis, không phải anomaly detection\nKhông identify specific tool integrations real-time\n❌ Store model invocation logs in an Amazon S3 bucket. Create an AWS Lambda function to process logs in real time. Manually update Amazon CloudWatch alarm thresholds based on token consumption trends that the Lambda function identifies.\nManual threshold updates\n→ KHÔNG \"automatically adjust\"\nCustom Lambda để process logs = high operational overhead\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nAutomatically adjust thresholds\n→\nCloudWatch Anomaly Detection\n(KHÔNG phải static alarms)\nTool-specific patterns từ logs\n→\nCloudWatch Metric Filters\nBedrock invocation logs\n→\nCloudWatch Logs\n(enable trong Bedrock settings)\nStatic alarms\n→ không adjust → vi phạm \"automatically adjust\" requirement\nAnomaly Detection\n= ML-based, auto-baseline adjustment"}, {"number": 28, "status": "Correct", "question": "A company upgraded its Amazon Bedrock powered foundation model (FM) that supports a multilingual customer service assistant. After the upgrade, the assistant exhibited inconsistent behavior across languages. The assistant began generating different responses in some languages when presented with identical questions.\nThe company needs a solution to detect and address similar problems for future updates. The evaluation must be completed within 45 minutes for all supported languages. The evaluation must process at least 15,000 test conversations in parallel. The evaluation process must be fully automated and integrated into the CI/CD pipeline. The solution must block deployment if quality thresholds are not met.\nWhich solution will meet these requirements?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Create a distributed traffic simulation framework that sends translation-heavy workloads to the assistant in multiple languages simultaneously. Use Amazon CloudWatch metrics to monitor latency, concurrency, and throughput. Run simulations before production releases to identify infrastructure bottlenecks.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Deploy the assistant in multiple AWS Regions with Amazon Route 53 latency-based routing and AWS Global Accelerator to improve global performance. Store multilingual conversation logs in Amazon S3. Perform weekly post-deployment audits to review consistency.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Create a pre-processing pipeline that normalizes all incoming messages into a consistent format before sending the messages to the assistant. Apply rule-based checks to flag potential hallucinations in the outputs. Focus the evaluation on the normalized text to simplify testing across languages.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Set up standardized multilingual test conversations with identical meaning. Run the test conversations in parallel by using Amazon Bedrock model evaluation jobs. Apply similarity and hallucination thresholds. Integrate the process into the CI/CD pipeline to block releases that fail.", "is_correct": true}], "correct_answers": ["D"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nMultilingual customer service assistant\ntrên Bedrock\nSau upgrade:\ninconsistent behavior across languages\n(identical questions → different responses)\nYêu cầu:\nDetect và address vấn đề cho\nfuture updates\nHoàn thành trong\n45 phút\ncho tất cả languages\nProcess\nít nhất 15,000 test conversations in parallel\nFully automated\nvà\nintegrated into CI/CD pipeline\nBlock deployment\nnếu quality thresholds không đạt\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nSet up standardized multilingual test conversations with identical meaning. Run the test conversations in parallel by using Amazon Bedrock model evaluation jobs. Apply similarity and hallucination thresholds. Integrate the process into the CI/CD pipeline to block releases that fail.\nStandardized multilingual test conversations\n→ detect inconsistency across languages\nBedrock model evaluation jobs\n→ parallel processing của 15,000+ conversations\nSimilarity thresholds\n→ enforce consistency giữa các languages\nCI/CD integration với blocking\n→ tự động block deployment khi threshold không đạt\nFully automated, scalable\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Create a distributed traffic simulation framework that sends translation-heavy workloads to the assistant in multiple languages simultaneously. Use Amazon CloudWatch metrics to monitor latency, concurrency, and throughput. Run simulations before production releases to identify infrastructure bottlenecks.\nTraffic simulation → test infrastructure, KHÔNG test language consistency\nCloudWatch metrics (latency, throughput) ≠ quality/consistency metrics\nKhông address linguistic inconsistency\n❌ Deploy the assistant in multiple AWS Regions with Amazon Route 53 latency-based routing and AWS Global Accelerator to improve global performance. Store multilingual conversation logs in Amazon S3. Perform weekly post-deployment audits to review consistency.\nWeekly audits\n= reactive, không phải CI/CD pipeline integration\nRoute 53 + Global Accelerator = networking, không address consistency\nPost-deployment audit KHÔNG block deployment\n❌ Create a pre-processing pipeline that normalizes all incoming messages into a consistent format before sending the messages to the assistant. Apply rule-based checks to flag potential hallucinations in the outputs. Focus the evaluation on the normalized text to simplify testing across languages.\nNormalizing input masks linguistic differences → không test real multilingual behavior\nRule-based checks\n= không scalable cho 15,000+ conversations\nKhông CI/CD integrated\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nParallel evaluation + CI/CD + block deployment\n→\nAmazon Bedrock Model Evaluation jobs\n+ CI/CD integration\nConsistency across languages\n→\nsimilarity thresholds\ntrong evaluation\nBlock deployment on failure\n→ CI/CD pipeline với evaluation gate\nTraffic simulation\n→ test infrastructure performance, KHÔNG phải language quality\nWeekly/post-deployment audits\n→ reactive, KHÔNG phải CI/CD gate"}, {"number": 29, "status": "Correct", "question": "A company is planning to deploy multiple generative AI (GenAI) applications to five independent business units that operate in multiple countries in Europe and the Americas. Each application uses Amazon Bedrock Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) patterns with business unit-specific knowledge bases that store terabytes of unstructured data.\nThe company must establish well-architected, standardized components for security controls, observability practices, and deployment patterns across all the GenAI applications. The components must be reusable, versioned, and governed consistently.\nWhich solution will meet these requirements?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Configure Amazon API Gateway REST API endpoints for the GenAI applications. Deploy common security, observability, and RAG patterns based on the AWS Well-Architected Generative AI Lens in standardized AWS CloudFormation templates. Use CloudFormation Guard after the deployment to validate policy compliance in each business unit.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Document security controls, observability requirements, and RAG patterns based on the AWS Well-Architected Generative AI Lens in a shared design document. Use Amazon Macie to enforce deployment. Delegate implementation responsibility to each business unit.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Create standardized AWS CloudFormation templates to implement security, observability, and RAG patterns based on the AWS Well-Architected Generative AI Lens. Establish a centralized repository that performs version control. Integrate a CI/CD pipeline with CloudFormation Guard to enforce consistent and repeatable deployments across business units.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Use AWS Service Catalog to define standardized portfolios and versioned products for each business unit. Use the portfolios to enforce security, observability, and RAG patterns based on the AWS Well-Architected Generative AI Lens. Require the business units to use the Service Catalog console to deploy resources.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["C"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\n5 business units\n, Europe + Americas,\nmultiple countries\nMỗi unit có\nBedrock RAG + knowledge base\n(terabytes of unstructured data)\nCần:\nstandardized, reusable, versioned, governed\ncomponents cho:\nSecurity controls\nObservability practices\nDeployment patterns\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nCreate standardized AWS CloudFormation templates to implement security, observability, and RAG patterns based on the AWS Well-Architected Generative AI Lens. Establish a centralized repository that performs version control. Integrate a CI/CD pipeline with CloudFormation Guard to enforce consistent and repeatable deployments across business units.\nCloudFormation templates\n= infrastructure as code, reusable, versionable\nAWS Well-Architected GenAI Lens\n= best practices foundation cho GenAI governance\nCentralized repository + version control\n= governed, consistent\nCI/CD + CloudFormation Guard\n= enforce compliance automatically trước deployment\nĐáp ứng tất cả: reusable + versioned + governed + standardized\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Configure Amazon API Gateway REST API endpoints for the GenAI applications. Deploy common security, observability, and RAG patterns based on the AWS Well-Architected Generative AI Lens in standardized AWS CloudFormation templates. Use CloudFormation Guard after the deployment to validate policy compliance in each business unit.\nCloudFormation Guard after deployment\n= reactive (sau khi deploy) → Nên dùng Guard trong CI/CD (trước deploy) = proactive\nAPI Gateway endpoints không liên quan đến standardized deployment patterns\nKhông có centralized repository/version control\n❌ Use AWS Service Catalog to define standardized portfolios and versioned products for each business unit. Use the portfolios to enforce security, observability, and RAG patterns based on the AWS Well-Architected Generative AI Lens. Require the business units to use the Service Catalog console to deploy resources.\nService Catalog → IT governance cho end-users, nhưng\nthiếu CI/CD integration\nRequire console usage\n→ không automated, không CI/CD integrated\nKhông enforce automated compliance như CloudFormation Guard\n❌ Document security controls, observability requirements, and RAG patterns based on the AWS Well-Architected Generative AI Lens in a shared design document. Use Amazon Macie to enforce deployment. Delegate implementation responsibility to each business unit.\nShared document\n= không versioned, không automated\nMacie\n= data classification, KHÔNG phải deployment enforcement tool\nDelegate implementation\n= inconsistent, không governed centrally\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nReusable + versioned + governed GenAI patterns\n→\nCloudFormation templates + centralized repo + version control\nAWS Well-Architected GenAI Lens\n→ best practices cho GenAI security, observability, RAG\nCloudFormation Guard trong CI/CD\n= proactive enforcement (trước deploy) | Guard after deployment = reactive\nAWS Service Catalog\n→ IT product catalog nhưng thiếu CI/CD pipeline integration\nDelegate implementation\n→ inconsistency → KHÔNG phải \"standardized\""}, {"number": 30, "status": "Correct", "question": "A company is designing a solution that uses foundation models (FMs) to support multiple AI workloads. Some FMs must be invoked on demand and in real time. Other FMs require consistent high-throughput access for batch processing.\nThe solution must support hybrid deployment patterns and run workloads across cloud infrastructure and on-premises infrastructure to comply with data residency and compliance requirements.\nWhich combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Deploy FMs to Amazon SageMaker AI endpoints with support for edge deployment by using Amazon SageMaker Neo. Orchestrate the FMs by using AWS Lambda to support hybrid deployment.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Use Amazon Bedrock with auto-scaling to handle unpredictable traffic surges.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Configure provisioned throughput in Amazon Bedrock to ensure consistent performance for high-volume workloads.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Use AWS Lambda to orchestrate low-latency FM inference by invoking FMs hosted on Amazon SageMaker AI asynchronous endpoints.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "E", "text": "Use Amazon SageMaker JumpStart to host and invoke the FMs.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["A", "C"], "explanation": "A.\nDeploy FMs to Amazon SageMaker AI endpoints with support for edge deployment by using Amazon SageMaker Neo. Orchestrate the FMs by using AWS Lambda to support hybrid deployment."}, {"number": 31, "status": "Correct", "question": "A company deploys multiple Amazon Bedrock based generative AI (GenAI) applications across multiple business units for customer service, content generation, and document analysis. Some applications show unpredictable token consumption patterns. The company requires a comprehensive observability solution that provides real-time visibility into token usage patterns across multiple models. The observability solution must support custom dashboards for multiple stakeholder groups and provide alerting capabilities for token consumption across all the foundational models that the company's applications use.\nWhich combination of solutions will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead? (Choose two.)", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Create custom Amazon CloudWatch dashboards that combine native Amazon Bedrock token and invocation CloudWatch metrics. Set up CloudWatch alarms to monitor token usage thresholds.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Use Amazon CloudWatch metrics as data sources to create custom Amazon QuickSight dashboards that show token usage trends and usage patterns across FMs.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Create dashboards that show token usage trends and patterns across the company's FMs by using an Amazon Bedrock zero-ETL integration with Amazon Managed Grafana.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Implement Amazon EventBridge rules to capture Amazon Bedrock model invocation events. Route token usage data to an Amazon Data Firehose delivery stream that targets Amazon OpenSearch Serverless. Use OpenSearch dashboards to analyze usage patterns.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "E", "text": "Use Amazon CloudWatch Logs Insights to analyze Amazon Bedrock invocation logs for token consumption patterns and usage attribution by application. Create custom queries to identify high-usage scenarios. Add log widgets to dashboards to enable continuous monitoring.", "is_correct": true}], "correct_answers": ["A", "E"], "explanation": "A.\nCreate custom Amazon CloudWatch dashboards that combine native Amazon Bedrock token and invocation CloudWatch metrics. Set up CloudWatch alarms to monitor token usage thresholds."}, {"number": 32, "status": "Correct", "question": "A company is building a legal research AI assistant that uses Amazon Bedrock with an Anthropic Claude foundation model (FM). The AI assistant must retrieve highly relevant case law documents to augment the FM's responses. The AI assistant must identify semantic relationships between legal concepts, specific legal terminology, and citations. The AI assistant must perform quickly and return precise results.\nWhich solution will meet these requirements?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Use Amazon OpenSearch service to deploy a hybrid search architecture that combines vector search with keyword search. Apply an Amazon Bedrock reranker model to optimize result relevance.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Use Amazon OpenSearch Service with vector search and Amazon Bedrock Titan embeddings to index and search legal documents. Use custom AWS Lambda functions to merge results with keyword-based filters that are stored in an Amazon RDS database.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Configure an Amazon Bedrock knowledge base to use a default vector search configuration. Use Amazon Bedrock to expand queries to improve retrieval for legal documents based on specific terminology and citations.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Enable the Amazon Kendra query suggestion feature for end users. Use Amazon Bedrock to perform post-processing of search results to identify semantic similarity in the documents and to produce precise results.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["A"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nLegal research AI assistant\ndùng Bedrock + Anthropic Claude\nCần retrieve\nhighly relevant case law documents\nIdentify\nsemantic relationships\ngiữa:\nLegal concepts\nSpecific legal terminology\nCitations\nYêu cầu:\nperform quickly\n,\nreturn precise results\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nUse Amazon OpenSearch Service to deploy a hybrid search architecture that combines vector search with keyword search. Apply an Amazon Bedrock reranker model to optimize result relevance.\nHybrid search\n(vector + keyword) = tối ưu cho legal domain:\nVector search\n→ semantic relationships, legal concepts\nKeyword search\n→ exact legal terminology, citation matching\nReranker model\n→ optimize final relevance của combined results →\nprecise results\nOpenSearch native hybrid search → perform quickly\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Configure an Amazon Bedrock knowledge base to use a default vector search configuration. Use Amazon Bedrock to expand queries to improve retrieval for legal documents based on specific terminology and citations.\nDefault vector search only\n→ thiếu exact keyword matching cho specific legal terminology và citations\nQuery expansion có thể làm giảm precision (tìm ra nhiều nhưng kém chính xác hơn)\n❌ Enable the Amazon Kendra query suggestion feature for end users. Use Amazon Bedrock to perform post-processing of search results to identify semantic similarity in the documents and to produce precise results.\nKendra query suggestion = suggest queries, không phải retrieve documents\nPost-processing bởi Bedrock = thêm latency, không \"perform quickly\"\nKendra không phải optimal cho legal semantic search ở scale\n❌ Use Amazon OpenSearch Service with vector search and Amazon Bedrock Titan embeddings to index and search legal documents. Use custom AWS Lambda functions to merge results with keyword-based filters that are stored in an Amazon RDS database.\nCustom Lambda + RDS\n= HIGH operational complexity\nMerging logic trong Lambda = fragile, slow\nRDS cho keyword filters = over-engineered so với OpenSearch hybrid search native\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nSemantic relationships + specific terminology + citations\n→\nHybrid search\n(vector + keyword)\nPrecise results sau retrieval\n→\nReranker model\nLegal terminology exact matching\n→ cần\nkeyword search\n(không chỉ vector)\nHybrid search\n= OpenSearch native feature, không cần custom Lambda/RDS\nVector only → semantic nhưng miss exact terms | Keyword only → exact nhưng miss semantic →\nHybrid = best of both"}, {"number": 33, "status": "Correct", "question": "Example Corp provides a personalized video generation service that millions of enterprise customers use. Customers generate marketing videos by submitting prompts to the company's proprietary generative AI (GenAI) model. To improve output relevance and personalization, Example Corp wants to enhance the prompts by using customer-specific context such as product preferences, customer attributes, and business history.\nThe customers have strict data governance requirements. The customers must retain full ownership and control over their own data. The customers do not require real-time access. However, semantic accuracy must be high and retrieval latency must remain low to support customer experience use cases.\nExample Corp wants to minimize architectural complexity in its integration pattern. Example Corp does not want to deploy and manage services in each customer's environment unless necessary.\nWhich solution will meet these requirements?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Use federated search with Model Context Protocol (MCP) by deploying real-time MCP servers for each customer. Retrieve data in real time during prompt generation.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Ensure that each customer sets up an Amazon Q Business index that includes the customer's internal data. Ensure that each customer designates Example Corp as a data accessor to allow Example Corp to retrieve relevant content by using a secure API to enrich prompts at runtime.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Ensure that each customer configures an Amazon Bedrock knowledge base. Allow cross-account querying so Example Corp can retrieve structured data for prompt augmentation.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Configure Amazon Kendra to crawl customer data sources. Share the resulting indexes across accounts so Example Corp can query each customer's Amazon Kendra index to retrieve augmentation data.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["B"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nExample Corp\n- personalized video generation, dùng proprietary GenAI model\nĐề bài có 4 điều kiện mấu chốt cần thoả mãn đồng thời:\nCustomer giữ toàn quyền sở hữu & kiểm soát dữ liệu\n(data governance nghiêm ngặt)\nKhông cần real-time access\n, nhưng\nsemantic accuracy phải cao\nvà\nlatency phải thấp\nTối thiểu hoá độ phức tạp kiến trúc\n— Example Corp\nkhông muốn\nphải deploy/quản lý service trong môi trường của từng customer\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nEnsure that each customer sets up an Amazon Q Business index that includes the customer's internal data. Ensure that each customer designates Example Corp as a data accessor to allow Example Corp to retrieve relevant content by using a secure API to enrich prompts at runtime.\nAmazon Q Business có tính năng\n\"data accessor\"\n(ISV accessor) được thiết kế chính xác cho use case này: mỗi customer tự tạo và quản lý\nAmazon Q Business index\nchứa dữ liệu nội bộ của họ (product preferences, business history...) — dữ liệu\nvẫn nằm trong tài khoản/quyền kiểm soát của customer\n, không bị copy hay di chuyển sang môi trường của Example Corp. Sau đó customer chỉ cần\ncấp quyền \"data accessor\"\ncho Example Corp, cho phép Example Corp\ntruy vấn\n(không phải sở hữu) nội dung liên quan qua một\nsecure API\ntại thời điểm cần enrich prompt.\nĐiều này thoả mãn tất cả yêu cầu:\nOwnership & control\n: dữ liệu và index luôn thuộc về customer, Example Corp chỉ được \"mượn\" quyền truy vấn có kiểm soát — đúng chuẩn data governance nghiêm ngặt.\nSemantic accuracy cao + latency thấp\n: Amazon Q Business được xây dựng cho enterprise search/RAG, có khả năng semantic retrieval hiệu năng cao sẵn có.\nTối thiểu kiến trúc phức tạp\n: Example Corp\nkhông phải tự deploy hạ tầng\ntrong môi trường từng customer — chỉ cần gọi API tới data accessor. Việc setup index là trách nhiệm của\ncustomer\n, không phải Example Corp.\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Use federated search with Model Context Protocol (MCP) by deploying real-time MCP servers for each customer. Retrieve data in real time during prompt generation.\nDeploy MCP servers for each customer\n→ vi phạm yêu cầu \"không deploy trong customer environment\"\nReal-time retrieval\n→ đề nói không cần real-time → unnecessary complexity\n❌ Ensure that each customer configures an Amazon Bedrock knowledge base. Allow cross-account querying so Example Corp can retrieve structured data for prompt augmentation.\nBedrock Knowledge Base không có cơ chế \"data accessor\" chuẩn hoá dành riêng cho mô hình multi-tenant B2B như Q Business.\nCross-account querying kiểu này đòi hỏi Example Corp phải tự thiết lập cơ chế truy cập, quản lý permission phức tạp cho\nhàng triệu\ncustomer riêng lẻ →\ntăng độ phức tạp kiến trúc\n, đi ngược lại yêu cầu \"minimize architectural complexity\".\n❌ Configure Amazon Kendra to crawl customer data sources. Share the resulting indexes across accounts so Example Corp can query each customer's Amazon Kendra index to retrieve augmentation data.\nViệc\n\"share indexes across accounts\"\nđồng nghĩa index (và gián tiếp là dữ liệu) được\nchia sẻ trực tiếp\nsang phía Example Corp truy cập tự do, làm mờ ranh giới ownership — không đảm bảo chặt chẽ nguyên tắc \"customer retains full ownership and control\" như cơ chế data accessor có kiểm soát của Q Business. Kendra cũng không có khái niệm \"data accessor\" managed sẵn cho mô hình chia sẻ có kiểm soát này.\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nCustomer data ownership + Example Corp access\n→\nAmazon Q Business\nvới\ndata accessor\npattern\nNo deploy in customer environment\n→ loại các option cần deploy server/infrastructure tại customer\nHigh semantic accuracy\n→ Q Business vector search > Kendra keyword search\nAmazon Q Business data accessor\n= cho phép third party truy cập data mà không transfer ownership\nMCP servers per customer\n→ deploy trong customer environment → vi phạm constraint"}, {"number": 34, "status": "Correct", "question": "A healthcare company is developing a document management system that stores medical research papers in an Amazon S3 bucket. The company needs to build a comprehensive metadata framework that will improve search precision for a generative AI (GenAI) application that analyzes the research papers. The metadata framework must include document timestamps, author information, and research domain classifications.\nThe solution must maintain a consistent metadata structure across all uploaded documents. The solution must give foundation models (FMs) the ability to understand document context without accessing the full content.\nWhich solution will meet these requirements?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Store document timestamps in Amazon S3 system metadata. Use S3 object tags to implement domain classification. Implement custom user-defined metadata to store author information.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Set up S3 Object Lock with legal holds to track document timestamps. Use S3 object tags to store author information. Implement S3 access points for domain classification.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Use S3 Inventory reports to track document timestamps. Create S3 access points to implement domain classification. Store author information in S3 Storage Lens dashboards.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Use custom user-defined metadata to store author information. Use S3 Object Lock retention periods to track document timestamps. Use S3 Event Notifications to implement domain classification.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["A"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nHealthcare company\n, document management system, medical research papers lưu trong\nS3\nCần\ncomprehensive metadata framework\ncho GenAI app:\nDocument timestamps\nAuthor information\nResearch domain classifications\nConsistent metadata structure\nacross all documents\nFMs cần\nunderstand document context without accessing full content\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nStore document timestamps in Amazon S3 system metadata. Use S3 object tags to implement domain classification. Implement custom user-defined metadata to store author information.\nS3 system metadata\n→ timestamps (LastModified, etc.) được quản lý tự động và consistently\nS3 object tags\n→ key-value pairs lý tưởng cho domain classification (searchable, filterable)\nCustom user-defined metadata\n→ flexible storage cho author information\nTất cả native S3 features → consistent structure, FMs có thể read metadata mà không cần full content\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Set up S3 Object Lock with legal holds to track document timestamps. Use S3 object tags to store author information. Implement S3 access points for domain classification.\nS3 Object Lock\n= WORM storage cho compliance, KHÔNG phải để track timestamps\nS3 access points\n= control access patterns, KHÔNG phải store classification data\nSai mục đích của các features\n❌ Use S3 Inventory reports to track document timestamps. Create S3 access points to implement domain classification. Store author information in S3 Storage Lens dashboards.\nS3 Inventory\n= list objects cho auditing/reporting, không phải per-document timestamp metadata\nS3 Storage Lens\n= analytics dashboard, KHÔNG phải metadata storage\nHoàn toàn sai mục đích của các services\n❌ Use custom user-defined metadata to store author information. Use S3 Object Lock retention periods to track document timestamps. Use S3 Event Notifications to implement domain classification.\nS3 Object Lock retention periods\n= compliance/immutability, KHÔNG phải timestamp metadata\nS3 Event Notifications\n= trigger events khi có changes, KHÔNG phải store classifications\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nDocument timestamps\n→\nS3 system metadata\n(tự động, consistent)\nClassification/categorical data\n→\nS3 object tags\n(searchable, filterable, key-value)\nCustom attributes (author, etc.)\n→\nS3 user-defined metadata\n(x-amz-meta-*)\nS3 Object Lock\n→ WORM/compliance, KHÔNG phải timestamps\nS3 Access Points\n→ access control patterns, KHÔNG phải metadata storage\nS3 Storage Lens\n→ usage analytics, KHÔNG phải document metadata"}, {"number": 35, "status": "Incorrect", "question": "A financial services company is developing a customer service AI assistant application that uses a foundation model (FM) in Amazon Bedrock. The application must provide transparent responses by documenting reasoning and by citing sources that are used for Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG). The application must capture comprehensive audit trails for all responses to users. The application must be able to serve up to 10,000 concurrent users and must respond to each customer inquiry within 2 seconds.\nWhich solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Enable tracing for Amazon Bedrock agents. Configure structured prompts that direct the FM to provide evidence presentations. Integrate Amazon Bedrock knowledge bases with data sources to enable RAG. Configure the application to reference and cite authoritative content. Deploy the application in a Multi-AZ architecture. Use Amazon API Gateway and AWS Lambda functions to scale the application. Use Amazon CloudFront to provide low-latency delivery.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Use Amazon CloudWatch to monitor latency and error rates. Embed model prompts directly in the application backend to cite sources. Store application interactions with users in Amazon RDS for audits.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Enable tracing for Amazon Bedrock agents. Integrate a custom RAG pipeline with Amazon OpenSearch Service to retrieve and cite sources. Configure structured prompts to present retrieved evidence. Deploy the application behind an Amazon API Gateway REST API. Use AWS Lambda functions and Amazon CloudFront to scale the application and to provide low latency. Store logs in Amazon S3 and use AWS CloudTrail to capture audit trails.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Store generated responses and supporting evidence in an Amazon S3 bucket. Enable versioning on the bucket for audits. Use AWS Glue to catalog retrieved documents. Process the retrieved documents in Amazon Athena to generate periodic compliance reports.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["A"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nFinancial services\n, customer service AI assistant,\nBedrock + RAG\nYêu cầu:\nTransparent responses\nvới reasoning và citing sources\nComprehensive audit trails\ncủa tất cả responses\nScale\n10,000 concurrent users\n, respond\nwithin 2 seconds\nLEAST operational overhead\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nEnable tracing for Amazon Bedrock agents. Configure structured prompts that direct the FM to provide evidence presentations. Integrate Amazon Bedrock knowledge bases with data sources to enable RAG. Configure the application to reference and cite authoritative content. Deploy in a Multi-AZ architecture. Use Amazon API Gateway and AWS Lambda to scale the application. Use Amazon CloudFront to provide low-latency delivery.\nBedrock agent tracing\n→ audit trails của reasoning và responses\nStructured prompts\n→ direct FM để cite sources → transparent responses\nBedrock Knowledge Bases\n→ native RAG, managed service\nMulti-AZ + API Gateway + Lambda + CloudFront\n→ scale 10,000 concurrent users, < 2 seconds\nTất cả managed services → LEAST operational overhead\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Enable tracing for Amazon Bedrock agents. Integrate a custom RAG pipeline with Amazon OpenSearch Service to retrieve and cite sources. Configure structured prompts to present retrieved evidence. Deploy the application behind an Amazon API Gateway REST API. Use AWS Lambda functions and Amazon CloudFront to scale the application and to provide low latency. Store logs in Amazon S3 and use AWS CloudTrail to capture audit trails.\nCustom RAG pipeline\n= HIGH operational overhead (tự manage OpenSearch indexing, etc.)\nCloudTrail = API audit, không phải response-level audit trail\n❌ Use Amazon CloudWatch to monitor latency and error rates. Embed model prompts directly in the application backend to cite sources. Store application interactions with users in Amazon RDS for audits.\nNo tracing/transparency mechanism\nRDS cho audit = kém scalable hơn cho 10,000 concurrent users\nKhông có RAG mechanism\n❌ Store generated responses and supporting evidence in an Amazon S3 bucket. Enable versioning on the bucket for audits. Use AWS Glue to catalog retrieved documents. Process the retrieved documents in Amazon Athena to generate periodic compliance reports.\nGlue + Athena = batch processing, không phải real-time audit trail\nKhông address transparency/citing sources\nKhông address 2-second response requirement\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nTransparent responses + cite sources\n→\nBedrock agent tracing\n+ structured prompts\nAudit trails\n→\nBedrock agent tracing\n(capture reasoning chain, không phải CloudTrail)\nScale + low latency\n→\nAPI Gateway + Lambda + CloudFront + Multi-AZ\nCustom RAG\n→ HIGH overhead |\nBedrock Knowledge Bases\n→ LEAST overhead\nCloudTrail\n= AWS API audit |\nBedrock tracing\n= AI response audit → KHÁC nhau"}, {"number": 36, "status": "Incorrect", "question": "A bank is developing a generative AI (GenAI)-powered AI assistant that uses Amazon Bedrock to assist the bank's website users with account inquiries and financial guidance. The bank must ensure that the AI assistant does not reveal any personally identifiable information (PII) in customer interactions.\nThe AI assistant must not send PII in prompts to the GenAI model. The AI assistant must not respond to customer requests to provide investment advice. The bank must collect audit logs of all customer interactions, including any images or documents that are transmitted during customer interactions.\nWhich solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational effort?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Use Amazon Macie to detect and redact PII in user inputs and in the model responses. Apply prompt engineering techniques to force the model to avoid investment advice topics. Use AWS CloudTrail to capture conversation logs.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Use an AWS Lambda function and Amazon Comprehend to detect and redact PII. Use Amazon Comprehend topic modeling to prevent the AI assistant from discussing investment advice topics. Set up custom metrics in Amazon CloudWatch to capture customer conversations.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Configure Amazon Bedrock guardrails to apply a sensitive information policy to detect and filter PII. Set up a topic policy to ensure that the AI assistant avoids investment advice topics. Use the Converse API to log model invocations. Enable delivery and image logging to Amazon S3.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Use regex controls to match patterns for PII. Apply prompt engineering techniques to avoid returning PII or investment advice topics to customers. Enable model invocation logging, delivery logging, and image logging to Amazon S3.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["C"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nBank\n, GenAI assistant dùng\nAmazon Bedrock\n, website users\n3 yêu cầu cụ thể:\nAI KHÔNG reveal\nPII\ntrong responses\nAI KHÔNG send\nPII trong prompts\nđến GenAI model\nAI KHÔNG respond to\ninvestment advice requests\nAudit logs\ncủa tất cả interactions (bao gồm\nimages và documents\n)\nLEAST operational effort\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nConfigure Amazon Bedrock guardrails to apply a sensitive information policy to detect and filter PII. Set up a topic policy to ensure that the AI assistant avoids investment advice topics. Use the Converse API to log model invocations. Enable delivery and image logging to Amazon S3.\nBedrock Guardrails sensitive information policy\n→ detect & filter PII trong cả input (prompts) VÀ output (responses)\nTopic policy\n→ block investment advice topics (native Guardrails feature)\nConverse API\n→ standard API cho multi-turn, hỗ trợ logging\nDelivery và image logging → S3\n→ capture tất cả interactions bao gồm images/documents\nTất cả native Bedrock features →\nLEAST operational effort\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Use Amazon Macie to detect and redact PII in user inputs and in the model responses. Apply prompt engineering techniques to force the model to avoid investment advice topics. Use AWS CloudTrail to capture conversation logs.\nMacie\n= phát hiện PII trong S3, KHÔNG phải real-time redaction trong conversation\nPrompt engineering\n= không reliable để enforce topic restrictions\nCloudTrail\n= API audit, KHÔNG capture conversation content/images\n❌ Use an AWS Lambda function and Amazon Comprehend to detect and redact PII. Use Amazon Comprehend topic modeling to prevent the AI assistant from discussing investment advice topics. Set up custom metrics in Amazon CloudWatch to capture customer conversations.\nLambda + Comprehend = CUSTOM pipeline → HIGH operational effort\nComprehend topic modeling không designed cho real-time conversation blocking\nCloudWatch metrics ≠ audit logs của conversations\n❌ Use regex controls to match patterns for PII. Apply prompt engineering techniques to avoid returning PII or investment advice topics to customers. Enable model invocation logging, delivery logging, and image logging to Amazon S3.\nRegex\n= fragile, không comprehensive cho PII detection\nPrompt engineering\n= không reliable enforcement\nLogging phần đúng nhưng detection mechanism kém\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nBlock PII trong input + output\n→\nBedrock Guardrails sensitive information policy\nBlock specific topics\n→\nBedrock Guardrails topic policy\nAudit logs bao gồm images/documents\n→\nBedrock model invocation logging + delivery logging + image logging → S3\nAmazon Macie\n→ S3 data scanning, KHÔNG phải real-time conversation PII filtering\nPrompt engineering\n→ NOT reliable cho compliance enforcement\nKhi thấy PII + topic restriction + logging trong Bedrock →\nGuardrails + native logging\n= answer"}, {"number": 37, "status": "Correct", "question": "A company is building a generative AI (GenAI) application that uses Amazon Bedrock APIs to process complex customer inquiries. During peak usage periods, the application experiences intermittent API timeouts that cause issues such as broken response chunks and delayed data delivery. The application struggles to ensure that prompts remain within token limits when handling complex customer inquiries of varying lengths. Users have reported truncated inputs and incomplete responses. The company has also observed foundation model (FM) invocation failures.\nThe company needs a retry strategy that automatically handles transient service errors and prevents overwhelming Amazon Bedrock during peak usage periods. The strategy must also adapt to changing service availability and support response streaming and token-aware request handling.\nWhich solution will meet these requirements?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Use the AWS SDK to configure a retry strategy in standard mode. Wrap Amazon Bedrock API calls in try-catch blocks that handle timeout exceptions. Return cached completions for failed streaming requests. Enforce a global token limit for all users. Add jitter-based retry logic and lightweight token trimming for each request. Resume broken streams by requesting only the missing chunks from the point of failure. Maintain a small in-memory buffer of the most recent chunks to minimize redundant data transfer.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Set Amazon Bedrock client request timeouts to 30 seconds. Implement client-side load shedding. Buffer partial results and stop new requests when the application performance begins to degrade. Set static token usage caps for all requests. Configure exponential backoff retries, dynamic chunk sizing, and context-aware token limits.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Implement an adaptive retry strategy that uses exponential backoff with jitter and a circuit breaker pattern that temporarily disables retries when error rates exceed a predefined threshold. Implement a streaming response handler that monitors for chunk delivery timeouts. Configure the handler to buffer successfully received chunks and intelligently resume streaming from the last received chunk when connections are re-established.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Implement a standard retry strategy that uses a 1-second fixed delay between attempts and a 3-retry maximum for all errors. Handle streaming response timeouts by restarting streams. Cap token usage for each session.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["C"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nGenAI app\ndùng Bedrock, xử lý\ncomplex customer inquiries\nPeak usage\n: intermittent API timeouts →\nbroken response chunks, delayed delivery\nPrompts cần\nstay within token limits\ncho varying-length inputs\nĐề bài có\n4 yêu cầu chính\n:\nAPI timeout / transient errors\nPeak usage, tránh làm quá tải Bedrock\nStreaming response bị đứt giữa chừng\nService availability thay đổi\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nImplement an adaptive retry strategy that uses exponential backoff with jitter and a circuit breaker pattern that temporarily disables retries when error rates exceed a predefined threshold. Implement a streaming response handler that monitors for chunk delivery timeouts. Configure the handler to buffer successfully received chunks and intelligently resume streaming from the last received chunk when connections are re-established.\n1. Pattern Exponential Backoff + Jitter\nThay vì retry cố định mỗi 1 giây:\nRequest → fail\n ↓\nretry 1 → wait 1s\nretry 2 → wait 2s\nretry 3 → wait 4s\nretry 4 → wait 8s\nThêm\njitter\nđể nhiều client không cùng retry tại một thời điểm:\nClient A → retry sau 2.3s\nClient B → retry sau 1.7s\nClient C → retry sau 2.8s\nĐiều này đặc biệt quan trọng trong\npeak usage\n, giúp tránh tình trạng:\nBedrock overloaded\n ↓\n1000 requests fail\n ↓\n1000 requests retry cùng lúc\n ↓\nBedrock càng overloaded\n ↓\nretry tiếp...\n2. Pattern Circuit Breaker\nKhi tỷ lệ lỗi vượt ngưỡng:\nNormal\n ↓\nErrors tăng\n ↓\nCircuit OPEN\n ↓\nTạm thời không retry\n ↓\nGiảm pressure lên Bedrock\n ↓\nService ổn định\n ↓\nCircuit HALF-OPEN\n ↓\nTest request\n ↓\nOK → CLOSE\nNó giải quyết trực tiếp yêu cầu:\n\"prevents overwhelming Amazon Bedrock during peak usage periods\"\n3. Streaming response\nĐề bài nói có: broken response chunks and delayed data delivery. Giải pháp đáp án\n: 'buffer successfully received chunks'\nVí dụ Bedrock trả về:\nChunk 1 ✓\nChunk 2 ✓\nChunk 3 ✓\nChunk 4 ✓\nChunk 5 ✗ timeout\nApplication giữ lại:\nChunk 1\nChunk 2\nChunk 3\nChunk 4\nSau khi connection được thiết lập lại, application có cơ chế tiếp tục xử lý từ trạng thái gần nhất thay vì mất toàn bộ response.\nLưu ý:\nĐây là logic application-level; không nên hiểu là Bedrock tự động cung cấp cơ chế \"resume từ chunk N\" cho mọi streaming API. Trong thực tế, việc resume cần được thiết kế dựa trên API/protocol và khả năng idempotency của application.\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Implement a standard retry strategy that uses a 1-second fixed delay between attempts and a 3-retry maximum for all errors. Handle streaming response timeouts by restarting streams. Cap token usage for each session.\nFixed delay\n→ thundering herd problem\nRestart entire stream\n→ inefficient, không resume từ last chunk\nSession token cap\n= blunt instrument, không token-aware\n❌ Use the AWS SDK to configure a retry strategy in standard mode. Wrap Amazon Bedrock API calls in try-catch blocks that handle timeout exceptions. Return cached completions for failed streaming requests. Enforce a global token limit for all users. Add jitter-based retry logic and lightweight token trimming for each request. Resume broken streams by requesting only the missing chunks from the point of failure. Maintain a small in-memory buffer of the most recent chunks to minimize redundant data transfer.\nCached completions\ncho streaming = không phù hợp (responses là dynamic)\nGlobal token limit\n= không per-request token-aware\n\"Requesting only missing chunks\" = không phải cách streaming works trong Bedrock\n❌ Set Amazon Bedrock client request timeouts to 30 seconds. Implement client-side load shedding. Buffer partial results and stop new requests when the application performance begins to degrade. Set static token usage caps for all requests. Configure exponential backoff retries, dynamic chunk sizing, and context-aware token limits.\nStatic token caps\n→ không adaptive\nLoad shedding\n= drop requests, không phải retry intelligently\nQuá nhiều custom mechanisms → complex\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nPrevent overwhelming service (thundering herd)\n→\nExponential backoff with jitter\nAdapt to changing availability\n→\nCircuit breaker pattern\n(open when error rate high)\nBroken streaming chunks\n→\nBuffer chunks + resume from last received chunk\nFixed delay retry\n→ thundering herd → KHÔNG dùng\nCircuit breaker\n= temporarily disable retries (khác với retry logic thông thường)"}, {"number": 38, "status": "Correct", "question": "A company is implementing a serverless inference API by using AWS Lambda. The API will dynamically invoke multiple AI models hosted on Amazon Bedrock. The company needs to design a solution that can switch between model providers without modifying or redeploying Lambda code in real time. The design must include safe rollout of configuration changes and validation and rollback capabilities.\nWhich solution will meet these requirements?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Store the active model provider in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store. Configure a Lambda function to read the parameter at runtime to determine which model to invoke.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Store the active model provider in AWS AppConfig. Configure a Lambda function to read the configuration at runtime to determine which model to invoke.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Store the active model provider in a JSON file hosted on Amazon S3. Use AWS AppConfig to reference the S3 file as a hosted configuration source. Configure a Lambda function to read the file through AppConfig at runtime to determine which model to invoke.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Configure an Amazon API Gateway REST API to route requests to separate Lambda functions. Hardcode each Lambda function to a specific model provider. Switch the integration target manually.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["B"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nServerless inference API\ndùng\nAWS Lambda\n, invoke multiple AI models trên\nAmazon Bedrock\nCần\nswitch between model providers\nmà\nKHÔNG modify hoặc redeploy Lambda code\nYêu cầu:\nsafe rollout\n,\nvalidation\n, và\nrollback capabilities\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nStore the active model provider in AWS AppConfig. Configure a Lambda function to read the configuration at runtime to determine which model to invoke.\nAWS AppConfig\n= configuration management với:\nSafe rollout\n(deployment strategies: linear, exponential)\nValidation\n(validators before deployment)\nRollback capabilities\n(automatic rollback nếu CloudWatch alarms trigger)\nLambda reads config at runtime → switch models\nwithout code changes\nAppConfig hỗ trợ feature flags và dynamic configuration → perfect fit\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Store the active model provider in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store. Configure a Lambda function to read the parameter at runtime to determine which model to invoke.\nParameter Store = simple config storage, KHÔNG có:\nSafe rollout strategies\nBuilt-in validation\nAutomatic rollback\nChỉ là key-value store, không có deployment management\n❌ Configure an Amazon API Gateway REST API to route requests to separate Lambda functions. Hardcode each Lambda function to a specific model provider. Switch the integration target manually.\nHardcode\n= vi phạm yêu cầu \"không modify Lambda code\"\nManual switch\n= không phải safe rollout/automated\n❌ Store the active model provider in a JSON file hosted on Amazon S3. Use AWS AppConfig to reference the S3 file as a hosted configuration source. Configure a Lambda function to read the file through AppConfig at runtime to determine which model to invoke.\nGần đúng nhưng phức tạp không cần thiết: S3 + AppConfig reference\nAppConfig có thể store configuration trực tiếp mà không cần S3 intermediary\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nSafe rollout + validation + rollback + no code change\n→\nAWS AppConfig\nAppConfig vs Parameter Store\n: AppConfig = deployment management | Parameter Store = simple config storage\nAppConfig features\n: deployment strategies, validators, automatic rollback → exact fit cho \"safe rollout\"\nHardcode trong Lambda\n→ phải redeploy → vi phạm requirement\nKhi thấy \"switch without redeploy + safe rollout + rollback\" →\nAppConfig\nluôn"}, {"number": 39, "status": "Incorrect", "question": "A hotel company wants to enhance a legacy Java-based property management system (PMS) by adding AI capabilities. The company wants to use Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases to provide staff with room availability information and hotel-specific details. The solution must maintain separate access controls for each hotel that the company manages. The solution must provide room availability information in near real time and must maintain consistent performance during peak usage periods.\nWhich solution will meet these requirements?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Deploy a single Amazon Bedrock knowledge base that contains combined data for all hotels. Configure AWS Lambda functions to synchronize data from each hotel's PMS database through direct API connections. Implement AWS CloudTrail logging with hotel-specific filters to audit access logs for each hotel's data.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Build a centralized Amazon Bedrock agent that uses multiple knowledge bases. Implement AWS IAM Identity Center with hotel-specific permission sets to control hotel staff data access.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Create an Amazon EventBridge rule for each hotel that is invoked by changes to the PMS database for each hotel. Configure the rule to send updates to a centralized Amazon Bedrock knowledge base in a management AWS account. Configure resource-based policies to enforce hotel-specific access controls for hotel staff.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Implement one Amazon Bedrock knowledge base for each hotel in a multi-account structure. Use direct data ingestion to provide real-time room availability information. Schedule regular synchronization for less critical information.", "is_correct": true}], "correct_answers": ["D"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nHotel company\n, legacy\nJava-based PMS\n, thêm AI capabilities\nDùng\nAmazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases\ncho room availability + hotel-specific details\nYêu cầu:\nSeparate access controls cho mỗi hotel\nNear real-time\nroom availability information\nConsistent performance during peak usage\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nImplement one Amazon Bedrock knowledge base for each hotel in a multi-account structure. Use direct data ingestion to provide real-time room availability information. Schedule regular synchronization for less critical information.\nOne KB per hotel\n→ separate access controls tự nhiên (per-KB IAM policies)\nMulti-account structure\n→ strongest isolation giữa hotels\nDirect data ingestion\n→ near real-time updates cho room availability\nScheduled sync\ncho less critical data → balance performance và cost\nConsistent performance: dedicated KB per hotel → không chia sẻ resources\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Deploy a single Amazon Bedrock knowledge base that contains combined data for all hotels. Configure AWS Lambda functions to synchronize data from each hotel's PMS database through direct API connections. Implement AWS CloudTrail logging with hotel-specific filters to audit access logs for each hotel's data.\nSingle KB cho tất cả hotels\n→ khó enforce separate access controls\nCloudTrail filters ≠ proper access controls\nSingle KB = potential data leakage giữa hotels\n❌ Create an Amazon EventBridge rule for each hotel that is invoked by changes to the PMS database for each hotel. Configure the rule to send updates to a centralized Amazon Bedrock knowledge base in a management AWS account. Configure resource-based policies to enforce hotel-specific access controls for hotel staff.\nCentralized KB\n→ tất cả hotels share một KB → weaker isolation\nResource-based policies = có thể complex để manage per-hotel\nEventBridge → Lambda → KB = near real-time nhưng thêm complexity\n❌ Build a centralized Amazon Bedrock agent that uses multiple knowledge bases. Implement AWS IAM Identity Center with hotel-specific permission sets to control hotel staff data access.\nCentralized agent = single point of management nhưng complex routing\nIAM Identity Center = identity federation, phù hợp cho user auth nhưng không phải KB isolation\nKhông address near real-time ingestion mechanism\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nSeparate access controls + isolation per entity\n→\nSeparate KB per entity + multi-account\nNear real-time data\n→\nDirect data ingestion\nvào KB (không phải scheduled only)\nConsistent performance\n→ dedicated resources per hotel (separate KBs) vs shared\nMulti-account\n→ strongest isolation boundary trong AWS\nSingle KB tất cả\n→ data isolation risk → KHÔNG phù hợp khi cần separate access controls"}, {"number": 40, "status": "Correct", "question": "A company uses an AI assistant application to summarize the company's website content and provide information to customers. The company plans to use Amazon Bedrock to give the application access to a foundation model (FM).\nThe company needs to deploy the AI assistant application to a development environment and a production environment. The solution must integrate the environments with the FM. The company wants to test the effectiveness of various FMs in each environment. The solution must provide product owners with the ability to easily switch between FMs for testing purposes in each environment.\nWhich solution will meet these requirements?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Create one AWS CDK application. Create multiple pipelines in AWS CodePipeline. Configure each pipeline to have its own settings for each FM. Configure the application to invoke the Amazon Bedrock FMs by using the aws_bedrock.ProvisionedModel.fromProvisionedModelArn() method.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Create one AWS CDK application. Configure the application to invoke the Amazon Bedrock FMs by using the aws_bedrock.FoundationModel.fromFoundationModelId() method. Create a pipeline in AWS CodePipeline pipeline that has a deployment stage for each environment that uses AWS CodeBuild deploy actions.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Create one AWS CDK application for the production environment. Configure the application to invoke the Amazon Bedrock FMs by using the aws_bedrock.ProvisionedModel.fromProvisionedModelArn() method. Create a pipeline in AWS CodePipeline. Configure the pipeline to deploy to the production environment by using an AWS CodeBuild deploy action. For the development environment, manually recreate the resources by referring to the production application code.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Create a separate AWS CDK application for each environment. Configure the applications to invoke the Amazon Bedrock FMs by using the aws_bedrock.FoundationModel.fromFoundationModelId() method. Create a separate pipeline in AWS CodePipeline for each environment.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["B"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nCompany dùng\nAmazon Bedrock\ncho AI assistant summarize website content\nDeploy vào\ndevelopment environment\nvà\nproduction environment\nYêu cầu:\nIntegrate environments với FM\nTest effectiveness của various FMs\ntrong mỗi environment\nProduct owners cần\neasily switch between FMs\nfor testing\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nCreate one AWS CDK application. Configure the application to invoke Amazon Bedrock FMs by using the\naws_bedrock.FoundationModel.fromFoundationModelId()\nmethod. Create a pipeline in AWS CodePipeline that has a deployment stage for each environment that uses AWS CodeBuild deploy actions.\nOne CDK application\n→ đơn giản, không duplicate code\nfromFoundationModelId()\nmethod\n→ reference FM bằng model ID, dễ switch bằng cách thay ID\nSingle pipeline với deployment stages per environment\n→ deploy cùng code lên dev và prod\nProduct owners switch FM bằng cách thay model ID → không cần redeploy toàn bộ\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Create one AWS CDK application. Create multiple pipelines in AWS CodePipeline. Configure each pipeline to have its own settings for each FM. Configure the application to invoke the Amazon Bedrock FMs by using the aws_bedrock.ProvisionedModel.fromProvisionedModelArn() method.\nMultiple pipelines per FM\n→ overkill, không cần thiết\nfromProvisionedModelArn()\n= cho provisioned throughput models (committed, fixed cost), không phải on-demand testing\nMỗi FM cần pipeline riêng → không \"easily switch\"\n❌ Create a separate AWS CDK application for each environment. Configure the applications to invoke the Amazon Bedrock FMs by using the aws_bedrock.FoundationModel.fromFoundationModelId() method. Create a separate pipeline in AWS CodePipeline for each environment.\nSeparate CDK apps\n→ code duplication, harder to maintain\nSeparate pipelines = khó sync changes giữa environments\nKhông efficiently support switching FMs\n❌ Create one AWS CDK application for the production environment. Configure the application to invoke the Amazon Bedrock FMs by using the aws_bedrock.ProvisionedModel.fromProvisionedModelArn() method. Create a pipeline in AWS CodePipeline. Configure the pipeline to deploy to the production environment by using an AWS CodeBuild deploy action. For the development environment, manually recreate the resources by referring to the production application code.\nManual recreation for dev\n= not automated, error-prone\nfromProvisionedModelArn()\n= provisioned models (không phải flexible FM testing)\nKhông đáp ứng yêu cầu \"easily switch between FMs\"\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nEasily switch FMs + testing\n→\nfromFoundationModelId()\n(flexible, on-demand)\nfromProvisionedModelArn()\n→ dành cho\nprovisioned throughput\n(fixed commitment, không phải flexible testing)\nOne CDK app + multi-stage pipeline\n→ best practice cho multi-environment deployment\nSeparate CDK apps per environment\n→ code duplication → harder to maintain\nfromFoundationModelId()\nvs\nfromProvisionedModelArn()\n: Foundation = on-demand flexible | Provisioned = committed throughput"}, {"number": 41, "status": "Incorrect", "question": "A healthcare company is using Amazon Bedrock to develop a real-time patient care AI assistant to respond to queries for separate departments that handle clinical inquiries, insurance verification, appointment scheduling, and insurance claims. The company wants to use a multi-agent architecture.\nThe company must ensure that the AI assistant is scalable and can onboard new features for patients. The AI assistant must be able to handle thousands of parallel patient interactions. The company must ensure that patients receive appropriate domain-specific responses to queries.\nWhich solution will meet these requirements?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Isolate data for each agent by using separate knowledge bases. Use IAM filtering to control access to each knowledge base. Deploy a supervisor agent to perform natural language intent classification on patient inquiries. Configure the supervisor agent to route queries to specialized collaborator agents to respond to department-specific queries. Configure each specialized collaborator agent to use Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) with the agent's department-specific knowledge base.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Create a separate supervisor agent for each department. Configure individual collaborator agents to perform natural language intent classification for each specialty domain within each department. Integrate each collaborator agent with department-specific knowledge bases only. Implement manual handoff processes between the supervisor agents.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Isolate data for each department in separate knowledge bases. Use IAM filtering to control access to each knowledge base. Deploy a single general-purpose agent. Configure multiple action groups within the general-purpose agent to perform specific department functions. Implement rule-based routing logic within the general-purpose agent instructions.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Implement multiple independent supervisor agents that run in parallel to respond to patient inquiries for each department. Configure multiple collaborator agents for each supervisor agent. Integrate all agents with the same knowledge base. Use external routing logic to merge responses from multiple supervisor agents.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["A"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nHealthcare company\n, Amazon Bedrock,\nmulti-agent architecture\n4 departments: clinical inquiries, insurance verification, appointment scheduling, insurance claims\nYêu cầu:\nScalable\n, onboard new features easily\nHandle\nthousands of parallel patient interactions\nDomain-specific responses\ncho từng department\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nIsolate data for each agent by using separate knowledge bases. Use IAM filtering to control access to each knowledge base. Deploy a supervisor agent to perform natural language intent classification on patient inquiries. Configure the supervisor agent to route queries to specialized collaborator agents to respond to department-specific queries. Configure each specialized collaborator agent to use Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) with the agent's department-specific knowledge base.\nSupervisor + collaborator agents\n= đúng multi-agent architecture trong Amazon Bedrock\nSupervisor\nclassify intent → route đến đúng department agent\nSeparate KBs per department\n→ domain-specific responses + data isolation\nIAM filtering\n→ access control per KB\nScalable\n: thêm department = thêm collaborator agent mới dễ dàng\nBedrock native multi-agent support → handle parallel interactions\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Create a separate supervisor agent for each department. Configure individual collaborator agents to perform natural language intent classification for each specialty domain within each department. Integrate each collaborator agent with department-specific knowledge bases only. Implement manual handoff processes between the supervisor agents.\nMultiple supervisors + manual handoff\n= NOT scalable, không handle parallel interactions tốt\nManual handoff = latency, không automated\n❌ Isolate data for each department in separate knowledge bases. Use IAM filtering to control access to each knowledge base. Deploy a single general-purpose agent. Configure multiple action groups within the general-purpose agent to perform specific department functions. Implement rule-based routing logic within the general-purpose agent instructions.\nSingle agent với rule-based routing\n≠ multi-agent architecture (đề yêu cầu multi-agent)\nRule-based logic = brittle, không scalable\n❌ Implement multiple independent supervisor agents that run in parallel to respond to patient inquiries for each department. Configure multiple collaborator agents for each supervisor agent. Integrate all agents with the same knowledge base. Use external routing logic to merge responses from multiple supervisor agents.\nSame knowledge base\n→ không phân biệt domain-specific knowledge\nExternal routing logic = custom complexity, not native Bedrock\nMerge responses từ multiple supervisors = không phù hợp\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nMulti-agent + domain-specific routing\n→\nSupervisor agent + Collaborator agents\n(Bedrock native)\nScalable multi-agent\n→ Supervisor classify intent → route → Collaborators (thêm collaborator = scale)\nSeparate data per agent\n→\nSeparate Knowledge Bases + IAM filtering\nRule-based routing\n→ brittle, NOT multi-agent pattern\nBedrock Multi-Agent pattern\n: 1 Supervisor orchestrates N Collaborators, mỗi Collaborator có KB riêng"}, {"number": 42, "status": "Correct", "question": "A financial technology company is using Amazon Bedrock to build an assessment system for the company's customer service AI assistant. The AI assistant must provide financial recommendations that are factually accurate, compliant with financial regulations, and conversationally appropriate. The company needs to combine automated quality evaluations at scale with targeted human reviews of critical interactions.\nWhat solution will meet these requirements?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Configure a pipeline in which financial experts manually score all responses for accuracy, compliance, and conversational quality. Use Amazon SageMaker notebooks to analyze results to identify improvement areas.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Configure Amazon Bedrock evaluations that use Anthropic Claude Sonnet as a judge model to assess response accuracy and appropriateness. Configure custom Amazon Bedrock guardrails to check responses for compliance with financial policies. Add Amazon Augmented AI (Amazon A2I) human reviews for flagged critical interactions.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Configure Amazon CloudWatch to monitor response patterns from the AI assistant. Configure CloudWatch alerts for potential compliance violations. Establish a team of human evaluators to review flagged interactions.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Create an Amazon Lex bot to manage the customer service interactions. Configure AWS Lambda functions to check responses against a static compliance database. Configure intents in the bot that call the Lambda functions to check the responses. Add an additional intent to collect end-user reviews.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["B"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nFintech company\n, assessment system cho\ncustomer service AI assistant\nAI phải:\nfactually accurate\n,\ncompliant with financial regulations\n,\nconversationally appropriate\nCần:\nautomated quality evaluations at scale\n+\ntargeted human reviews\ncho critical interactions\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nConfigure Amazon Bedrock evaluations that use Anthropic Claude Sonnet as a judge model to assess response accuracy and appropriateness. Configure custom Amazon Bedrock guardrails to check responses for compliance with financial policies. Add Amazon Augmented AI (Amazon A2I) human reviews for flagged critical interactions.\nBedrock evaluations + LLM-as-a-judge (Claude Sonnet)\n→ automated quality evaluation at scale\nCustom Bedrock guardrails\n→ compliance với financial regulations (topic policies, content filters)\nAmazon A2I\n= AWS native service cho\nhuman-in-the-loop\nreviews → targeted human review của critical cases\nKết hợp automated + human review = đáp ứng đầy đủ yêu cầu\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Configure a pipeline in which financial experts manually score all responses for accuracy, compliance, and conversational quality. Use Amazon SageMaker notebooks to analyze results to identify improvement areas.\nManually score ALL\n= không scalable\nKhông có automated quality evaluation\nSageMaker notebooks = ad-hoc analysis, không systematic\n❌ Create an Amazon Lex bot to manage the customer service interactions. Configure AWS Lambda functions to check responses against a static compliance database. Configure intents in the bot that call the Lambda functions to check the responses. Add an additional intent to collect end-user reviews.\nLex bot = chatbot interface, không phải evaluation system\nStatic compliance database\n= không update được với changing regulations\nEnd-user reviews\n≠ targeted human review of critical interactions\n❌ Configure Amazon CloudWatch to monitor response patterns from the AI assistant. Configure CloudWatch alerts for potential compliance violations. Establish a team of human evaluators to review flagged interactions.\nCloudWatch = metrics/logs monitoring, KHÔNG phải content evaluation\nManual human team without structured A2I workflow = không scalable\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nAutomated evaluation at scale\n→\nBedrock Model Evaluation + LLM-as-a-judge\nHuman review cho critical cases\n→\nAmazon A2I (Augmented AI)\n= AWS native HITL\nCompliance với policies\n→\nBedrock Guardrails\n(topic + content policies)\nA2I\n= structured human review workflow với thresholds, routing → perfect cho \"targeted human reviews\"\nCloudWatch\n= metrics monitoring, KHÔNG phải content quality evaluation"}, {"number": 43, "status": "Correct", "question": "A company is creating a workflow to review customer-facing communications before the company sends the communications. The company uses a pre-defined message template to generate the communications and stores the communications in an Amazon S3 bucket. The workflow needs to capture a specific portion from the template and send it to an Amazon Bedrock model. The workflow must store model responses back to the original S3 bucket.\nWhich solution will meet these requirements?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Create an Amazon Bedrock agent that has an action group. Configure instructions to define how the agent should parse the communications. Configure the action group to retrieve the communications from the S3 bucket, invoke the Amazon Bedrock model, and store the model responses back to the S3 bucket.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Create an Amazon Bedrock agent that has a single action group. Configure three AWS Lambda functions in the action group. Configure the functions to retrieve the communications from the S3 bucket, parse the communications and invoke the Amazon Bedrock model, and store the model responses back to the S3 bucket.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Create an AWS Step Functions Express workflow state machine. Use an Amazon S3 integration GetObject step to retrieve the original communications. Use an intrinsic function Pass step to parse the communications and to pass the results to an Amazon Bedrock InvokeModel step. Configure an Amazon S3 integration PutObject step to store the model responses back to the S3 bucket.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Create a flow in Amazon Bedrock Flows. Configure S3 action nodes at the beginning and end of the flow to retrieve and store the communications and the model responses. In the middle of the flow, configure an expression to parse each communication. Configure an agent step to send the parsed input to the model for review.", "is_correct": true}], "correct_answers": ["D"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nCompany review\ncustomer-facing communications\ntrước khi gửi\nDùng\npre-defined message template\nlưu trong\nS3\nWorkflow cần:\nCapture specific portion\ntừ template\nSend to Bedrock model\nđể review\nStore model responses back\nto original S3 bucket\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nCreate a flow in Amazon Bedrock Flows. Configure S3 action nodes at the beginning and end of the flow to retrieve and store the communications and the model responses. In the middle of the flow, configure an expression to parse each communication. Configure an agent step to send the parsed input to the model for review.\nAmazon Bedrock Flows\n= visual workflow orchestration native trong Bedrock\nS3 action nodes\n→ native S3 read/write operations trong Flows\nExpression node\n→ parse/extract specific portion từ template\nAgent step\n→ invoke Bedrock model cho review\nToàn bộ native Bedrock Flows → LEAST operational overhead\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Create an AWS Step Functions Express workflow state machine. Use an Amazon S3 integration GetObject step to retrieve the original communications. Use an intrinsic function Pass step to parse the communications and to pass the results to an Amazon Bedrock InvokeModel step. Configure an Amazon S3 integration PutObject step to store the model responses back to the S3 bucket.\nStep Functions approach phức tạp hơn Bedrock Flows cho use case đơn giản này\nStep Functions Express = short-lived (max 5 min) nhưng vẫn thêm operational overhead\nBedrock Flows được designed specifically cho use case này\n❌ Create an Amazon Bedrock agent that has an action group. Configure instructions to define how the agent should parse the communications. Configure the action group to retrieve the communications from the S3 bucket, invoke the Amazon Bedrock model, and store the model responses back to the S3 bucket.\nBedrock Agent = conversational agent với memory/reasoning, overkill cho simple workflow\nAgent không phải optimal cho deterministic sequential processing workflow\n❌ Create an Amazon Bedrock agent that has a single action group. Configure three AWS Lambda functions in the action group. Configure the functions to retrieve the communications from the S3 bucket, parse the communications and invoke the Amazon Bedrock model, and store the model responses back to the S3 bucket.\n3 separate Lambda functions = unnecessary complexity\nLambda functions thêm operational overhead\nBedrock Flows với native nodes là simpler và more appropriate\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nSequential workflow: S3 read → process → Bedrock invoke → S3 write\n→\nAmazon Bedrock Flows\nBedrock Flows nodes\n: S3 node, Expression node, Agent/Model node → deterministic workflow\nBedrock Flows\nvs\nBedrock Agent\n: Flows = deterministic pipeline | Agent = conversational/reasoning\nStep Functions\n= workflow orchestration nhưng Bedrock Flows is simpler cho Bedrock-centric workflows\nS3 action nodes\ntrong Bedrock Flows = native S3 integration (không cần Lambda)"}, {"number": 44, "status": "Incorrect", "question": "A company wants to create an annual rewards program for its customers. The rewards that customers earn vary based on different parameters such as the categories of the items ordered and the customers' purchase history.\nThe company needs a generative AI (GenAI) solution that uses three Amazon Bedrock agents to help customers during online catalog browsing. The agents must use knowledge bases and action groups to handle the search, recommendation, and order modules. The modules must operate sequentially. An AWS Lambda function must calculate estimated rewards for each recommended item. The solution must provide graceful degradation during service disruptions.\nWhich solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Define an Amazon API Gateway REST API behind each agent. Create a second Lambda function to orchestrate the calls to the agents and the rewards Lambda function. Configure the second Lambda function with a retry/fallback mechanism.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Create an AWS Step Functions state machine with four tasks that run the agents and the rewards Lambda function. Set up retry and catch branches for each of the task steps.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Configure each agent with a separate retry/fallback mechanism. Create a second Lambda function to orchestrate the calls to the agents and the rewards Lambda function. Define an Amazon API Gateway REST API behind the second Lambda function.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Create a second Lambda function to orchestrate the calls to the agents and the rewards Lambda function. Create an AWS Step Functions state machine with one task that runs the second Lambda function. Set up retry and catch branches for the task step.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["B"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nAnnual rewards program\n, 3 Bedrock agents (search, recommendation, order modules)\nAgents dùng\nknowledge bases + action groups\nModules chạy\nsequentially\nLambda function\ntính toán estimated rewards\nCần\ngraceful degradation\nkhi service disruptions\nMOST operational efficiency\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nCreate an AWS Step Functions state machine with four tasks that run the agents and the rewards Lambda function. Set up retry and catch branches for each of the task steps.\nStep Functions state machine\n→ orchestrate sequential agents (search → recommendation → order → Lambda rewards)\n4 tasks\n= 3 agents + 1 Lambda function = exactly matching requirements\nRetry và catch branches PER TASK\n→ graceful degradation at each step (nếu một bước fail, có thể catch và handle)\nStep Functions\n= optimal cho sequential workflow orchestration\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Define an Amazon API Gateway REST API behind each agent. Create a second Lambda function to orchestrate the calls to the agents and the rewards Lambda function. Configure the second Lambda function with a retry/fallback mechanism.\nAPI Gateway behind each agent = unnecessary complexity\nCustom orchestration Lambda = MORE operational overhead vs Step Functions\nRetry/fallback trong Lambda code = fragile\n❌ Configure each agent with a separate retry/fallback mechanism. Create a second Lambda function to orchestrate the calls to the agents and the rewards Lambda function. Define an Amazon API Gateway REST API behind the second Lambda function.\nRetry per agent\n+ orchestration Lambda = redundant layers\nNOT MOST operational efficiency\n❌ Create a second Lambda function to orchestrate the calls to the agents and the rewards Lambda function. Create an AWS Step Functions state machine with one task that runs the second Lambda function. Set up retry and catch branches for the task step.\nOne task\nwrap everything trong Lambda = không granular retry/catch per step\nNếu Lambda fails, không biết step nào failed → kém graceful degradation\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nSequential agents + graceful degradation\n→\nStep Functions state machine\nvới\nretry và catch per task\nMOST operational efficiency\n→ Step Functions managed orchestration (không phải custom Lambda orchestration)\nGraceful degradation\n→ catch branches trong Step Functions (khi một bước fail → fallback path)\n4 tasks trong Step Functions\n= 3 agents + 1 Lambda = exact mapping\nAPI Gateway behind each agent\n= overkill complexity, không operational efficient"}, {"number": 45, "status": "Skipped", "question": "A company uses AWS Lambda functions to build an AI agent solution. A GenAI developer must set up a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that accesses user information. The GenAI developer must also configure the AI agent to use the new MCP server. The GenAI developer must ensure that only authorized users can access the MCP server.\nWhich solution will meet these requirements?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Use a Lambda function to host the MCP server. Grant the AI agent Lambda functions permission to invoke the Lambda function that hosts the MCP server. Configure the AI agent's MCP client to invoke the MCP server asynchronously.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Use a Lambda function to host the MCP server. Grant the AI agent Lambda functions permission to invoke the Lambda function that hosts the MCP server. Configure the AI agent to use the STDIO transport with the MCP server.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Use a Lambda function to host the MCP server. Create an Amazon API Gateway HTTP API that proxies requests to the Lambda function. Configure the AI agent solution to use the Streamable HTTP transport to make requests through the HTTP API. Use Amazon Cognito to enforce OAuth 2.1.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Use a Lambda layer to host the MCP server. Add the Lambda layer to the AI agent Lambda functions. Configure the agentic AI solution to use the STDIO transport to send requests to the MCP server. In the AI agent's MCP configuration, specify the Lambda layer ARN as the command. Specify the user credentials as environment variables.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["C"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nAWS Lambda\nAI agent solution dùng\nModel Context Protocol (MCP) server\nMCP server cần\naccess user information\nAI agent cần\nconfigure và use MCP server\nYêu cầu: chỉ\nauthorized users\nmới được access MCP server\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nUse a Lambda function to host the MCP server. Create an Amazon API Gateway HTTP API that proxies requests to the Lambda function. Configure the AI agent solution to use the Streamable HTTP transport to make requests through the HTTP API. Use Amazon Cognito to enforce OAuth 2.1.\nLambda\nhost MCP server = serverless, scalable\nAPI Gateway HTTP API\n= expose MCP server securely\nStreamable HTTP transport\n= MCP standard transport cho remote servers (HTTP-based)\nAmazon Cognito + OAuth 2.1\n= proper authorization mechanism cho MCP (MCP spec yêu cầu OAuth 2.1 cho remote servers)\nĐáp ứng \"only authorized users\" requirement\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Use a Lambda function to host the MCP server. Grant the AI agent Lambda functions permission to invoke the Lambda function that hosts the MCP server. Configure the AI agent's MCP client to invoke the MCP server asynchronously.\nAsynchronous invocation\n= không phù hợp cho MCP (cần synchronous request-response)\nKhông có authorization mechanism\n❌ Use a Lambda function to host the MCP server. Grant the AI agent Lambda functions permission to invoke the Lambda function that hosts the MCP server. Configure the AI agent to use the STDIO transport with the MCP server.\nSTDIO transport\n= chỉ dùng cho\nlocal\nMCP servers (same process/machine)\nLambda-hosted MCP server là\nremote\n→ cần\nHTTP transport\n(không phải STDIO)\n❌ Use a Lambda layer to host the MCP server. Add the Lambda layer to the AI agent Lambda functions. Configure the agentic AI solution to use the STDIO transport to send requests to the MCP server. In the AI agent's MCP configuration, specify the Lambda layer ARN as the command. Specify the user credentials as environment variables.\nLambda layer\nkhông phải cách host MCP server (layer = code/library sharing)\nSTDIO transport\n= local only, không phù hợp\nCredentials trong environment variables\n= insecure, không phải proper auth\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nRemote MCP server\n→\nStreamable HTTP transport\n(không phải STDIO)\nSTDIO transport\n→ chỉ cho\nlocal/same-process\nMCP servers\nMCP authorization\n→\nOAuth 2.1\n(MCP specification requirement cho remote servers)\nAmazon Cognito\n= OAuth 2.1 provider trong AWS ecosystem\nLambda layer\n= shared code/dependencies, KHÔNG phải server hosting"}, {"number": 46, "status": "Skipped", "question": "A company uses Amazon Bedrock to develop an AI assistant to provide customer support. Analysis shows that 40% of customer queries use varied phrasing or wording to ask the same questions.\nThe company wants a solution to reduce redundant model calls. The solution must ensure that semantically equivalent questions receive consistent answers. The solution must ensure low latency.\nWhich solution will meet these requirements?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Create a caching solution by using Amazon DynamoDB to create a global secondary index on the normalized query text. Apply stemming to incoming queries. Query the index of cached customer queries.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Deploy Amazon OpenSearch Service that has k-nearest neighbor (k-NN) capabilities to store query-response text pairs. Use an approximate k-NN technique to find similar queries and their responses.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Use Amazon Bedrock to generate embeddings from customer queries. Use Amazon MemoryDB for Valkey to store hash sets of vector embeddings and model responses. Use a RANGE query to find similar queries and their responses.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Deploy an Amazon DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX) cluster as an in-memory cache. Specify the query text as the partition key and the model response text as the sort key. Query the cache by using a filter expression with the LIKE operator.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["C"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\n40% customer queries\ndùng\nvaried phrasing\nđể hỏi\ncâu hỏi giống nhau\nCần\nreduce redundant model calls\nSemantically equivalent questions\n→\nconsistent answers\nLow latency\nYêu cầu:\nhệ thống phải nhận ra và trả về\ncùng một câu trả lời đã cache\n, thay vì gọi lại model tốn kém.\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nUse Amazon Bedrock to generate embeddings from customer queries. Use Amazon MemoryDB for Valkey to store hash sets of vector embeddings and model responses. Use a RANGE query to find similar queries and their responses.\nGiảm redundant model calls\n: Query mới được embed thành vector, so sánh với các vector đã lưu — nếu tìm thấy vector \"đủ gần\" (trong ngưỡng similarity), trả thẳng response đã cache,\nkhông cần gọi lại Bedrock LLM\n→ tiết kiệm chi phí và số lần gọi model.\nSemantically equivalent questions → consistent answers\n: Dùng\nembeddings\n(không phải so khớp text/từ khóa) để đo độ tương đồng ngữ nghĩa — nên \"Làm sao reset mật khẩu?\" và \"Tôi quên đăng nhập rồi, sửa sao đây?\" vẫn được nhận diện là cùng ý dù từ ngữ hoàn toàn khác nhau.\nLow latency\n:\nMemoryDB for Valkey\nlà in-memory database (giống Redis) với độ trễ\ndưới mili-giây\n— lý tưởng cho tầng cache cần phản hồi cực nhanh, khác hẳn với việc phải chờ LLM sinh câu trả lời từ đầu.\nVề kỹ thuật\n\"RANGE query\"\n: trong vector similarity search có 2 kiểu truy vấn phổ biến —\nKNN\n(tìm k vector gần nhất, dù gần bao nhiêu cũng trả về) và\nRange query\n(chỉ trả về các vector nằm trong một\nngưỡng khoảng cách/similarity threshold\nnhất định). Với bài toán cache, Range query phù hợp hơn KNN: ta chỉ muốn tái sử dụng response khi câu hỏi\nthực sự đủ giống về ý nghĩa\n(trong ngưỡng cho phép), chứ không phải cứ lấy câu \"gần nhất\" dù có thể vẫn khác ý khá nhiều.\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Deploy an Amazon DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX) cluster as an in-memory cache. Specify the query text as the partition key and the model response text as the sort key. Query the cache by using a filter expression with the LIKE operator.\n(DAX + query text làm partition key + LIKE filter)\n→ DAX chỉ tăng tốc cho các truy vấn DynamoDB dựa trên\nexact key match\n; dùng nguyên văn câu hỏi làm partition key nghĩa là chỉ cache hit khi câu hỏi\ngiống hệt\nnhau. Toán tử\nLIKE\ncũng chỉ so khớp\nchuỗi con\n(substring), hoàn toàn không hiểu ngữ nghĩa → không giải quyết được vấn đề \"varied phrasing\" mà đề bài nêu (40% câu hỏi diễn đạt khác nhau).\n❌ Deploy Amazon OpenSearch Service that has k-nearest neighbor (k-NN) capabilities to store query-response text pairs. Use an approximate k-NN technique to find similar queries and their responses.\n(OpenSearch + k-NN)\n→ Về mặt kỹ thuật\ncó thể\nlàm được semantic search (OpenSearch hỗ trợ approximate k-NN cho vector), nhưng OpenSearch là\nsearch engine trên đĩa\n, độ trễ vốn dĩ cao hơn nhiều (thường hàng chục ms) so với in-memory store như MemoryDB.\nVới yêu cầu\n\"low latency\"\nđược nhấn mạnh riêng trong đề, MemoryDB phù hợp hơn cho vai trò\ncache layer\nthời gian thực.\n❌ Create a caching solution by using Amazon DynamoDB to create a global secondary index on the normalized query text. Apply stemming to incoming queries. Query the index of cached customer queries.\n(DynamoDB GSI + normalized text + stemming)\n→ Đây chỉ là so khớp\nvăn bản\n(dựa trên từ/cụm từ sau khi chuẩn hoá),\nkhông hiểu ngữ nghĩa\n.\nStemming chỉ xử lý được biến thể của cùng một từ (running/runs → run), nhưng không thể nhận ra 2 câu diễn đạt hoàn toàn khác nhau lại cùng một ý → thất bại ở yêu cầu \"semantically equivalent questions\".\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nSemantically equivalent queries + low latency cache\n→\nBedrock Embeddings + MemoryDB for Valkey\nLIKE operator / text matching\n→ keyword match, KHÔNG phải semantic similarity\nAmazon MemoryDB for Valkey\n= in-memory + vector search = optimal cho semantic caching\nSemantic caching pattern\n: query → embed → vector search in cache → hit? return cached | miss? call FM → store\nOpenSearch k-NN\n= vector search nhưng kém hơn in-memory MemoryDB về latency"}, {"number": 47, "status": "Skipped", "question": "A company is using Amazon Bedrock and Anthropic Claude 3 Haiku to develop an AI assistant. The AI assistant normally processes 10,000 requests each hour but experiences surges of up 30,000 requests each hour during peak usage periods. The AI assistant must respond within 2 seconds while operating across multiple AWS Regions.\nThe company observes that during peak usage periods, the AI assistant experiences throughput bottlenecks that cause increased latency and occasional request timeouts. The company must resolve the performance issues.\nWhich solution will meet this requirement?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Implement batch inference for all requests by using Amazon S3 buckets across multiple Regions. Use Amazon SQS to set up an asynchronous retrieval process.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Set up auto scaling AWS Lambda functions in each Region. Implement client-side round-robin request distribution. Purchase one model unit (MU) of provisioned throughput as a backup.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Implement token batching to reduce API overhead. Use cross-Region inference profiles to automatically distribute traffic across available Regions.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Purchase provisioned throughput and sufficient model units (MUs) in a single Region. Configure the application to retry failed requests with exponential backoff.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["C"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nAnthropic Claude 3 Haiku\ntrên Bedrock.\nĐề bài có các yêu cầu mấu chốt:\nTraffic tăng đột biến từ 10,000 → 30,000 req/giờ (surge 3x) trong peak\nPhải trả lời trong\n2 giây\n(real-time, không thể async)\nHoạt động\nacross multiple Regions\nVấn đề gốc:\nthroughput bottleneck\ngây tăng latency và timeout\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nImplement token batching to reduce API overhead. Use cross-Region inference profiles to automatically distribute traffic across available Regions.\nCross-Region inference profiles\nlà tính năng của Amazon Bedrock cho phép\ntự động phân phối traffic\nqua nhiều AWS Region (nơi model đã được deploy sẵn), tăng throughput khả dụng gộp lại của nhiều region thay vì bị giới hạn bởi quota/capacity của một region duy nhất. Đây chính là giải pháp trực tiếp cho vấn đề \"throughput bottleneck\" khi traffic surge — không cần công ty tự dựng logic load-balancing, Bedrock tự làm việc này.\nToken batching\ngiúp giảm số lượng API call/overhead bằng cách gộp nhiều request nhỏ lại (khi phù hợp), giảm tải lên hệ thống — bổ trợ thêm cho việc giảm bottleneck mà\nkhông phá vỡ yêu cầu phản hồi 2 giây\n(khác với batch inference kiểu offline).\nKết hợp cả hai: vừa giảm overhead xử lý, vừa tận dụng được throughput của nhiều Region cùng lúc — giải quyết đúng gốc rễ vấn đề \"throughput bottleneck\" mà vẫn giữ được tính real-time.\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Purchase provisioned throughput and sufficient model units (MUs) in a single Region. Configure the application to retry failed requests with exponential backoff.\n(Provisioned Throughput + nhiều MU trong 1 Region + retry với exponential backoff)\n→ Vấn đề là công ty cần hoạt động\nacross multiple Regions\n(đề bài nêu rõ), nhưng đáp án này chỉ dùng\n\"a single Region\"\n— không đáp ứng yêu cầu multi-region. Ngoài ra, \"retry với exponential backoff\" chỉ là cơ chế xử lý khi request thất bại (phòng ngừa), không phải giải pháp\nchủ động ngăn\nbottleneck xảy ra — không giải quyết được nguyên nhân gốc rễ của vấn đề.\n❌ Set up auto scaling AWS Lambda functions in each Region. Implement client-side round-robin request distribution. Purchase one model unit (MU) of provisioned throughput as a backup.\n(Lambda auto scaling + client-side round-robin + 1 MU backup)\n→ Vấn đề không nằm ở compute layer (Lambda) mà nằm ở\nthroughput của model Bedrock\n. Auto scaling Lambda không giải quyết được việc Bedrock model bị giới hạn throughput.\n\"Client-side round-robin\" là cách tự làm thủ công thứ mà Cross-Region inference profiles đã làm sẵn và tốt hơn (managed, tự động). \"One MU as backup\" cũng quá ít — không đủ để xử lý mức surge 3x (10K→30K).\n❌ Implement batch inference for all requests by using Amazon S3 buckets across multiple Regions. Use Amazon SQS to set up an asynchronous retrieval process.\n(Batch inference + S3 + SQS async)\n→\nVi phạm trực tiếp\nyêu cầu \"respond within 2 seconds\". Batch inference và xử lý bất đồng bộ qua SQS được thiết kế cho các workload\nkhông cần real-time\n(xử lý hàng loạt, có thể chờ lâu) — hoàn toàn không phù hợp với AI assistant cần phản hồi tức thời trong vài giây.\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nTraffic spikes + multiple Regions + low latency\n→\nCross-Region inference profiles\nReduce API overhead\n→\nToken batching\n(gộp requests khi có thể)\nCross-Region inference profiles\n→ auto-route đến Region có capacity → no throttling\nBatch inference (async)\n→ KHÔNG phù hợp khi cần real-time response < 2 seconds\nProvisioned throughput single Region\n→ không scale cross-region, fixed cost"}, {"number": 48, "status": "Skipped", "question": "A financial services company is developing a generative AI (GenAI) application that serves both premium customers and standard customers. The application uses AWS Lambda functions behind an Amazon API Gateway REST API to process requests. The company needs to dynamically switch between AI models based on which customer tier each user belongs to. The company also wants to perform A/B testing for new features without redeploying code. The company needs to validate model parameters like temperature and maximum token limits before applying changes.\nWhich solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Use AWS AppConfig to manage model configurations. Use feature flags to perform A/B testing. Define JSON schema validation rules for model parameters. Configure Lambda functions to retrieve configurations by using the AWS AppConfig Agent.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Store model configurations in Amazon DynamoDB tables. Optimize access patterns to retrieve configurations according to customer tier. Configure Lambda functions to query DynamoDB at the beginning of each request to determine which model to use.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Create an Amazon ElastiCache (Redis OSS) cluster to store model configurations. Set short TTL values. Run custom validation logic in Lambda functions. Use Amazon CloudWatch metrics to monitor configuration usage.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Create an AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store parameters for each configuration. Use Lambda functions to poll for parameter updates. Use Amazon EventBridge events to trigger redeployments when configurations change.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["A"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nFinancial services\n, GenAI app,\npremium + standard customers\nCần\ndynamically switch AI models\ndựa trên\ncustomer tier\nA/B testing\ncho new features\nwithout redeploying code\nValidate model parameters\n(temperature, max tokens)\nbefore applying changes\nLEAST operational overhead\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nUse AWS AppConfig to manage model configurations. Use feature flags to perform A/B testing. Define JSON schema validation rules for model parameters. Configure Lambda functions to retrieve configurations by using the AWS AppConfig Agent.\nAppConfig\n= dynamic configuration management without code redeployment\nFeature flags\n= A/B testing native feature của AppConfig\nJSON schema validation\n→ validate model parameters trước khi apply\nAppConfig Agent\n= local caching agent trong Lambda → low latency config retrieval\nAutomatic rollback\nnếu validation fails → LEAST operational overhead\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Create an AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store parameters for each configuration. Use Lambda functions to poll for parameter updates. Use Amazon EventBridge events to trigger redeployments when configurations change.\nRedeployments\nkhi config thay đổi → vi phạm \"without redeploying code\"\nParameter Store KHÔNG có validation rules, feature flags, hay A/B testing\n❌ Store model configurations in Amazon DynamoDB tables. Optimize access patterns to retrieve configurations according to customer tier. Configure Lambda functions to query DynamoDB at the beginning of each request to determine which model to use.\nDynamoDB KHÔNG có feature flags, A/B testing, hay parameter validation\nQuery DynamoDB mỗi request = thêm latency\nKhông có rollback capability\n❌ Create an Amazon ElastiCache (Redis OSS) cluster to store model configurations. Set short TTL values. Run custom validation logic in Lambda functions. Use Amazon CloudWatch metrics to monitor configuration usage.\nCustom validation logic\n= HIGH operational overhead\nElastiCache KHÔNG có feature flags, A/B testing\nShort TTL = potential stale config issues\nKhông có structured rollback\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nDynamic config + no redeploy + A/B testing + validation + rollback\n→\nAWS AppConfig\nFeature flags\n= AppConfig native → A/B testing built-in\nJSON schema validation\ntrong AppConfig → validate trước khi deploy config\nAppConfig Agent\n= local caching trong Lambda/EC2 → low latency\nParameter Store\n= simple config, NO feature flags/validation/A/B testing\nKhi thấy \"switch config without redeploy + A/B + validate\" →\nAppConfig\nlà answer"}, {"number": 49, "status": "Skipped", "question": "A GenAI developer is building a Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG)-based customer support application that uses Amazon Bedrock foundation models (FMs). The application needs to process 50 GB of historical customer conversations that are stored in an Amazon S3 bucket as JSON files. The application must use the processed data as its retrieval corpus. The application's data processing workflow must extract relevant data from customer support documents, remove customer personally identifiable information (PII), and generate embeddings for vector storage. The processing workflow must be cost-effective and must finish within 4 hours.\nWhich solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Use AWS Lambda and Amazon Comprehend to process files in parallel, remove PII, and call Amazon Bedrock APIs to generate vectors. Configure Lambda concurrency limits and memory settings to optimize throughput.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Create an AWS Glue ETL job to run PII detection scripts on the data. Use Amazon SageMaker Processing to run the HuggingFaceProcessor to generate embeddings by using a pre-trained model. Store the embeddings in Amazon OpenSearch Service.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Deploy an Amazon EMR cluster that runs Apache Spark with user-defined functions (UDFs) that call Amazon Comprehend to detect PII. Use Amazon Bedrock APIs to generate vectors. Store outputs in Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL with the pgvector extension.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Implement a data processing pipeline that uses AWS Step Functions to orchestrate a workload that uses Amazon Comprehend to detect PII and Amazon Bedrock to generate embeddings. Directly integrate the workflow with Amazon OpenSearch Serverless to store vectors and provide similarity search capabilities.", "is_correct": true}], "correct_answers": ["D"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nRAG-based customer support app\n,\n50 GB\nhistorical conversations trong\nS3 (JSON files)\nData processing workflow cần:\nExtract relevant data\ntừ support documents\nRemove PII\nGenerate embeddings\ncho vector storage\nCost-effective\n,\nfinish within 4 hours\nLEAST operational overhead\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nImplement a data processing pipeline that uses AWS Step Functions to orchestrate a workload that uses Amazon Comprehend to detect PII and Amazon Bedrock to generate embeddings. Directly integrate the workflow with Amazon OpenSearch Serverless to store vectors and provide similarity search capabilities.\nStep Functions\norchestrate the pipeline (serverless, managed)\nAmazon Comprehend\n→ detect và remove PII (managed NLP service)\nAmazon Bedrock\n→ generate embeddings (native, no model management)\nOpenSearch Serverless\n→ store vectors, similarity search, no cluster management\nTất cả serverless/managed →\nLEAST operational overhead\nStep Functions có built-in retry, timeout → handle 50GB within 4 hours\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Use AWS Lambda and Amazon Comprehend to process files in parallel, remove PII, and call Amazon Bedrock APIs to generate vectors. Configure Lambda concurrency limits and memory settings to optimize throughput.\nLambda = 15-minute timeout per invocation → không phù hợp cho large 50GB processing\nManually configure concurrency = operational overhead\nKhông có proper orchestration cho failure handling\n❌ Create an AWS Glue ETL job to run PII detection scripts on the data. Use Amazon SageMaker Processing to run the HuggingFaceProcessor to generate embeddings by using a pre-trained model. Store the embeddings in Amazon OpenSearch Service.\nSageMaker Processing = HIGH operational overhead (manage instances)\nHuggingFace model = phải manage model deployment\nOpenSearch Service (non-serverless) = manage clusters\n❌ Deploy an Amazon EMR cluster that runs Apache Spark with user-defined functions (UDFs) that call Amazon Comprehend to detect PII. Use Amazon Bedrock APIs to generate vectors. Store outputs in Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL with the pgvector extension.\nEMR cluster = VERY HIGH operational overhead\nAurora PostgreSQL cluster = thêm infra to manage\nSpark + UDFs = complex setup\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nLEAST overhead + 50GB batch processing\n→\nStep Functions + serverless services\nPII detection\n→\nAmazon Comprehend\n(managed, không phải custom model)\nEmbeddings\n→\nAmazon Bedrock\n(không phải SageMaker/HuggingFace)\nVector storage\n→\nOpenSearch Serverless\n(không phải managed OpenSearch/Aurora)\nLambda cho large batch\n→ 15-min timeout = KHÔNG phù hợp cho 50GB/4 hours\nEMR/SageMaker\n→ HIGH overhead → loại khi thấy \"LEAST operational overhead\""}, {"number": 50, "status": "Skipped", "question": "A financial services company is creating a Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) application that uses Amazon Bedrock to generate summaries of market activities. The application relies on a vector database that stores a small proprietary dataset that has a low index count. The application must perform similarity searches. The Amazon Bedrock model's responses must maximize accuracy and maintain high performance.\nThe company needs to configure the vector database and integrate it with the application.\nWhich solution will meet these requirements?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Launch an Amazon MemoryDB cluster and configure the index by using the Flat algorithm. Configure a horizontal scaling policy based on performance metrics.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Launch an Amazon MemoryDB cluster and configure the index by using the Hierarchical Navigable Small World (HNSW) algorithm. Configure a vertical policy based on performance metrics.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Launch an Amazon Aurora PostgresSQL cluster and configure the index by using the Inverted File with Flat Compression (IVFFlat) algorithm. Configure the instance class to scale to a larger size when the load increases.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Launch an Amazon DocumentDB cluster that has an Inverted File with Flat Compression (IVFFlat) index and a high probe value. Configure connections to the cluster as a replica set Distribute reads to replica instances.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["A"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nFinancial services\n, RAG application, Amazon Bedrock\nĐề bài có 3 điều kiện mấu chốt cần bám sát:\nDataset\nnhỏ, index count thấp\n(low index count)\nCần\ntối đa hoá độ chính xác\n(maximize accuracy)\nVẫn phải duy trì\nhiệu năng cao\n(high performance)\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nLaunch an Amazon MemoryDB cluster and configure the index by using the Flat algorithm. Configure a horizontal scaling policy based on performance metrics.\nVề thuật toán index — chọn Flat (exact search), không chọn ANN (HNSW/IVFFlat):\nCó 2 nhóm thuật toán similarity search:\nFlat (exact/brute-force k-NN)\n: so sánh vector query với\ntoàn bộ\nvector trong index, đảm bảo\n100% chính xác\n(tìm đúng k neighbor gần nhất tuyệt đối). Chi phí: O(n) — chậm nếu n (số lượng vector) lớn.\nANN (Approximate Nearest Neighbor)\nnhư HNSW, IVFFlat: xây dựng cấu trúc đồ thị/cụm để tìm kiếm nhanh hơn nhiều, nhưng\nđánh đổi độ chính xác\n— chỉ tìm được neighbor \"gần đúng\", có thể bỏ sót kết quả tốt nhất.\nVì dataset ở đây\nnhỏ và index count thấp\n, chi phí tính toán của Flat search là hoàn toàn chấp nhận được (không tốn kém vì n nhỏ), nên ta có thể chọn Flat để đạt\nđộ chính xác tuyệt đối\nmà không đánh đổi hiệu năng đáng kể — thoả cả 2 điều kiện \"accuracy\" và \"performance\" cùng lúc. Đây chính là trường hợp lý tưởng để dùng Flat thay vì ANN.\nVề việc chọn MemoryDB:\nAmazon MemoryDB (dựa trên Redis) là\nin-memory database\n, cho\nđộ trễ cực thấp (sub-millisecond)\n— phù hợp để bù lại phần \"chi phí\" của Flat search (vốn chậm hơn ANN về mặt lý thuyết), đảm bảo vẫn giữ được hiệu năng cao dù dùng thuật toán exact-search.\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Launch an Amazon MemoryDB cluster and configure the index by using the Hierarchical Navigable Small World (HNSW) algorithm. Configure a vertical policy based on performance metrics.\n(MemoryDB + HNSW + vertical scaling)\n→ HNSW cũng là thuật toán\nANN (approximate)\ndựa trên đồ thị phân lớp, đánh đổi accuracy lấy tốc độ — phù hợp cho dataset\nlớn\n(nơi Flat quá chậm), nhưng ở đây dataset nhỏ nên không cần đánh đổi này. Thêm nữa, \"vertical scaling\" (nâng cấp instance) có giới hạn và kém linh hoạt hơn \"horizontal scaling\" khi cần mở rộng theo tải.\n❌ Launch an Amazon Aurora PostgresSQL cluster and configure the index by using the Inverted File with Flat Compression (IVFFlat) algorithm. Configure the instance class to scale to a larger size when the load increases.\n(Aurora PostgreSQL + IVFFlat + scale instance lớn hơn)\n→ IVFFlat là thuật toán\napproximate\n(dựa trên clustering + compression), nghĩa là hy sinh một phần accuracy để đổi lấy tốc độ —\nngược với yêu cầu \"maximize accuracy\"\ncủa đề bài. Ngoài ra Aurora là disk-based relational DB, độ trễ vốn dĩ cao hơn nhiều so với in-memory MemoryDB.\n❌ Launch an Amazon DocumentDB cluster that has an Inverted File with Flat Compression (IVFFlat) index and a high probe value. Configure connections to the cluster as a replica set Distribute reads to replica instances.\n(DocumentDB + IVFFlat + probe cao)\n→ cùng vấn đề với A: IVFFlat vẫn là approximate search, dù tăng \"probe value\" (số cụm được quét) có thể cải thiện độ chính xác phần nào nhưng vẫn không đạt được exact match như Flat. DocumentDB cũng không phải lựa chọn tối ưu về latency cho vector search so với MemoryDB.\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nSmall dataset + maximize accuracy\n→\nFlat algorithm\n(exact search, 100% accuracy)\nLarge dataset + high performance\n→\nHNSW\n(approximate, fast)\nIn-memory + low latency vector search\n→\nAmazon MemoryDB\nFlat vs HNSW vs IVFFlat\n: Flat = exact (best accuracy, slow for large) | HNSW = approximate (fast, slight accuracy loss) | IVFFlat = approximate (clustered)\nLow index count + maximize accuracy\n→ Flat algorithm không slow → perfect fit\nHorizontal scaling\n= scale out (add nodes) >\nVertical scaling\n= scale up (bigger instance)"}, {"number": 51, "status": "Skipped", "question": "A company wants to create an application to analyze fashion trends. The application must analyze videos and photos from public fashion shows to understand style elements and trends. The solution must store the extracted information and provide a dashboard that summarizes the fashion trends. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Use an Anthropic Claude model in Amazon Bedrock to analyze text descriptions from fashion show videos and photos. Use Stable Diffusion for image analysis. Store results in Amazon OpenSearch Service. Create a dashboard by using Amazon Managed Grafana with OpenSearch visualizations.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Use Amazon Rekognition Custom Labels to train a custom model for fashion trend analysis. Store results in Amazon DynamoDB. Create a dashboard using Amazon Managed Grafana with custom plugins for fashion trend analytics.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Use AWS Step Functions to process videos and photos from fashion shows by using Amazon Bedrock multimodal FMs. Store analysis results in Amazon S3. Use an Amazon QuickSight dashboard to visualize trends in the data.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Use Amazon EventBridge to trigger AWS Lambda functions that use Amazon QuickSight Q to analyze videos and photos from fashion shows. Store analysis results in Amazon S3. Deploy a QuickSight dashboard with ML-powered trend analysis.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["C"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nPhân tích\nvideo và ảnh (videos and photos)\ntừ fashion show\nLưu trữ\nthông tin trích xuất (extracted information)\n+ cung cấp\ndashboard tổng hợp xu hướng (dashboard)\nYêu cầu:\nLEAST operational overhead\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nUse AWS Step Functions to process videos and photos from fashion shows by using Amazon Bedrock multimodal FMs. Store analysis results in Amazon S3. Use an Amazon QuickSight dashboard to visualize trends in the data.\nBedrock\nmultimodal FM (multimodal foundation model)\nphân tích trực tiếp video/ảnh mà\nkhông cần train model (no custom training)\n.\nStep Functions orchestrate quy trình đơn giản, quản lý hoàn toàn (fully managed).\nKết hợp S3 lưu kết quả + QuickSight dashboard chuẩn là pattern ít vận hành nhất.\nĐáp ứng đúng yêu cầu \"LEAST operational overhead\" so với các lựa chọn cần huấn luyện model riêng.\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Use Amazon EventBridge to trigger AWS Lambda functions that use Amazon QuickSight Q to analyze videos and photos from fashion shows. Store analysis results in Amazon S3. Deploy a QuickSight dashboard with ML-powered trend analysis.\nQuickSight Q là công cụ\ntruy vấn ngôn ngữ tự nhiên (NLQ)\ncho BI, không phân tích trực tiếp video/ảnh.\nKhông phù hợp về mặt kỹ thuật để \"hiểu style elements\" từ ảnh/video.\nKhông tận dụng khả năng multimodal của Bedrock.\n❌ Use Amazon Rekognition Custom Labels to train a custom model for fashion trend analysis. Store results in Amazon DynamoDB. Create a dashboard using Amazon Managed Grafana with custom plugins for fashion trend analytics.\nCần\nhuấn luyện model tùy chỉnh (custom training)\n→ tốn nhiều effort vận hành.\nKhông phải giải pháp \"LEAST operational overhead\".\n❌ Use an Anthropic Claude model in Amazon Bedrock to analyze text descriptions from fashion show videos and photos. Use Stable Diffusion for image analysis. Store results in Amazon OpenSearch Service. Create a dashboard by using Amazon Managed Grafana with OpenSearch visualizations.\nStable Diffusion dùng để\ntạo ảnh (generate image)\n, không phải phân tích ảnh (analyze).\nKiến trúc phức tạp, sai mục đích sử dụng công cụ.\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nPhân tích trực tiếp video/ảnh + \"LEAST overhead\" →\nBedrock multimodal FM\n(không cần custom training)\nCần train model riêng (Rekognition Custom Labels, SageMaker JumpStart custom) → operational overhead CAO\nQuickSight Q → chỉ dùng cho NLQ trên dữ liệu BI, không phân tích ảnh/video\nStable Diffusion → sinh ảnh (generate), không phải phân tích ảnh (analyze)"}, {"number": 52, "status": "Skipped", "question": "A company is implementing AI governance policies. The policies require all FM interactions to be secured with guardrails. The company configures Amazon Bedrock guardrails. The company must ensure that all InvokeModel and Converse API calls to FMs apply the guardrails. Which solution will enforce guardrail compliance for the API calls in the MOST operationally efficient way?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Create an AWS Lambda function that validates and enforces guardrails before proxying requests to Amazon Bedrock. Use the Lambda function as the exclusive endpoint for all FM interactions.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Configure IAM policies for the InvokeModel and Converse API calls with both bedrock:Guardrailldentifier and bedrock: PromptRouterArn condition keys. Apply the policies to all IAM roles. Require prompt router validation before allowing access to Amazon Bedrock FMs.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Configure IAM policies for the InvokeModel and Converse API calls with the bedrock: Guardrailldentifier condition key. Apply the policies to all IAM roles that access the Amazon Bedrock FMs.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Store guardrail identifiers in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store. Create an AWS Lambda function that retrieves the guardrail identifier from Parameter Store each time before making calls to Amazon Bedrock FMs.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["C"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nĐảm bảo mọi\nlời gọi InvokeModel/Converse API\nđều áp dụng\nguardrails\nYêu cầu:\nMOST operationally efficient\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nConfigure IAM policies for the InvokeModel and Converse API calls with the bedrock: Guardrailldentifier condition key. Apply the policies to all IAM roles that access the Amazon Bedrock FMs.\nIAM condition key (bedrock:GuardrailIdentifier)\nlà tính năng\nnative của AWS\n, enforce trực tiếp ở tầng IAM, không cần code thêm.\nKhông cần build thêm hạ tầng (Lambda, proxy...) → operationally efficient nhất.\nÁp dụng cho tất cả IAM roles đảm bảo compliance toàn diện.\nĐây là cách chính thống AWS khuyến nghị để bắt buộc guardrail.\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Configure IAM policies for the InvokeModel and Converse API calls with both bedrock:Guardrailldentifier and bedrock: PromptRouterArn condition keys. Apply the policies to all IAM roles. Require prompt router validation before allowing access to Amazon Bedrock FMs.\nPromptRouterArn\nkhông liên quan đến việc enforce guardrail, đây là điều kiện thừa/gây nhiễu.\nThêm yêu cầu prompt router validation không cần thiết → tăng phức tạp không lý do.\n❌ Create an AWS Lambda function that validates and enforces guardrails before proxying requests to Amazon Bedrock. Use the Lambda function as the exclusive endpoint for all FM interactions.\nPhải tự xây dựng và duy trì\nLambda proxy layer (custom code)\n→ tăng operational overhead đáng kể.\nKhông tận dụng tính năng native của Bedrock/IAM.\n❌ Store guardrail identifiers in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store. Create an AWS Lambda function that retrieves the guardrail identifier from Parameter Store each time before making calls to Amazon Bedrock FMs.\nThêm bước gọi Parameter Store mỗi request → tăng độ trễ và độ phức tạp vận hành.\nKhông đảm bảo enforce bắt buộc (developer vẫn có thể quên gọi guardrail).\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nEnforce guardrail bắt buộc cho mọi API call →\nIAM condition key\nbedrock:GuardrailIdentifier\n\"MOST operationally efficient\" + có sẵn native feature → chọn IAM/native, tránh Lambda/custom proxy\nĐáp án có thêm điều kiện/dịch vụ không liên quan (PromptRouterArn) → thường là bẫy (distractor)"}, {"number": 53, "status": "Skipped", "question": "A GenAI developer deployed a fine-tuned LLM to an Amazon SageMaker AI endpoint. The GenAI developer used the default serving configuration for continuous batching with the AMI including the Deep Java Library (DJL). The model is being served on GPUbased Amazon EC2 instances, each with 8 GPUs. As the model scales to production, the GenAI developer discovers that many instances are needed to meet traffic demands. The GenAI developer wants to avoid increased costs from the overutilization. The GenAI developer analyzes logs. The GenAI developer discovers that the maximum I/O sequence length in real requests is 10 times smaller than what the model was originally configured to handle. Additionally, the current concurrency for each instance is low. Profiling shows that the model’s weights and activations can fit entirely within 4 GPUs.\nWhich combination of steps can the GenAI developer take to improve resource utilization? (Select TWO.)", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Reduce the model's maximum sequence length to provide a higher rolling batch size for each GPU.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Increase the number of SageMaker Al instances and spread requests more evenly to reduce the load for each instance.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Enable speculative decoding to reduce response latency for each request.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Use tensor parallelism with a degree of 4 to deploy two model replicas for each instance.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "E", "text": "Split the model across all 8 GPUs by using a tensor parallelism degree of 8 to improve memory efficiency.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["A", "D"], "explanation": "A.\nReduce the model's maximum sequence length to provide a higher rolling batch size for each GPU."}, {"number": 54, "status": "Skipped", "question": "A financial services company wants to develop a mobile app that will help users with account inquiries and general account information. The company has a large amount of email exchange data between customers and support staff to use as source material. The data is stored in an Amazon S3 bucket and contains personally identifiable information (PII) that should not appear in search results. Which solution will meet these requirements?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Use Amazon Kendra to enable enterprise search of the email data that is stored in Amazon S3. Integrate Amazon Kendra with an Amazon Bedrock FM. Use a system prompt to identify and remove PII during query processing.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Use Amazon Comprehend to detect and redact PII from the email data that is stored in Amazon S3. Integrate Amazon Comprehend with Amazon Kendra to enable enterprise search of the processed data.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Use Amazon Textract to extract text from the email data. Use Amazon Macie to scan for Pll in Amazon S3. Integrate Amazon Textract and Amazon S3 with Amazon Kendra to enable enterprise search of the processed data.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Use Amazon Comprehend to detect and redact PII from the email data that is stored in Amazon S3. Integrate Amazon Comprehend with Amazon DocumentDB to enable database queries for enterprise search.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["B"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nEmail data lưu trong\nS3\n, chứa\nPII\nPII\nkhông được xuất hiện trong kết quả tìm kiếm (should not appear in search results)\nCần giải pháp cho mobile app hỏi đáp tài khoản\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nUse Amazon Comprehend to detect and redact PII from the email data that is stored in Amazon S3. Integrate Amazon Comprehend with Amazon Kendra to enable enterprise search of the processed data.\nAmazon Comprehend\nlà dịch vụ chuyên biệt để\nphát hiện và redact PII (detect and redact PII)\nmột cách xác định (deterministic), đáng tin cậy.\nDữ liệu đã redact PII trước khi index → đảm bảo PII\nkhông bao giờ xuất hiện\ntrong kết quả tìm kiếm.\nKendra\nlà dịch vụ\nenterprise search\nphù hợp cho use case tìm kiếm tài liệu email.\nĐây là kiến trúc tách biệt rõ ràng: redact trước, search sau — đúng best practice.\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Use Amazon Kendra to enable enterprise search of the email data that is stored in Amazon S3. Integrate Amazon Kendra with an Amazon Bedrock FM. Use a system prompt to identify and remove PII during query processing.\nXử lý PII qua\nsystem prompt\nkhông đáng tin cậy (non-deterministic), FM có thể bỏ sót.\nPII vẫn được\nindex\nvào Kendra trước, rủi ro rò rỉ cao hơn.\n❌ Use Amazon Textract to extract text from the email data. Use Amazon Macie to scan for Pll in Amazon S3. Integrate Amazon Textract and Amazon S3 with Amazon Kendra to enable enterprise search of the processed data.\nMacie chỉ phát hiện (detect)\n, không\nredact\nPII → PII vẫn còn trong dữ liệu index.\nTextract dùng để trích xuất text từ ảnh/scan, không cần thiết vì email đã là text.\n❌ Use Amazon Comprehend to detect and redact PII from the email data that is stored in Amazon S3. Integrate Amazon Comprehend with Amazon DocumentDB to enable database queries for enterprise search.\nDocumentDB\nlà NoSQL database cho query có cấu trúc, không phải\nenterprise search engine\nnhư Kendra.\nKhông đáp ứng nhu cầu \"enterprise search\" hiệu quả.\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nPhát hiện + xóa PII (detect and redact) →\nAmazon Comprehend\nChỉ phát hiện PII, không xử lý →\nAmazon Macie\n(không đủ nếu cần redact)\nEnterprise search trên tài liệu phi cấu trúc →\nAmazon Kendra\nXử lý PII bằng prompt/FM → không đáng tin cậy, tránh chọn khi có giải pháp dịch vụ chuyên biệt"}, {"number": 55, "status": "Skipped", "question": "A financial services company operates RAG for an application that answers user questions by using internal market analysis reports. The application uses Amazon Bedrock for the embedding model. The application uses an Amazon OpenSearch Service cluster as the vector store. An AWS Lambda function performs the embedding and search logic. After a recent code update to the Lambda function, the application starts returning generic responses. For example, the application returns “no relevant information found” even for questions that previously returned accurate answers. Amazon CloudWatch Logs shows no errors. AWS X-Ray confirms successful FM invocation. The OpenSearch Service cluster is healthy. Query latency remains normal. What is the cause of this issue?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "The updated Lambda function uses a different version of the embedding model.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "B", "text": "The Amazon Bedrock FM temperature parameter was increased.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "The Lambda function's IAM role is missing the permission for bedrock:InvokeModel.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "The document embeddings in OpenSearch Service were deleted during the application update and have not been re-indexed.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["A"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nRAG dùng Bedrock +\nOpenSearch (vector store)\n, Lambda thực hiện\nembedding và search\nSau khi\nupdate code Lambda\n, app trả\n\"no relevant information found\"\nKhông có lỗi CloudWatch\n,\nX-Ray xác nhận FM invocation thành công\n, cluster khỏe mạnh, latency bình thường\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nThe updated Lambda function uses a different version of the embedding model.\nBản chất của RAG là\nso khớp vector\n: câu hỏi được embed thành vector, rồi so sánh (cosine similarity) với các vector tài liệu đã lưu sẵn trong OpenSearch. Điều kiện tiên quyết để so khớp có ý nghĩa là\nvector câu hỏi và vector tài liệu phải cùng nằm trong một không gian embedding\n— tức phải được tạo ra từ cùng một model.\nKhi Lambda được update code và (vô tình) đổi sang\nversion embedding model khác\n(ví dụ Titan Embeddings G1 → Titan Text Embeddings V2, hoặc đổi dimension 1536 → 1024...), vector của câu hỏi mới sẽ nằm ở một không gian toán học hoàn toàn khác so với vector tài liệu cũ đã index trong OpenSearch. Kết quả:\nSimilarity score giữa query vector và mọi document vector đều rất thấp/vô nghĩa\nApp không tìm thấy tài liệu nào \"đủ gần\" → trả về \"no relevant information found\"\nNhưng về mặt kỹ thuật\nmọi thứ vẫn chạy đúng, không có lỗi\n: Lambda invoke thành công, FM invoke thành công (X-Ray xác nhận), OpenSearch khỏe mạnh, latency bình thường — vì bản chất đây là\nlỗi logic/semantic, không phải lỗi hệ thống\n.\nĐây khớp hoàn hảo với mọi triệu chứng đề bài mô tả: không có CloudWatch error, FM invoke thành công, cluster khỏe, latency bình thường.\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ The document embeddings in OpenSearch Service were deleted during the application update and have not been re-indexed.\nNếu embeddings bị xóa,\nOpenSearch cluster health\ncó thể vẫn \"healthy\" nhưng đây là thay đổi ở\ndata layer\n, không phải do\nLambda code update\nnhư đề nêu.\nĐề bài chỉ rõ nguyên nhân liên quan đến việc\ncập nhật code Lambda\n, không phải data bị xóa.\n❌ The Lambda function's IAM role is missing the permission for bedrock:InvokeModel.\nBị loại trực tiếp vì đề đã nói rõ\n\"X-Ray confirms successful FM invocation\"\n→ chứng minh quyền IAM vẫn OK.\n❌ The Amazon Bedrock FM temperature parameter was increased.\nTemperature ảnh hưởng đến\nđộ đa dạng của câu trả lời sinh ra (generation)\n, không ảnh hưởng đến\nretrieval\n(tìm tài liệu liên quan) — sai bản chất vấn đề.\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nRAG trả \"no relevant info\" dù mọi thứ \"khỏe mạnh\" sau code update →\nembedding model version mismatch\nX-Ray confirm FM invocation thành công → loại bỏ nguyên nhân IAM/permission\nVấn đề retrieval (không tìm thấy) ≠ vấn đề generation (temperature, sinh câu trả lời)\nSilent RAG failure không lỗi rõ ràng → luôn nghĩ đến\nvector space mismatch"}, {"number": 56, "status": "Skipped", "question": "A company is developing a RAG application by using Amazon Bedrock. The application processes customer support documents. Initially, the application retrieves many relevant documents. However, users report that the most relevant information often appears lower in the results. The company wants to improve the relevance ranking of retrieved results to ensure that the most useful information appears first. Which combination of steps will improve the relevance of retrieved results with MINIMAL operational overhead? (Select TWO.)", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Use Knowledge Bases with hybrid search capabilities and Amazon OpenSearch Serverless to combine vector embeddings with keyword matching.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Create an Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL database with the pgvector extension to store document embeddings. Create a similarity scoring algorithm that combines vector distances with document metadata to rank results.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Use Amazon Bedrock reranker models with Amazon OpenSearch Service to reorder retrieved results based on semantic relevance to the query.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Configure Amazon OpenSearch Serverless with the Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases plugin. Use OpenSearch's Learning to Rank feature for relevance scoring. Integrate relevance scoring with Knowledge Bases for result reranking.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "E", "text": "Use Amazon SageMaker JumpStart FMs with Amazon Kendra Intelligent Ranking to create custom relevancy scoring algorithms.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["A", "C"], "explanation": "A.\nUse Knowledge Bases with hybrid search capabilities and Amazon OpenSearch Serverless to combine vector embeddings with keyword matching."}, {"number": 57, "status": "Skipped", "question": "A financial services company needs to use Amazon Bedrock to create an AI assistant that will help customer support representatives across multiple business units. A GenAI developer must ensure that prompt templates are properly governed through approval workflows. Additionally, the company requires comprehensive logging of all model invocations with a 7-year retention period for regulatory compliance. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements with MINIMAL operational overhead? (Select TWO.)", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Use Amazon Bedrock Prompt Management with multi-stage approval workflows. Use IAM policies that require multi-party authorization.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Store prompt templates in Amazon DynamoDB tables with composite keys partitioned by business units. Implement IAM policies that grant role-based access to business units for template approval. Use DynamoDB item-level permissions to control prompt template modifications and approvals.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Set up Amazon EventBridge rules to capture Amazon Bedrock model invocation events. Route events to Amazon CloudWatch Logs groups that are organized by business unit. Export the logs to Amazon S3. Enable S3 Object Lock with compliance retention mode set to 7 years.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Enable Amazon Bedrock model invocation logging with Amazon S3 as the destination. Enable S3 Object Lock with compliance retention mode set to 7 years. Create separate prefixes for each business unit.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "E", "text": "Enable AWS CloudTrail data events for all Amazon Bedrock APIs. Deliver the logs to CloudTrail Lake with a 7-year retention setting. Tag each event with the business unit ID. Run CloudTrail Lake queries to monitor prompt activity.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["A", "D"], "explanation": "A.\nUse Amazon Bedrock Prompt Management with multi-stage approval workflows. Use IAM policies that require multi-party authorization."}, {"number": 58, "status": "Skipped", "question": "A GenAI developer is implementing a solution to create images from text descriptions. The GenAI developer successfully tested a pre-trained Hugging Face model by using Amazon SageMaker JumpStart. Now, the GenAI developer needs to deploy the model so that users can generate images on demand. The solution must use GPUs for inference. The solution must be able to handle text datasets up to 50 MB with image descriptions. The solution requires responses within 15 minutes. Which deployment strategy will meet these requirements?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Deploy a SageMaker Real-Time Inference endpoint that uses an accelerated computing SageMaker Al instance type. Create an AWS Lambda function for ondemand invocation of the SageMaker Al endpoint to manage image generation.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Deploy a SageMaker Asynchronous Inference endpoint that uses an accelerated computing SageMaker Al instance type. Create an AWS Lambda function for ondemand invocation of the SageMaker Al endpoint to manage image generation.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Deploy a SageMaker Serverless Inference endpoint that uses a general purpose SageMaker Al instance type. Create an AWS Lambda function for on-demand invocation of the SageMaker Al endpoint to manage image generation.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Create a SageMaker Al batch transform job that uses an accelerated computing SageMaker Al instance type to manage image generation. Create an AWS Lambda function to start the batch transform job.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["B"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nModel Hugging Face từ SageMaker JumpStart, sinh ảnh từ text\nCần\nGPU\n, input\nlên đến 50MB (up to 50MB)\n, response trong\n15 phút (within 15 minutes)\nNgười dùng generate\non-demand\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nDeploy a SageMaker Asynchronous Inference endpoint that uses an accelerated computing SageMaker Al instance type. Create an AWS Lambda function for ondemand invocation of the SageMaker Al endpoint to manage image generation.\nAsynchronous Inference\nhỗ trợ\npayload lớn (lên đến 1GB)\nvà\nthời gian xử lý dài (lên đến 15 phút+)\n, phù hợp với yêu cầu 50MB và 15 phút.\nHỗ trợ đầy đủ\nGPU instance types (accelerated computing)\n.\nVẫn cho phép invocation\non-demand\nqua queue, phù hợp mô hình sử dụng theo yêu cầu người dùng.\nĐây là lựa chọn duy nhất đáp ứng đồng thời cả 3 điều kiện: GPU, payload lớn, xử lý lâu.\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Deploy a SageMaker Serverless Inference endpoint that uses a general purpose SageMaker Al instance type. Create an AWS Lambda function for on-demand invocation of the SageMaker Al endpoint to manage image generation.\nServerless Inference không hỗ trợ GPU\n(chỉ CPU) → không đáp ứng yêu cầu bắt buộc dùng GPU.\nGiới hạn payload và timeout cũng nhỏ hơn nhiều so với yêu cầu.\n❌ Deploy a SageMaker Real-Time Inference endpoint that uses an accelerated computing SageMaker Al instance type. Create an AWS Lambda function for ondemand invocation of the SageMaker Al endpoint to manage image generation.\nReal-Time endpoint giới hạn\npayload nhỏ và timeout ngắn\n(tối đa ~60 giây), không đáp ứng \"response trong 15 phút\" và payload 50MB.\n❌ Create a SageMaker Al batch transform job that uses an accelerated computing SageMaker Al instance type to manage image generation. Create an AWS Lambda function to start the batch transform job.\nBatch Transform dùng cho xử lý\nhàng loạt offline\n, không phù hợp với yêu cầu \"on-demand\" theo từng request của user.\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nPayload lớn (>MB) + thời gian xử lý dài (phút) + on-demand →\nSageMaker Asynchronous Inference\nCần GPU nhưng thấy \"Serverless Inference\" → loại ngay (Serverless không hỗ trợ GPU)\nResponse nhanh, payload nhỏ → Real-Time Inference\nXử lý hàng loạt, không cần phản hồi ngay → Batch Transform"}, {"number": 59, "status": "Skipped", "question": "A financial services company is developing a research agent that processes complex financial data queries. The company must deploy existing Python agent code to Amazon Bedrock AgentCore Runtime. The company wants to reduce infrastructure management overhead and operational complexity. The agent must be able to handle quick data lookups that require sub-second responses. The agent must be able to handle comprehensive research report generation. For example, streaming responses over several minutes. The solution must automatically manage HTTP server configuration, endpoint routing, and health monitoring. Which deployment approaches will meet these requirements with MINIMAL operational overhead? (Select TWO.)", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Deploy the agent on Amazon ECS on AWS Fargate by using a custom container image that runs the AgentCore SDK application.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Implement the AgentCore SDK with the @app.entrypoint decorator to automatically handle server setup and endpoint management.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Implement a FastAPI server with a configuration of /invocations and /ping endpoints and container orchestration.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Deploy the agent by using the AgentCore starter toolkit for automated packaging, containerization, and deployment workflows.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "E", "text": "Deploy the agent on Amazon SageMaker Al real-time endpoints by using a custom inference container", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["B", "D"], "explanation": "A.\nDeploy the agent on Amazon ECS on AWS Fargate by using a custom container image that runs the AgentCore SDK application."}, {"number": 60, "status": "Skipped", "question": "A news media company wants to develop a content conformance tool that automatically reviews and adjusts articles to ensure compliance with a style guide. Journalists need a web-based article editor that provides real-time analysis of content upon request. When journalists click an \"analyze\" button, the system should immediately begin providing suggested revisions through the editor interface. Articles are tagged with content categories in the metadata. Examples of categories include news, sports, and editorial. The company wants to use an Amazon Bedrock FM to analyze content and provide immediate feedback through the web-based article editor interface. Which architecture will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Configure an Application Load Balancer with Amazon ECS tasks that run custom containers. Implement content category routing logic and style guide checking within the containers. Use Amazon Bedrock with streaming support to generate suggestions. Use WebSocket connections to stream results to the journalists in real time.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Deploy an Amazon API Gateway WebSocket API linked to an AWS Lambda function. Configure the function to read the content category from metadata and route content to the appropriate Amazon Bedrock model based on the category tag. Configure the function to use Amazon Bedrock Prompt Management to enforce style guide rules. Use the Amazon Bedrock streaming API to return suggestions in real time.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Implement an Amazon SQS queue for article ingestion. Create AWS Step Functions workflows to process content. Use AWS Lambda functions to determine the content category from metadata and invoke appropriate Amazon Bedrock models with style guide prompts. Store results in Amazon DynamoDB. Use an Amazon API Gateway WebSocket API for real-time streaming of suggestions to the journalists.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Create an Amazon API Gateway REST API with AWS Lambda function URLs to enable response streaming. Configure the Lambda function to process articles and stream suggestions using chunked transfer encoding.", "is_correct": true}], "correct_answers": ["D"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nWeb-based article editor, click nút\n\"analyze\"\n→ phân tích\ntheo yêu cầu (on request)\n, không phải liên tục\nTrả về\ngợi ý chỉnh sửa ngay lập tức (immediate suggested revisions)\nqua editor\nNội dung gắn\ncategory trong metadata\nYêu cầu:\nLEAST operational overhead\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nCreate an Amazon API Gateway REST API with AWS Lambda function URLs to enable response streaming. Configure the Lambda function to process articles and stream suggestions using chunked transfer encoding.\nVì phân tích được kích hoạt\ntheo yêu cầu (on click \"analyze\")\n— đây là mô hình\nrequest/response đơn giản\n, không cần kết nối 2 chiều liên tục (không cần WebSocket).\nLambda function URLs với response streaming\nlà giải pháp\nđơn giản, ít thành phần nhất\n, không cần quản lý WebSocket connections.\nChunked transfer encoding cho phép trả kết quả\nreal-time\nngay khi Bedrock sinh ra, đáp ứng yêu cầu \"immediate feedback\".\nKiến trúc gọn nhẹ nhất trong các lựa chọn, phù hợp \"LEAST operational overhead\".\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Implement an Amazon SQS queue for article ingestion. Create AWS Step Functions workflows to process content. Use AWS Lambda functions to determine the content category from metadata and invoke appropriate Amazon Bedrock models with style guide prompts. Store results in Amazon DynamoDB. Use an Amazon API Gateway WebSocket API for real-time streaming of suggestions to the journalists.\nKiến trúc\nquá phức tạp\nvới nhiều thành phần (queue, orchestration, database) cho một tác vụ chỉ cần request/response đơn giản.\n❌ Deploy an Amazon API Gateway WebSocket API linked to an AWS Lambda function. Configure the function to read the content category from metadata and route content to the appropriate Amazon Bedrock model based on the category tag. Configure the function to use Amazon Bedrock Prompt Management to enforce style guide rules. Use the Amazon Bedrock streaming API to return suggestions in real time.\nWebSocket đòi hỏi quản lý kết nối liên tục (connection management)\n, không cần thiết vì tương tác chỉ là \"click theo yêu cầu\", không phải real-time hai chiều liên tục.\n❌ Configure an Application Load Balancer with Amazon ECS tasks that run custom containers. Implement content category routing logic and style guide checking within the containers. Use Amazon Bedrock with streaming support to generate suggestions. Use WebSocket connections to stream results to the journalists in real time.\nYêu cầu tự quản lý\ncontainers, ALB, custom routing\n→ overhead vận hành rất cao so với giải pháp serverless Lambda.\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\n\"On request/on click\" (một lần request-response) →\nLambda function URL + streaming (chunked transfer encoding)\n, KHÔNG cần WebSocket\nCần kết nối 2 chiều liên tục, cập nhật liên tục không theo yêu cầu → mới cần\nAPI Gateway WebSocket\nNhiều thành phần (SQS, Step Functions, ECS) cho tác vụ đơn giản → dấu hiệu overhead cao, thường sai khi hỏi \"LEAST overhead\""}, {"number": 61, "status": "Skipped", "question": "An ecommerce company has an application that uses Amazon Bedrock to generate product descriptions and recommendations. Currently, the application resides in a single AWS Region. When invoking a model in Amazon Bedrock during peak periods, the application receives an error. The error message says, \"Too many requests, please wait before trying again.\" The company must increase the throughput for invocations during peak periods without introducing additional operational overhead. The company must maintain compatibility with the existing Amazon Bedrock API. The company must use the same FM. Which solution will meet these requirements in the MOST costeffective way?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Create an AWS Lambda function to invoke the model in Amazon Bedrock with the original Region as the default. Configure the Lambda function to fall back to Amazon Bedrock in a secondary Region.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Use cross-Region inference to distribute traffic across multiple Regions within a geographic area.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Use prompt routing to distribute traffic across multiple FMs from the same family.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Use provisioned throughput to provision a higher level of throughput for the FM.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["B"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nApp Bedrock ở\nmột Region duy nhất (single Region)\n, bị lỗi\n\"Too many requests\"\nlúc peak\nCần tăng throughput,\nkhông tăng operational overhead\n, giữ\ncompatibility với Bedrock API hiện tại\n,\ngiữ nguyên FM (same FM)\nYêu cầu:\nMOST cost-effective\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nUse cross-Region inference to distribute traffic across multiple Regions within a geographic area.\nCross-Region inference\nlà tính năng\nnative của Bedrock\n, tự động phân phối traffic sang các Region khác trong cùng khu vực địa lý mà\nkhông cần thay đổi code hay thêm hạ tầng\n.\nKhông phát sinh chi phí cấu hình thêm (no extra provisioning cost)\n, dùng chung API hiện tại → tương thích 100%.\nGiữ nguyên FM đang dùng, chỉ tăng khả năng chịu tải (throughput) qua nhiều Region.\nĐây là giải pháp\ncost-effective nhất\ntrong các lựa chọn vì tận dụng capacity có sẵn.\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Create an AWS Lambda function to invoke the model in Amazon Bedrock with the original Region as the default. Configure the Lambda function to fall back to Amazon Bedrock in a secondary Region.\nYêu cầu\ntự viết và duy trì logic fallback (custom code)\n→ tăng operational overhead, không tận dụng tính năng native.\n❌ Use prompt routing to distribute traffic across multiple FMs from the same family.\nĐề yêu cầu rõ\n\"must use the same FM\"\n→ prompt routing (chuyển đổi giữa các FM khác nhau)\nvi phạm trực tiếp yêu cầu này\n.\n❌ Use provisioned throughput to provision a higher level of throughput for the FM.\nProvisioned Throughput yêu cầu\ncam kết trả phí theo giờ/tháng (hourly/monthly commitment)\n, chi phí cao hơn đáng kể → không phải \"MOST cost-effective\".\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nThrottling \"Too many requests\" + không đổi FM + cost-effective →\nCross-Region inference\nCần giữ nguyên FM (same FM) → loại ngay đáp án có \"prompt routing giữa nhiều FM\"\nTăng throughput cố định, chấp nhận trả phí cam kết →\nProvisioned Throughput\n(thường KHÔNG phải cost-effective nhất)"}, {"number": 62, "status": "Skipped", "question": "A company is developing an AI assistant that processes customer data by using Amazon Bedrock. The AI assistant has multiple guardrails. The guardrails include prompt injection detection, sensitive information filtering, and denied topic blocking. When a customer query is blocked, a GenAI developer needs a detailed analysis of which specific guardrail rule was invoked and why the content was flagged. Then, the GenAI developer must fine-tune guardrail configurations and distinguish between legitimate customer queries and actual security threats. Which configuration provides the MOST detailed analysis of guardrail decision-making for content filtering?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Enable Amazon Bedrock model evaluation with automated evaluation jobs that include guardrail assessment metrics. Configure the evaluation framework to test prompt injection resistance by using company-specific test cases. Use the evaluation dashboard to analyze which guardrail policies are most effective at blocking malicious content while preserving legitimate queries.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Enable Amazon Bedrock model invocation logging to capture full request and response data. Configure Amazon CloudWatch alarms on InvocationsIntervened metrics filtered by Guardrail ContentSource dimensions. Analyze patterns by using CloudWatch Insights queries to identify which content source triggered interventions.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Configure guardrail tracing with {\"trace\": \"enabled\"} in guardrailConfig. Monitor InvocationsIntervened metrics filtered by the Guardrail Content Source dimension to identify whether input prompts or output responses triggered interventions.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Configure guardrail tracing with {\"trace\": \"enabled\"} in guardrailConfig. Monitor InvocationsIntervened metrics filtered by the Guardrail PolicyType dimensions: ContentPolicy, TopicPolicy, and SensitiveInformationPolicy.", "is_correct": true}], "correct_answers": ["D"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nBedrock guardrails gồm:\nprompt injection detection\n,\nsensitive information filtering\n,\ndenied topic blocking\nKhi bị block, cần biết\nguardrail rule cụ thể nào bị kích hoạt (which specific guardrail rule)\nvà lý do\nYêu cầu: phân tích\nCHI TIẾT NHẤT (MOST detailed)\nvề quyết định guardrail\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nConfigure guardrail tracing with\n{\"trace\": \"enabled\"}\nin guardrailConfig. Monitor InvocationsIntervened metrics filtered by the Guardrail PolicyType dimensions: ContentPolicy, TopicPolicy, and SensitiveInformationPolicy.\nGuardrail tracing (\ntrace: enabled\n)\ncung cấp\nlý do chi tiết (detailed reasoning)\ncho từng đánh giá guardrail.\nPolicyType dimension\n(ContentPolicy, TopicPolicy, SensitiveInformationPolicy) khớp\nchính xác\nvới 3 loại guardrail được đề cập trong đề (prompt injection = ContentPolicy, denied topic = TopicPolicy, sensitive info = SensitiveInformationPolicy).\nĐây là mức chi tiết\ncụ thể nhất theo loại rule\n, giúp phân biệt chính xác rule nào bị kích hoạt.\nĐáp ứng đúng yêu cầu \"distinguish which specific guardrail rule was invoked\".\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Enable Amazon Bedrock model evaluation with automated evaluation jobs that include guardrail assessment metrics. Configure the evaluation framework to test prompt injection resistance by using company-specific test cases. Use the evaluation dashboard to analyze which guardrail policies are most effective at blocking malicious content while preserving legitimate queries.\nDùng để\nđánh giá tổng thể hiệu quả (effectiveness)\ncủa guardrail, không cung cấp phân tích\nchi tiết theo từng request cụ thể\n.\n❌ Enable Amazon Bedrock model invocation logging to capture full request and response data. Configure Amazon CloudWatch alarms on InvocationsIntervened metrics filtered by Guardrail ContentSource dimensions. Analyze patterns by using CloudWatch Insights queries to identify which content source triggered interventions.\nContentSource\nchỉ phân biệt\ninput hay output\nbị chặn, không cho biết\nloại rule cụ thể (policy type)\nnào bị kích hoạt.\n❌ Configure guardrail tracing with\n{\"trace\": \"enabled\"}\nin guardrailConfig. Monitor InvocationsIntervened metrics filtered by the Guardrail Content Source dimension to identify whether input prompts or output responses triggered interventions.\nCó bật tracing (đúng một phần) nhưng chỉ filter theo\nContentSource\n(input/output) —\nkém chi tiết hơn\nso với filter theo\nPolicyType\n(loại rule cụ thể).\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nCần biết \"rule cụ thể nào\" bị kích hoạt →\nGuardrail tracing (\ntrace: enabled\n) + filter theo PolicyType dimension\nContentSource dimension → chỉ biết input/output, KHÔNG biết loại rule cụ thể\nPolicyType dimension (ContentPolicy/TopicPolicy/SensitiveInformationPolicy) → mức chi tiết cao nhất, khớp với từng loại guardrail\n\"MOST detailed analysis\" → luôn ưu tiên tracing + dimension chi tiết nhất có thể"}, {"number": 63, "status": "Skipped", "question": "A GenAI developer is building a virtual assistant application by using an Anthropic Claude model on Amazon Bedrock. The application sends user queries and expects conversational responses. The GenAI developer wants to configure the application to stop generating output after a specific phrase is generated in the response. Which solution will meet these requirements?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Add the trigger phrase \"stop at this phrase\" in the user prompt.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Use the stop sequences parameter in the inference call to specify a trigger phrase.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Use the top-k parameter to control the diversity of tokens in the model's output.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Use the temperature parameter in the inference call to control the likelihood of the phrase appearing.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["B"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nVirtual assistant dùng\nAnthropic Claude trên Bedrock\nCần\ndừng sinh output (stop generating)\nsau khi xuất hiện\nphrase cụ thể (specific phrase)\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nUse the stop sequences parameter in the inference call to specify a trigger phrase.\nStop sequences\nlà tham số\nnative của inference API\n, được thiết kế chính xác để dừng generation khi model sinh ra chuỗi ký tự chỉ định.\nĐây là cơ chế\ndeterministic\n, đảm bảo dừng đúng lúc, không phụ thuộc vào cách model \"hiểu\" yêu cầu.\nKhông cần thay đổi prompt hay xử lý hậu kỳ (post-processing).\nĐây là tham số tiêu chuẩn có sẵn trong mọi model Bedrock hỗ trợ.\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Add the trigger phrase \"stop at this phrase\" in the user prompt.\nĐây chỉ là\nhướng dẫn bằng ngôn ngữ tự nhiên (natural language instruction)\n, không đảm bảo (non-deterministic) model sẽ tuân theo chính xác.\n❌ Use the top-k parameter to control the diversity of tokens in the model's output.\nTop-k\nkiểm soát\nđộ đa dạng token (token diversity)\ntrong sampling, không liên quan đến việc dừng generation tại vị trí cụ thể.\n❌ Use the temperature parameter in the inference call to control the likelihood of the phrase appearing.\nTemperature\nkiểm soát\nđộ ngẫu nhiên/sáng tạo (randomness)\ncủa output, không phải cơ chế để dừng sinh văn bản tại một điểm cụ thể.\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nDừng generation tại phrase/chuỗi cụ thể →\nstop sequences parameter\nKiểm soát độ đa dạng từ vựng →\ntop-k / top-p\nKiểm soát độ ngẫu nhiên/sáng tạo →\ntemperature\nYêu cầu qua natural language trong prompt (không đảm bảo) → luôn là bẫy khi có tham số kỹ thuật chuyên dụng thay thế"}, {"number": 64, "status": "Skipped", "question": "A company needs secure authentication for a third-party application that uses Amazon Bedrock. The solution must integrate with the company's existing identity provider (IdP). The solution must maintain comprehensive audit logs of authentication and API calls. The solution must eliminate long-lived credentials and provide temporary access to Amazon Bedrock. Which solutions will meet these requirements? (Select TWO.)", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Create an IAM role and configure federation by using AWS STS AssumeRole API calls. Store the application's IAM user credentials in the application configuration.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Deploy AWS IAM Identity Center with SAML federation to the IdP. Configure custom permission sets that grant access to Amazon Bedrock.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Create IAM users for each employee that needs access to the application. Assign permissions through IAM policies. Implement credential rotation by using AWS Secrets Manager.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Configure an Amazon API Gateway Lambda authorizer. Configure the authorizer to validate credentials against the company's LDAP server and then issue signed JSON Web Tokens (JWTs) for Amazon Bedrock access.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "E", "text": "Implement an OpenID Connect (OIDC) integration with Amazon Cognito. Configure the integration to authenticate users through the IdP and exchange tokens for temporary AWS credentials. Configure the integration to allow the application to access Amazon Bedrock.", "is_correct": true}], "correct_answers": ["B", "E"], "explanation": "A.\nCreate an IAM role and configure federation by using AWS STS AssumeRole API calls. Store the application's IAM user credentials in the application configuration."}, {"number": 65, "status": "Skipped", "question": "A global healthcare company is deploying a GenAI application on Amazon Bedrock to produce treatment recommendations. Regulations vary for each country where the company operates. Some countries require the company to retain all model inputs and outputs for 2 years. Other countries require the company to submit data for local audits only. Medical providers require consistent medical terminology across all locations. However, the treatment recommendations that the model produces must adapt to local patient demographics. The solution must also integrate with existing electronic health record (EHR) systems. The application must support up to 10,000 healthcare provider queries every day with sub-second response times. The company must be able to review the application before deployments and approve prompt changes. The application must produce comprehensive logs for prompts, responses, and user context. Which solution will meet these requirements?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Store prompt templates in Amazon S3. Use S3 Object Lock to implement version control. Use Amazon EventBridge to track model invocations. Use AWS Config to monitor changes to prompt templates.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Use AWS CloudTrail to log API calls. Create standard prompts in Amazon Bedrock Prompt Management that include variables for patient demographics. Implement IAM policies to ensure that only approves users can access prompts.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Create AWS Lambda functions to dynamically generate prompts that enforce clinical language requirements. Use Amazon CloudWatch Logs to track model invocations. Use Amazon SQS queues to implement a prompt approval workflow.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Use Amazon CloudWatch Logs to collect detailed model invocation logs. Store the logs in Amazon S3. Create parameterized prompts in Amazon Bedrock Prompt Management that include variables for treatment options. Enable prompt versioning and set up an approval workflow.", "is_correct": true}], "correct_answers": ["D"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nQuy định khác nhau theo quốc gia:\nretain 2 năm\n, hoặc\nsubmit data audit\nCần\nthuật ngữ y khoa nhất quán (consistent medical terminology)\n, tích hợp\nEHR\n10,000 queries/ngày, sub-second response\nCần\nreview trước deploy + approve prompt changes\n+\nlogs đầy đủ (prompts, responses, user context)\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nUse Amazon CloudWatch Logs to collect detailed model invocation logs. Store the logs in Amazon S3. Create parameterized prompts in Amazon Bedrock Prompt Management that include variables for treatment options. Enable prompt versioning and set up an approval workflow.\nCloudWatch Logs → S3\nghi lại đầy đủ\nprompts, responses, user context\n— đáp ứng yêu cầu logging toàn diện.\nParameterized prompts với variables\nđảm bảo\nthuật ngữ y khoa nhất quán\nacross mọi lần gọi.\nPrompt versioning + approval workflow\ntrong Bedrock Prompt Management đáp ứng trực tiếp yêu cầu \"review before deployment, approve prompt changes\".\nToàn bộ dùng tính năng\nnative của Bedrock\n, không cần xây pipeline riêng, phù hợp scale 10K/ngày.\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Create AWS Lambda functions to dynamically generate prompts that enforce clinical language requirements. Use Amazon CloudWatch Logs to track model invocations. Use Amazon SQS queues to implement a prompt approval workflow.\nYêu cầu\ntự viết logic enforce ngôn ngữ (custom code)\nvà xây\nworkflow phê duyệt qua SQS thủ công\n→ tăng overhead, không tận dụng tính năng native.\n❌ Use AWS CloudTrail to log API calls. Create standard prompts in Amazon Bedrock Prompt Management that include variables for patient demographics. Implement IAM policies to ensure that only approves users can access prompts.\nCloudTrail chỉ log API calls (metadata)\n, không capture đầy đủ\nnội dung prompts/responses\nnhư yêu cầu.\n\"Standard prompts\" không đảm bảo tính nhất quán thuật ngữ như parameterized prompts.\n❌ Store prompt templates in Amazon S3. Use S3 Object Lock to implement version control. Use Amazon EventBridge to track model invocations. Use AWS Config to monitor changes to prompt templates.\nKhông dùng tính năng\nnative prompt versioning/approval\ncủa Bedrock Prompt Management, tự xây dựng version control bằng S3 → phức tạp hơn không cần thiết.\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nCần log đầy đủ prompts + responses + user context →\nCloudWatch Logs (model invocation logging) → S3\n, KHÔNG phải CloudTrail\nCần thuật ngữ nhất quán across nhiều lần gọi →\nParameterized prompts (variables) trong Prompt Management\nReview/approve trước khi deploy prompt →\nPrompt versioning + approval workflow\n(native Bedrock)"}, {"number": 66, "status": "Skipped", "question": "A GenAI developer is evaluating Amazon Bedrock foundation models (FMs) for a Europe-based company’s internal business application. The company has a multiaccount landing zone in AWS Control Tower and uses SCPs to allow accounts to use only eu-north-1 and eu-west-1. All customer data must remain in private networks within the approved Regions. The developer selects an FM hosted in eu-central-1 and euwest-3. The developer must enable access to the FM for employees and ensure requests are private and remain in the same Regions as the FM. Which solution meets these requirements?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Deploy the FM in SageMaker in eu-north-1. Configure SageMaker VPC endpoint. Extend SCPs. Integrate SageMaker with the app.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Deploy Lambda behind private API Gateway in eu-north-1. Create a VPC endpoint for the selected FM in eu-central-1 and eu-west-3. Extend SCPs. Integrate REST API with the app.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Use cross-Region inference through a Europe-scoped endpoint. Configure a Bedrock VPC endpoint. Extend SCPs to allow employees to use the FM through inference profiles in Europe Regions where the FM is available. Use an inference profile to integrate Bedrock with the app.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Deploy the FM on EC2 in eu-north-1. Put a private API Gateway in front. Configure a Bedrock VPC endpoint. Integrate the REST API with the app.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["C"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nMulti-account landing zone (Control Tower),\nSCP chỉ cho phép eu-north-1 và eu-west-1\nDữ liệu khách hàng phải ở\nprivate networks trong Regions được duyệt\nFM được host tại\neu-central-1 và eu-west-3\n(ngoài phạm vi SCP ban đầu!)\nCần: request\nprivate\n, ở lại\ncùng Region với FM\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nUse cross-Region inference through a Europe-scoped endpoint. Configure a Bedrock VPC endpoint. Extend SCPs to allow employees to use the FM through inference profiles in Europe Regions where the FM is available. Use an inference profile to integrate Bedrock with the app.\nCross-Region inference profile (Europe-scoped)\nlà tính năng native của Bedrock giúp truy cập FM tại các Region khác trong cùng khu vực địa lý, đúng khi FM hosted tại eu-central-1/eu-west-3 nhưng SCP ban đầu chỉ cho eu-north-1/eu-west-1.\nBedrock VPC endpoint\nđảm bảo request luôn\nprivate\n, không đi qua internet công cộng.\nExtend SCPs\nđể bổ sung quyền dùng inference profile là bước bắt buộc vì SCP ban đầu quá hẹp so với vị trí thực của FM.\nĐảm bảo dữ liệu chỉ di chuyển trong phạm vi\nđịa lý châu Âu (Europe geography)\n, đáp ứng yêu cầu data residency.\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Deploy the FM on EC2 in eu-north-1. Put a private API Gateway in front. Configure a Bedrock VPC endpoint. Integrate the REST API with the app.\nDeploy FM trên EC2\nkhông đúng vì đề nói \"developer selects an FM\" (dùng FM có sẵn trên Bedrock), không phải tự host model.\n❌ Deploy Lambda behind private API Gateway in eu-north-1. Create a VPC endpoint for the selected FM in eu-central-1 and eu-west-3. Extend SCPs. Integrate REST API with the app.\nCách tiếp cận\nthủ công/per-region\nnày thiếu cơ chế chuẩn (inference profile) để quản lý truy cập xuyên Region một cách nhất quán, phức tạp hơn cross-Region inference.\n❌ Deploy the FM in SageMaker in eu-north-1. Configure SageMaker VPC endpoint. Extend SCPs. Integrate SageMaker with the app.\nSai dịch vụ — đề yêu cầu dùng\nBedrock FM có sẵn\n, không phải tự deploy trên SageMaker.\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nFM hosted ở Region ngoài phạm vi SCP hiện tại, cần truy cập trong cùng khu vực địa lý →\nCross-Region inference profile\nRequest phải \"private\" → luôn kèm\nBedrock VPC endpoint\nSCP quá hẹp so với vị trí FM thực tế → cần\nextend SCPs\nđể cho phép inference profile"}, {"number": 67, "status": "Skipped", "question": "A retail company uses Amazon Bedrock to generate product recommendations by dynamically constructing prompts and sending them to FMs. A developer updated the app to instruct the FM to include a specific promotional message in responses. During testing, the promotional message does not always appear, and when it appears it is sometimes not coherent with the rest of the response. The developer must ensure the promotional message always appears in the FM responses. Which solution meets this requirement?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Reinforce the requirement to include the promotional message within product recommendations by using an output indicator in prompts to the FM.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Use an Amazon Bedrock Guardrails filter on the prompt. Set the input filter strength to HIGH.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Generate multiple response variants that include the promotional message in different ways. Use a reranker to select the most coherent version.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Run the prompt through Amazon Bedrock. Process the response through Amazon Bedrock AgentCore to add the promotional message. Rerank the results using the original prompt and desired message as context.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["C"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nPromotional message đôi khi\nkhông xuất hiện\n, đôi khi\nkhông coherent (thiếu mạch lạc)\nYêu cầu: đảm bảo message\nluôn xuất hiện (always appears)\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nGenerate multiple response variants that include the promotional message in different ways. Use a reranker to select the most coherent version.\nBằng cách\nbắt buộc mọi variant đều chứa promotional message\nngay từ bước generation, đảm bảo message\nluôn xuất hiện (guaranteed inclusion)\n.\nReranker\nchọn ra bản có\nđộ mạch lạc cao nhất (most coherent)\ntrong số các variants, giải quyết vấn đề \"không coherent\".\nGiải quyết đồng thời\ncả hai vấn đề\nnêu trong đề: presence + coherence.\nĐây là pattern chuẩn \"constrained generation + rerank\" cho use case cần nội dung bắt buộc nhưng vẫn tự nhiên.\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Use an Amazon Bedrock Guardrails filter on the prompt. Set the input filter strength to HIGH.\nGuardrails dùng để\nchặn nội dung (block content)\n, không có chức năng\nđảm bảo một nội dung cụ thể xuất hiện\ntrong response.\n❌ Run the prompt through Amazon Bedrock. Process the response through Amazon Bedrock AgentCore to add the promotional message. Rerank the results using the original prompt and desired message as context.\nThêm message\nhậu kỳ (post-hoc insertion)\ndễ dẫn đến\nthiếu tự nhiên/không mạch lạc\nvì không tích hợp trong quá trình sinh văn bản gốc.\n❌ Reinforce the requirement to include the promotional message within product recommendations by using an output indicator in prompts to the FM.\nChỉ là\ntăng cường prompt engineering\n, vẫn là\nnon-deterministic\n, không đảm bảo 100% message luôn xuất hiện.\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nCần đảm bảo nội dung LUÔN xuất hiện + mạch lạc →\ngenerate multiple variants (bắt buộc chứa nội dung) + rerank chọn bản coherent nhất\nChỉ tăng cường prompt (reinforce, indicator) → không đảm bảo 100%, thường là bẫy\nGuardrails → dùng để BLOCK, không dùng để ENFORCE presence của nội dung"}, {"number": 68, "status": "Skipped", "question": "A healthcare company wants to develop a proof-of-concept application that uses Amazon Bedrock to automatically summarize medical documents. The company has 3 weeks to validate the application's accuracy. The application must comply with the company's data privacy policies. The application must include metrics to evaluate summarization accuracy and processing time. Which solution will meet these requirements?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Create a dataset that includes 50–100 anonymized patient records. Implement Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) with a secure knowledge base. Use a judge model to evaluate accuracy metrics across three foundation models (FMs).", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Use the Strands SDK to deploy multiple agents that connect to multiple knowledge bases that contain specialized medical documents. Compare the responses of the agents. Evaluate the integration of the agents with the company's existing systems.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Fine-tune a single foundation model (FM) on patient records. Deploy the FM on Amazon Bedrock. Use Amazon Bedrock AgentCore to configure the FM as an agent. Conduct user testing on 500 company staff members.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Select the most powerful available AWS foundation model (FM). Create a chat interface by using Converse APIs. Test the application on 50–100 actual patient records by using only qualitative feedback from stakeholders. Use a custom web interface to gather real-world performance metrics.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["A"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nPoC tóm tắt tài liệu y tế,\n3 tuần\nđể validate accuracy\nPhải tuân thủ\ndata privacy policies\nCần\nmetrics đánh giá accuracy và processing time\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nCreate a dataset that includes 50–100 anonymized patient records. Implement Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) with a secure knowledge base. Use a judge model to evaluate accuracy metrics across three foundation models (FMs).\nDữ liệu được ẩn danh (anonymized)\nđáp ứng trực tiếp yêu cầu \"comply with data privacy policies\".\nRAG\nkhông cần training/fine-tuning → triển khai nhanh, phù hợp timeline\n3 tuần\n.\nJudge model\ncung cấp\nmetrics định lượng cho accuracy\nmột cách tự động, đáp ứng yêu cầu đo lường.\nSo sánh 3 FM giúp chọn model tốt nhất cho PoC, đúng quy mô nhỏ (50-100 records) phù hợp giai đoạn PoC.\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Fine-tune a single foundation model (FM) on patient records. Deploy the FM on Amazon Bedrock. Use Amazon Bedrock AgentCore to configure the FM as an agent. Conduct user testing on 500 company staff members.\nFine-tuning tốn thời gian\n, thường vượt quá 3 tuần cho một PoC.\nDùng\npatient records thô (chưa anonymized)\nđể train → vi phạm data privacy.\n❌ Select the most powerful available AWS foundation model (FM). Create a chat interface by using Converse APIs. Test the application on 50–100 actual patient records by using only qualitative feedback from stakeholders. Use a custom web interface to gather real-world performance metrics.\nDùng\ndữ liệu bệnh nhân thật (không anonymized)\n→ vi phạm privacy compliance.\nChỉ có\nfeedback định tính (qualitative)\n, không đáp ứng yêu cầu \"metrics\" định lượng cho accuracy và processing time.\n❌ Use the Strands SDK to deploy multiple agents that connect to multiple knowledge bases that contain specialized medical documents. Compare the responses of the agents. Evaluate the integration of the agents with the company's existing systems.\nKiến trúc\nquá phức tạp\nso với nhu cầu PoC đơn giản, không cần tích hợp hệ thống hiện có cho giai đoạn thử nghiệm.\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nPoC nhanh (vài tuần), cần accuracy metrics →\nRAG + judge model\n(KHÔNG fine-tune, vì tốn thời gian)\nData privacy compliance → luôn cần\nanonymized data\n\"Metrics\" định lượng (không phải qualitative feedback) → judge model / automated evaluation"}, {"number": 69, "status": "Skipped", "question": "A company wants to select a new FM for its AI assistant. A GenAI developer needs to generate evaluation reports to help a data scientist assess the quality and safety of various foundation models (FMs). The data scientist provides sample prompts for evaluation. The GenAI developer wants to use Amazon Bedrock to automate report generation and evaluation. Which solution will meet this requirement?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Combine sample prompts into one JSONL document. Store it in Amazon S3. Create a Bedrock evaluation job that uses a judge model. Specify S3 as input and Amazon QuickSight as output. Run an evaluation job for each FM and select the FM as the evaluator.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Combine sample prompts into one JSON document. Store it in Amazon S3. Create an Amazon Bedrock evaluation job that uses a judge model. Specify the S3 location as input and a different S3 location as output. Run an evaluation job for each FM and select the FM as the evaluator.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Combine sample prompts into one JSON document. Create a Bedrock knowledge base. Create a Bedrock evaluation job that uses the retrieval and response generation evaluation type. Specify an S3 bucket as output. Run an evaluation job for each FM.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Combine sample prompts into one JSON document. Create a Bedrock knowledge base with the document. Write a prompt that asks the FM to respond to each sample prompt. Use RetrieveAndGenerate API to generate a report for each model.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["B"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nData scientist cung cấp\nsample prompts\nđể đánh giá FM\nCần\ntự động hóa report generation và evaluation\nbằng Bedrock\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nCombine sample prompts into one JSON document. Store it in Amazon S3. Create an Amazon Bedrock evaluation job that uses a judge model. Specify the S3 location as input and a different S3 location as output. Run an evaluation job for each FM and select the FM as the evaluator.\nBedrock evaluation job với judge model\nlà tính năng\nnative, tự động hóa\nđể đánh giá chất lượng nhiều FM cùng lúc.\nS3 làm input và output\nlà cấu hình\nchuẩn, duy nhất được hỗ trợ\ncho evaluation job (không hỗ trợ QuickSight hay Knowledge Base làm output/input trực tiếp).\nChạy job riêng cho mỗi FM cho phép\nso sánh khách quan\ngiữa các model.\nĐây là pattern automation evaluation đúng chuẩn Bedrock, tránh phải tự viết logic đánh giá.\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Combine sample prompts into one JSON document. Create a Bedrock knowledge base with the document. Write a prompt that asks the FM to respond to each sample prompt. Use RetrieveAndGenerate API to generate a report for each model.\nĐây là cách dùng\nsai tính năng\n— RetrieveAndGenerate dành cho RAG, không phải cơ chế\nautomated model evaluation\n.\n❌ Combine sample prompts into one JSONL document. Store it in Amazon S3. Create a Bedrock evaluation job that uses a judge model. Specify S3 as input and Amazon QuickSight as output. Run an evaluation job for each FM and select the FM as the evaluator.\nQuickSight không phải là destination hợp lệ\ncho Bedrock evaluation job — output evaluation job chỉ có thể là\nAmazon S3\n.\n❌ Combine sample prompts into one JSON document. Create a Bedrock knowledge base. Create a Bedrock evaluation job that uses the retrieval and response generation evaluation type. Specify an S3 bucket as output. Run an evaluation job for each FM.\nLoại evaluation này dành riêng cho\nđánh giá hệ thống RAG\n(retrieval + generation), không phù hợp để đánh giá chất lượng FM tổng quát qua sample prompts đơn thuần.\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nTự động đánh giá chất lượng nhiều FM bằng sample prompts →\nBedrock evaluation job + judge model\nInput/Output của evaluation job → LUÔN LÀ\nAmazon S3\n, không phải QuickSight hay Knowledge Base\n⚠️\nLưu ý quan trọng:\ndataset chuẩn cho Bedrock evaluation job thực tế phải ở định dạng\nJSONL\n(mỗi dòng 1 JSON object) — đây là điểm hay bị hỏi riêng trong đề thi thật, cần nhớ kỹ nếu gặp câu tương tự nhấn mạnh vào format file."}, {"number": 70, "status": "Skipped", "question": "A company developed a multimodal content analysis application by using Amazon Bedrock. The application routes different content types (text, images, and code) to specialized foundation models (FMs). The application needs to handle multiple types of routing decisions. Simple routing based on file extension must have minimal latency. Complex routing based on content semantics requires analysis before FM selection. The application must provide detailed history and support fallback options when primary FMs fail. Which solution will meet these requirements?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Deploy separate AWS Step Functions workflows for each content type with routing logic in AWS Lambda functions. Use Amazon EventBridge to coordinate between workflows when fallback to alternate FMs is required.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Use Amazon SQS with different SQS queues for each content type. Configure AWS Lambda consumers that analyze content and invoke appropriate FMs based on message attributes by using Amazon Bedrock with an AWS SDK.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Create a hybrid solution. Handle simple routing based on file extensions in application code. Handle complex content-based routing by using an AWS Step Functions state machine with JSONata for content analysis and the InvokeModel API for specialized FMs.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Configure AWS Lambda functions that call Amazon Bedrock FMs for all routing logic. Use conditional statements to determine the appropriate FM based on content type and semantics.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["C"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nRouting content (text/image/code) đến nhiều FM chuyên biệt\nSimple routing theo file extension\ncần\nlatency tối thiểu\nComplex routing theo semantics\ncần\nphân tích trước khi chọn FM\nCần\nlịch sử chi tiết (detailed history)\n+\nfallback options\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nCreate a hybrid solution. Handle simple routing based on file extensions in application code. Handle complex content-based routing by using an AWS Step Functions state machine with JSONata for content analysis and the InvokeModel API for specialized FMs.\nRouting đơn giản xử lý trực tiếp trong application code\n→ độ trễ\ntối thiểu\n, không qua thêm dịch vụ trung gian.\nStep Functions state machine với JSONata\nxử lý routing phức tạp cần phân tích ngữ nghĩa, tách biệt rõ với luồng đơn giản.\nStep Functions\ntự động cung cấp execution history chi tiết\n(native), đáp ứng yêu cầu \"detailed history\".\nStep Functions hỗ trợ\nretry/catch (fallback) native\n, đáp ứng yêu cầu \"support fallback options when primary FMs fail\".\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Configure AWS Lambda functions that call Amazon Bedrock FMs for all routing logic. Use conditional statements to determine the appropriate FM based on content type and semantics.\nRouting đơn giản (theo file extension) vẫn phải qua Lambda + Bedrock call →\nkhông đạt latency tối thiểu\ncho trường hợp đơn giản.\n❌ Deploy separate AWS Step Functions workflows for each content type with routing logic in AWS Lambda functions. Use Amazon EventBridge to coordinate between workflows when fallback to alternate FMs is required.\nThêm\nEventBridge để coordinate fallback\nlà dư thừa vì Step Functions đã có cơ chế\nretry/catch native\n.\n❌ Use Amazon SQS with different SQS queues for each content type. Configure AWS Lambda consumers that analyze content and invoke appropriate FMs based on message attributes by using Amazon Bedrock with an AWS SDK.\nSQS/Lambda\nkhông cung cấp execution history chi tiết\nnhư Step Functions, khó đáp ứng yêu cầu \"detailed history\" và fallback rõ ràng.\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nCần vừa routing đơn giản (latency thấp) vừa routing phức tạp (cần phân tích) →\nHybrid: code đơn giản + Step Functions cho phức tạp\nCần \"detailed history\" + \"fallback\" native →\nAWS Step Functions\n(execution history + retry/catch built-in)\nRouting tất cả qua 1 Lambda/Bedrock call → vi phạm yêu cầu latency tối thiểu cho case đơn giản"}, {"number": 71, "status": "Skipped", "question": "A developer needs to build a foundation model-powered application that can search a product catalog, check inventory levels via an API, and place orders. The application must handle multi-step workflows autonomously. Which Amazon Bedrock feature should the developer use?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Amazon Bedrock Agents with action groups connected to Lambda functions.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Amazon Bedrock batch inference with the product catalog as input.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Amazon Bedrock Guardrails with custom word filters.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Amazon Bedrock Prompt Flows with a single prompt node.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["A"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nApp cần:\ntìm kiếm product catalog\n,\ncheck inventory qua API\n,\nđặt hàng (place orders)\nPhải\ntự động thực hiện multi-step workflows (autonomously)\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nAmazon Bedrock Agents with action groups connected to Lambda functions.\nBedrock Agents\nđược thiết kế chuyên biệt cho các tác vụ\nđa bước, tự động (multi-step, autonomous)\n, tự lập kế hoạch và thực thi.\nAction groups + Lambda\ncho phép agent gọi API bên ngoài (check inventory, place order) một cách linh hoạt.\nAgent tự động\norchestrate\ncác bước mà không cần lập trình luồng cứng (hard-coded flow).\nĐây là pattern chuẩn cho use case \"search → check → act\" (function calling qua nhiều bước).\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Amazon Bedrock Guardrails with custom word filters.\nGuardrails dùng để\nkiểm soát nội dung an toàn (safety)\n, không có khả năng\nthực thi workflow hoặc gọi API\n.\n❌ Amazon Bedrock Prompt Flows with a single prompt node.\nPrompt Flows phù hợp cho\nluồng xử lý cố định, đơn giản (fixed flow)\n, không phù hợp với yêu cầu\ntự động đa bước phức tạp\nnhư agent.\n❌ Amazon Bedrock batch inference with the product catalog as input.\nBatch inference dùng cho\nxử lý hàng loạt offline\n, không hỗ trợ\ntương tác real-time đa bước với API bên ngoài\n.\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nMulti-step workflow tự động, gọi API bên ngoài →\nBedrock Agents + Action Groups (Lambda)\nLuồng xử lý cố định, đơn giản →\nPrompt Flows\nXử lý hàng loạt, không cần tương tác real-time →\nBatch inference"}, {"number": 72, "status": "Skipped", "question": "A developer is using Amazon Bedrock Prompt Management to version and manage prompts across development, staging, and production environments. The team needs to ensure that prompt changes are tested before reaching production and that previous versions can be quickly restored. Which approach should the developer implement?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Store prompts as hardcoded strings in the application code and use Git branching for version control.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Create prompt versions in Bedrock Prompt Management and use prompt aliases to point each environment to the appropriate version.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Use Amazon S3 versioning to store prompt text files and reference them by version ID.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Maintain separate AWS accounts for each environment, each with its own copy of the prompts.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["B"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nVersion & manage prompts qua\ndev/staging/production\nCần\ntest trước khi lên production\n+\nkhôi phục nhanh phiên bản cũ (quickly restored)\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nCreate prompt versions in Bedrock Prompt Management and use prompt aliases to point each environment to the appropriate version.\nPrompt versioning\nlà tính năng\nnative\n, tự động lưu lại từng phiên bản prompt, cho phép\nkhôi phục nhanh (quick restore)\n.\nPrompt aliases\ncho phép trỏ mỗi môi trường (dev/staging/prod) đến version tương ứng mà\nkhông cần thay đổi code ứng dụng\n.\nĐây là pattern chuẩn để quản lý promotion prompt qua các môi trường một cách an toàn.\nKhông cần xây dựng thêm hạ tầng ngoài Bedrock.\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Store prompts as hardcoded strings in the application code and use Git branching for version control.\nYêu cầu\ntự quản lý version control thủ công qua Git\n, không tận dụng tính năng native của Bedrock, dễ sai sót khi deploy.\n❌ Maintain separate AWS accounts for each environment, each with its own copy of the prompts.\nCách này\ncực kỳ tốn kém và phức tạp về vận hành\n, không cần thiết cho việc quản lý version/alias đơn giản.\n❌ Use Amazon S3 versioning to store prompt text files and reference them by version ID.\nKhông tận dụng\ntính năng alias/version native của Prompt Management\n, phải tự quản lý version ID thủ công trong code.\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nQuản lý version + môi trường (dev/staging/prod) cho prompt →\nBedrock Prompt Management: versions + aliases\nCần \"quickly restore\" phiên bản cũ → tính năng\nnative versioning\n, không phải Git/S3 versioning tự quản lý"}, {"number": 73, "status": "Skipped", "question": "A developer is implementing data lineage tracking for their RAG-based application. Regulators require the ability to trace any generated response back to the specific source documents that informed it. Which approach provides this capability?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Store all source documents in a versioned S3 bucket and reference the bucket in responses.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Use AWS Glue Data Catalog to track all data transformations in the RAG pipeline.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Configure the RAG pipeline to return source citations with each response, including document IDs, chunk references, and relevance scores, and store this metadata in a data lineage database alongside the response.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Enable Bedrock model invocation logging and manually review logs to identify source documents.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["C"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nCần\ntrace response về source documents cụ thể (trace back to source documents)\nYêu cầu từ regulators\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nConfigure the RAG pipeline to return source citations with each response, including document IDs, chunk references, and relevance scores, and store this metadata in a data lineage database alongside the response.\nTrả về\ncitation trực tiếp trong mỗi response\n(document IDs, chunk references) tạo ra\nliên kết tường minh (explicit link)\ngiữa response và nguồn tài liệu.\nLưu metadata này vào\nlineage database\nđảm bảo khả năng\naudit/trace lại bất kỳ lúc nào\n, đúng yêu cầu regulator.\nĐây là cách\ntrực tiếp nhất\nđể đáp ứng \"trace any generated response back to specific source documents\".\nRelevance scores còn cung cấp thêm ngữ cảnh về mức độ liên quan của từng nguồn.\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Enable Bedrock model invocation logging and manually review logs to identify source documents.\nReview thủ công (manual)\nkhông scale được, không đảm bảo trace chính xác 100% và không tự động hóa.\n❌ Use AWS Glue Data Catalog to track all data transformations in the RAG pipeline.\nGlue Data Catalog dùng để track\nlineage của pipeline ETL/dữ liệu\n, không phải cơ chế trace\nresponse cụ thể → document cụ thể\ntrong RAG.\n❌ Store all source documents in a versioned S3 bucket and reference the bucket in responses.\nChỉ tham chiếu đến\nbucket chung\n, không chỉ rõ\ndocument/chunk cụ thể nào\nđã thực sự được dùng để tạo ra response đó → không đủ chi tiết truy vết.\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nTrace response → source document cụ thể →\nRAG source citations (doc ID, chunk ref) + lineage database\nYêu cầu regulator về traceability → cần\nmetadata tường minh gắn với từng response\n, không phải log chung chung"}, {"number": 74, "status": "Skipped", "question": "A developer is building a chatbot that needs to maintain conversation context across multiple user interactions within a session. The chatbot uses Amazon Bedrock's InvokeModel API directly. Which approach correctly maintains conversation history?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Amazon Bedrock automatically maintains conversation history for 24 hours across all API calls using the same access key.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "The developer must store conversation history in the application layer and include previous messages in the messages array of each subsequent Converse API call.", "is_correct": true}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Enable session persistence in the Bedrock model configuration to automatically store conversation state.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Use Amazon DynamoDB Streams to automatically capture and replay conversation history.", "is_correct": false}], "correct_answers": ["B"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nChatbot dùng\nInvokeModel API trực tiếp (directly)\nCần duy trì\nconversation context\nqua nhiều lượt tương tác\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nThe developer must store conversation history in the application layer and include previous messages in the messages array of each subsequent Converse API call.\nBedrock InvokeModel/Converse API là stateless\n— không tự động lưu lịch sử hội thoại giữa các lần gọi.\nDeveloper\nphải tự quản lý ở tầng ứng dụng (application layer)\n, lưu trữ history và gửi kèm trong mỗi request tiếp theo.\nĐây là kiến thức nền tảng quan trọng: Bedrock không có \"session memory\" tích hợp sẵn.\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Amazon Bedrock automatically maintains conversation history for 24 hours across all API calls using the same access key.\nSai bản chất\n— Bedrock API là\nstateless\n, không có cơ chế tự lưu lịch sử theo access key.\n❌ Enable session persistence in the Bedrock model configuration to automatically store conversation state.\nKhông tồn tại tính năng \"session persistence\" tự động\ntrong cấu hình model của Bedrock.\n❌ Use Amazon DynamoDB Streams to automatically capture and replay conversation history.\nĐây là giải pháp\nquá phức tạp và sai mục đích\n— DynamoDB Streams dùng để phản ứng với thay đổi dữ liệu, không phải cơ chế chuẩn để quản lý hội thoại.\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nDuy trì conversation history với InvokeModel/Converse API →\nBedrock là stateless, app phải tự lưu history và gửi lại trong messages array\nBất kỳ đáp án nào nói \"Bedrock tự động lưu session/history\" → LUÔN SAI, vì đây là kiến thức nền tảng hay bị đánh lừa"}, {"number": 75, "status": "Skipped", "question": "A developer is implementing content filtering for a customer-facing chatbot using Amazon Bedrock Guardrails. The chatbot must block hate speech, sexual content, and profanity while allowing medical terminology that might otherwise trigger content filters. How should the developer configure the guardrails?", "answers": [{"letter": "A", "text": "Enable all content filters at the HIGH strength level and add no exceptions.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "B", "text": "Disable content filters entirely and implement custom filtering logic in the application code.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "C", "text": "Use only denied topics without content filters since they provide more granular control.", "is_correct": false}, {"letter": "D", "text": "Configure content filters with appropriate strength levels for hate, sexual, and profanity categories, and use word filters to explicitly allow specific medical terms that should not be blocked.", "is_correct": true}], "correct_answers": ["D"], "explanation": "📝\nTóm tắt đề:\nChatbot cần\nchặn hate speech, sexual content, profanity\nĐồng thời\ncho phép thuật ngữ y khoa (medical terminology)\ndù có thể trigger filter\n✅\nĐáp án đúng:\nConfigure content filters with appropriate strength levels for hate, sexual, and profanity categories, and use word filters to explicitly allow specific medical terms that should not be blocked.\nCấu hình\nstrength levels riêng biệt cho từng category\n(hate, sexual, profanity) cho phép kiểm soát linh hoạt, không \"all-or-nothing\".\nWord filters với exception\ncho phép thuật ngữ y khoa\nkhông bị chặn nhầm (false positive)\n.\nĐây là cách\ncân bằng\ngiữa an toàn nội dung và tính chính xác chuyên môn — đúng yêu cầu đề bài.\nTận dụng đầy đủ tính năng granular configuration của Bedrock Guardrails.\nCác đáp án sai:\n❌ Enable all content filters at the HIGH strength level and add no exceptions.\nMức\nHIGH cho tất cả\nsẽ\nchặn nhầm cả thuật ngữ y khoa hợp lệ\n, vi phạm trực tiếp yêu cầu \"allowing medical terminology\".\n❌ Disable content filters entirely and implement custom filtering logic in the application code.\nLoại bỏ hoàn toàn bảo vệ có sẵn\ncủa Guardrails, phải tự xây dựng lại từ đầu → rủi ro cao và tốn nhiều effort không cần thiết.\n❌ Use only denied topics without content filters since they provide more granular control.\nDenied topics\ndùng để chặn\nchủ đề (topics)\ncụ thể, không phải cơ chế thiết kế để chặn\nhate/sexual/profanity\n— sai loại filter cho đúng mục đích.\n🔑\nTips and tricks:\nChặn nội dung độc hại NHƯNG cho phép thuật ngữ chuyên môn (y khoa, pháp lý...) →\ncontent filters với strength phù hợp + word filters exception\n\"HIGH cho tất cả, không exception\" → thường là bẫy khi đề có yêu cầu allow trường hợp đặc biệt\nDenied topics ≠ content filters: denied topics chặn\nchủ đề\n, content filters chặn\nloại nội dung độc hại\n(hate/sexual/violence/profanity)"}]}];